/* ---- The work-curse (DIRECTION §C). $workCursed = indentured; $workStation =
   "cage"/"vats"; $workOwed = a shift is due before the station will let you leave;
   $sneakedOut = took the keep-yourself path at the Arrivals (the fork is then spent).
   Seeded from the cross-life mark just below — a returner who ever took it starts cursed. */
<<set $workCursed to false>>
<<set $workStation to "">>
<<set $workOwed to false>>
<<set $sneakedOut to false>>
<<set $shiftsWorked to 0>>      /* indenture shifts worked this life; at setup.WORK_LEATHER_AT the job gives free leather */
<<set $workCooldown to 0>>      /* post-shift grace: while > 0, encounter-eligible moves roll NO encounter (you just worked) — decremented one per eligible move. Set to setup.WORK_COOLDOWN by doShift/doPressedShift. */
<<set $pressedReturn to "">>    /* one-off forced-shift routing: room to return to after a pressed shift (unclaimed submit) */
<<set $pressedStation to "">>   /* which station ("cage"/"vats") you were marched to */

/* ---- PERSISTENT across lives (memorize/recall — survive Engine.restart) ----
   Specific corruption marks/fates accumulate run-over-run and NEVER wash off
   (pure accumulation). The meter still starts clean each life; the MARKS are
   what carry, and enough of them open new paths. */
<<set $returns to recall("runs", 0)>>   /* how many runs have ended before this one */
<<set $marks to recall("marks", {})>>   /* snapshot of accumulated marks for easy conditionals */

/* CARRYOVER (owner 2026-06-17): an in-game ending (death/bad-end/escape) calls setup.restartCarry,
   which arms a one-shot "carryover" key before restarting — so the marks + map read above carry
   into this life. The MANUAL UIBar Restart reloads WITHOUT arming, so the block below wipes every
   cross-life key for a true fresh start. The flag is consumed either way. */
<<if not recall("carryover", false)>>
<<set $returns to 0>>
<<set $marks to {}>>
<<run forget("marks")>><<run forget("runs")>><<run forget("scars")>><<run forget("discovered")>><<run forget("build")>>
<</if>>
<<run forget("carryover")>>

/* Cross-life seed: a past work-curse mark starts this life PRE-INDENTURED at that post
   (vats outranks cage). WriggleFree routes you to the post. */
<<if $marks["work_vats"]>><<set $workCursed to true>><<set $workStation to "vats">><<set $workOwed to true>><<elseif $marks["work_cage"]>><<set $workCursed to true>><<set $workStation to "cage">><<set $workOwed to true>><</if>>

/* named-demon + moral history flags */
<<set $metTheWhisperer to false>>
<<set $metTallow to false>>
<<set $metUnderstudy to false>>
<<set $tookTheBargain to false>>
<<set $refusedTheWhisperer to false>>
<<set $hasWard to false>>
<<set $gaveUpFace to false>>

/* ---- Audio cache: DISABLED until real .mp3s exist (see audio/README.md).
   The chooser guards on SimpleAudio.tracks.has(), so nothing cached = silent
   + error-free. Un-comment when assets land. ---- */
/*
<<cacheaudio "base"     "audio/ambient_base.mp3">>
<<cacheaudio "whisper"  "audio/whisper_motif.mp3">>
<<cacheaudio "tallow"   "audio/tallow_motif.mp3">>
<<cacheaudio "wearer"   "audio/wearer_motif.mp3">>
<<cacheaudio "corrupt1" "audio/dark_a.mp3">>
<<cacheaudio "corrupt2" "audio/dark_b.mp3">>
*/

/* ---- Engine-level logic (setup., NOT $ — never serialized) ---- */
<<run
setup.lastTrack = null;
setup.SEAL_LIMIT = 440;   /* TUNABLE: belonging-points before the deep seals you in.
   Accrues per room by setup.depthOf (depth 1-9). RETUNED 200→360 by the clean-run audit
   (2026-06-07, docs/AUDIT-CLEAN-RUN.md + tools/clean-run-path.mjs): the brand-route escape is
   gated behind a FULL descent (rope at L6, brand at L9) + climb back — at the old 200 a real
   escape was structurally IMPOSSIBLE, and cross-life marks can't help (stats, not the clock).
   RETUNED 360→440 (2026-07-02, review R10+C1): two reasons. (1) The map had GROWN under the old
   number — the tool's structural floor is now 223 (was 183), so 360 had quietly shrunk from 2.0×
   to 1.6× the floor. (2) Leveling now books LEVEL_SEAL per level (a focused run levels 2-3× →
   +30-45) and rests/shifts/gambles book passTime. Arithmetic at 2026-07-02: floor 223, rule-of-
   thumb real focused run 1.4-1.7× ≈ 312-379, + lessons ≈ 342-424, + one mid-run rest ≈ 350-440
   — so 440 keeps ordinary focused play escapable while a re-diver (double descent ≈ 446 floor
   alone) or a resident who sleeps and works and gambles still seals. The passTime acts are all
   OPTIONAL — the structural movement floor is unchanged.
   Sealed → you can no longer leave: EndingResident if caught in the deep, EndingTrapped if caught
   reaching for the surface. Re-run the tool after map changes; tune to taste. */
setup.SEAL_WARN = 260;    /* the "the way up is closing" warning threshold (~60% of SEAL_LIMIT) */
setup.SEAL_RESET_TO = 0;  /* switching your dominant form (rat→pig, etc.) resets $deepTurns to this — the
   settling comes undone and the deep must re-claim the new you. TUNABLE. Self-limiting: to change which
   nature dominates you must pump corruption into a new class, marching you toward the corruption-loss end,
   so it is a trade (belonging-time for corruption), not a free dodge; the low-corruption clean-run route
   never switches forms, so its clock floor is untouched. See the belonging block in PassageHeader. */

/* ---- TIME BEYOND WALKING (review R10+C1, 2026-07-02). The seal fiction says STAYING makes
   you belong, but the clock only charged moving — a night's sleep, a worked shift, an evening
   at the wheel were all clock-free, and leveling was the one power faucet the deep gave away
   for nothing (while the level-up prose claimed "the deep has been teaching you"). Now the
   time-taking optional acts book belonging too, in the same currency as the per-move clock. */
setup.LEVEL_SEAL  = 15;   /* belonging booked PER LEVEL gained (flat, not depth-scaled — the lesson
   costs what it costs wherever it lands; CombatVictory sits at depth 0). Booked in gainXP. */
setup.REST_TIME   = 4;    /* room-equivalents a full rest takes (the most expensive non-walk act);
   charged by the rest rooms ONLY when the heal actually heals — a full-vigor walk-through is free,
   so the rest rooms stay usable as corridors and the structural budget is untouched. */
setup.SHIFT_TIME  = 2;    /* room-equivalents a worked shift takes (doShift / doPressedShift / pressedToWork) */
setup.GAMBLE_TIME = 1;    /* room-equivalents one wheel-spin / bones-throw takes (spinWheel / castBones) */
/* Book `rooms` room-equivalents of belonging at the CURRENT room's depth — same currency and
   same seal check as the per-move clock, so a rest in hell can itself flip the seal (R2's
   caption + settle-beat pick the crossing up on the next render, no extra wiring). Depth-0
   rooms (intro/combat/UI) are free, matching the walk clock. Returns the cost booked. */
setup.passTime = function (rooms) {
    var V = State.variables;
    var d = setup.depthOf[State.passage] || 0;
    if (d < 1 || !rooms) { return 0; }
    var cost = rooms * d;
    V.deepTurns = (V.deepTurns || 0) + cost;
    if (V.deepTurns >= setup.SEAL_LIMIT) { V.sealed = true; }
    return cost;
};

/* per-passage depth modifier = the room's LAYER NUMBER (1-9). Drives how fast
   $deepTurns accrues toward SEAL_LIMIT — deeper accrues faster. Intro/combat = 0. */
setup.depthOf = {
    Start: 0, Captured: 0, WriggleFree: 0, Combat: 0, CombatVictory: 0, CombatLost: 0, Equipment: 0, Map: 0,
    /* L1 Storm Drains (in layer1-storm-drains.twee) */
    Outfall: 1, Maintenance: 1, ExitShaft: 1, TheCatchbasin: 1, TheGaugeHouse: 1,
    TheStreetCatch: 1, TheGulley: 1, TheStrainer: 1, TheAreaGrate: 1, TheFoamfall: 1,
    TheRatDrift: 1, TheRatDriftCleared: 1, TheStormFront: 1, TheRiverMouth: 1,
    TheSubwayBreach: 1, TheCulvertRun: 1, TheTideFlap: 1, TheRainShaft: 1,
    TheGalleryOfGrates: 1, TheJunctionVault: 1, TheStreetStair: 1, TheLarder: 1, TheCurdworks: 1,
    /* L2 Trunk Mains */
    Confluence: 2, GritChamber: 2, GritChamberCleared: 2, Gut: 2,
    TheRisers: 2, TheSiphon: 2, TheBlackValve: 2, ThePumpRoom: 2,
    TheGritTrap: 2, TheLostConduit: 2, TheValvePuzzle: 2, TheStallRow: 2, TheBackflow: 2,
    TheScreeningHall: 2, TheScreeningHallCleared: 2, TheFatberg: 2, TheDrumStore: 2, TheWeir: 2,
    TheManholeBase: 2, TheRatRun: 2, TheRatKing: 2, TheRatKingCleared: 2, TheSluice: 2,
    TheCleanPool: 2, TheCleanPoolWon: 2,
    /* L3 Old Drains */
    TheGreatSink: 3, TheCorkscrew: 3, TheOlderStair: 3, TheChokedArch: 3,
    TheCounterweight: 3, TheLimeVault: 3, TheVotiveDrain: 3, TheDeadLetterDrain: 3,
    TheWeepingGrate: 3, TheWarmSilt: 3, TheBoneWeir: 3, TheOldOutfall: 3,
    TheCrawl: 3, TheCrawlCleared: 3, TheBoneWeirCleared: 3,
    TheInscription: 3, TheCisternOverflow: 3, TheBrokenSiphon: 3, TheTanneryDrain: 3,
    TheRootCellar: 3, TheDripstone: 3, TheSumpGalleries: 3, TheSumpGalleriesCleared: 3,
    /* L4 Drowned Galleries (the "between" band; in layer4-drowned-galleries.twee.
       DrownedHall retagged 3→4 when L3 was inserted above it in the descent) */
    DrownedHall: 4, DeepHub: 4, TheCatacomb: 4, Cistern: 4, Gallery: 4,
    TheReflectingHall: 4, TheStillFont: 4, TheReliquary: 4, TheSiltKings: 4,
    TheTombIsland: 4, TheUndertow: 4, TheReflection: 4, TheDrownedChoir: 4,
    TheDrownedChoirCleared: 4, TheSunkenStair: 4, TheColonnade: 4, TheBellChamber: 4,
    TheSunkenChapel: 4, TheArchive: 4, TheWeepingArch: 4, TheDeepWell: 4,
    TheDeepWellCleared: 4,               /* the Glut boss lander (owner 2026-06-17) */
    TheBathhouse: 4, TheBathhouseCleared: 4,   /* the drowned sewer-sentō + the kappa-bested lander (owner 2026-06-18) */
    TheSluiceFork: 4, TheSumpVault: 4,   /* clean-vs-dirty fork (waders) */
    /* L5 The Hellmouth (in layer5-hellmouth.twee) — the threshold/spawn.
       Collapsed 2026-06-05 to 3 rooms: hub + throat (descent/swallow) + arrivals. */
    Hellmouth: 5, TheThroat: 5, TheArrivals: 5, TheIndenture: 5,
    /* L6 The Shambles (in layer6-shambles.twee) — the carnival hell-town */
    TheMidway: 6, HellMarket: 6, HellTavern: 6, TheFlyOnTheWall: 6, TheBackAlleys: 6, TheBigTop: 6,
    TheStage: 6, TheGaff: 6, TheFreakShow: 6, TheGames: 6, TheWheel: 6, TheGutterBones: 6,
    TheLostAndFound: 6, TheTill: 6, TheQuietBooth: 6, TheMenagerie: 6, TheMenagerieCleared: 6,
    TheCarousel: 6, TheFortuneTeller: 6, ThePuppetShow: 6, TheHallOfMirrors: 6,
    TheButchersStall: 6, TheConfectioner: 6, TheCageAct: 6, TheSmithStall: 6, TheTrinketStall: 6,
    TheStill: 6, TheGuttering: 6, TheGutteringCleared: 6,
    /* L7 The Belly of the Beast (in layer7-belly.twee) */
    TheCloaca: 7, TheGullet: 7, TheChute: 7, TheSphincter: 7, TheNavel: 7,
    TheStillborn: 7, TheMeatRow: 7, TheOrganTrove: 7, TheToothWell: 7, TheSurgery: 7,
    TheMolt: 7, TheSty: 7, TheStyCleared: 7, TheBoneLoom: 7, TheBoneLoomCleared: 7,
    TheGutway: 7, TheVilli: 7, TheBirthingDens: 7, TheHolding: 7, ThePrivyShrine: 7, TheLatrine: 7,
    TheAbscess: 7, TheWeepingWall: 7, TheTallyBoy: 7,
    TheGapCrossing: 7, TheGapCleared: 7,   /* reusable two-way gap-crossing (high bone-bridge / low filthy crevice) */
    TheBreeder: 7,                 /* the sow-breeder NPC (off the dens) */
    TheFleshcutter: 7,             /* the curse-cutter NPC */
    /* L8 The Rendering Works (in layer8-rendering-works.twee) */
    TheIntake: 8, TheKillingFloor: 8, TheManway: 8, TheRunoff: 8, TheRenderLock: 8,
    TheTallowHeart: 8, TheTally: 8, TheCooling: 8, TheTallowStore: 8, TheCandleWorks: 8,
    TheSoapVat: 8, TheVat: 8, TheWard: 8, ThePits: 8, ThePitsCleared: 8, TheLine: 8,
    TheHooks: 8, TheBoilHouse: 8, TheGreaseTrap: 8, TheForemansWalk: 8, TheTallowFalls: 8,
    TheConveyorFork: 8, TheVentControl: 8, TheColdStore: 8,   /* clean-vs-dirty fork (switch) */
    /* L9 The Sulphur Deep (in layer9-sulphur-deep.twee) — the bottom */
    TheBrimstoneShore: 9, TheVentField: 9, TheRunback: 9, TheCastleGate: 9, TheThroneWard: 9,
    TheCrust: 9, TheSulphurHoard: 9, TheVentMouth: 9, TheTribute: 9, TheThinCrust: 9,
    TheCourt: 9, TheCourtCleared: 9, TheNineVents: 9, TheYellowHall: 9, TheSolfatara: 9,
    TheFumarole: 9, TheVitriol: 9, TheGypsumWalk: 9, TheCanaryCrust: 9, TheCinderfall: 9,
    TheBurningTree: 9,
    TheFumeCut: 9, TheVentCache: 9   /* clean-vs-dirty fork (gas mask) */
};

/* item registry. Weapons carry a damage `die` ("XdY"); armor carries an `ac`
   bonus (added to 10 + DEX mod). See docs/COMBAT.md. */
setup.items = {
    rope:     { name: "coil of rope",   kind: "tool",   desc: "frayed but strong; long enough to bridge a broken climb" },
    /* per-hazard PASS-CLEAN tools (DIRECTION clean-vs-dirty forks, owner 2026-06-07): carry the
       matching one and the discreet shortcut costs you nothing; lack it and the filth gets in. */
    waders:   { name: "rubber waders",  kind: "tool", wards: "flood", desc: "chest-high waders, perished but whole; the muck cannot reach you through them" },
    gasmask:  { name: "oilskin hood",   kind: "tool", wards: "fume",  desc: "a hooded oilskin with glass eyes and a charcoal snout; the bad air goes around you, not into you" },
    hook:     { name: "rusted gaff",    kind: "weapon", type: "hook",   tier: "copper" }, /* the sewer-found hook */
    knife:    { name: "flensing knife", kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "bronze" },
    pipe:     { name: "length of pipe", kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "copper" }, /* a club — BLUNT wrecks shit-golems (filth scatters under a club, parts around a blade) */
    leathers: { name: "tanned leathers",kind: "armor",  ac: 1, tier: "leather" },
    salve:    { name: "grave-moss salve", kind: "consumable", heal: 8, desc: "a wad of the pale moss that grows on the drowned; pressed to a wound it knits flesh fast and asks no questions" }, /* usable in combat (Items) — costs your turn, heals $hp */
    /* CLOTHING = armor (one body slot): light garments worn for a social/disguise EFFECT (gated in
       room code) rather than protection — wearing one means NOT wearing your real armor. */
    motley:   { name: "carnival motley", kind: "armor", ac: 1, tier: "clothes", desc: "a motley — the patched, parti-coloured suit of a fool or a fairground freak, pieced from a hundred castoff costumes; the barker fits you in it to make you look the part, which is the danger" },
    overalls: { name: "sty-hand's overalls", kind: "armor", ac: 1, tier: "clothes", desc: "heavy canvas work overalls off a hook in the breeding-dens, stiff with the sty's own filth; wear them and move like you've a trough to get to, and a boar reads you as one more hand come to muck out — not as meat" },
    brand:    { name: "branch that never stops burning", kind: "tool", desc: "broken from the tree in the Sulphur Deep that burns and is never consumed; a fire that lasts — fire enough to melt a fatberg from the way up" },
    /* junk: what a coin becomes in your hand under the coins-turn-to-objects curse
       (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §D). Worthless rubbish; clutters the pack, sells for nothing. */
    junk_hair:   { name: "knot of wet hair",  kind: "junk", desc: "a cold sodden hank that was a coin a breath ago" },
    junk_cap:    { name: "rusted bottlecap",   kind: "junk", desc: "crimped, lightless, worth less than the rust on it" },
    junk_button: { name: "cracked bone button",kind: "junk", desc: "off some drowned coat; the coin went grey and went this" },

    /* ============================ EQUIPMENT CATALOG (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §A/B/C/D/E) ============================
       Schema on each gear item:
         weapon   : die "XdY", dtype "blunt"|"edged", tier (see WEAPON_TIERS), magic?, curse?, apparentTier?
         armor    : ac (bonus), tier (see ARMOR_TIERS), magic?, curse?, apparentTier?
         accessory: slot "ring"|"necklace"|"boots"|"gloves", blessed|cursed (flavor), magic?, curse?
         magic    : { scope:"all"|"rat"|"pig"|"filth"|<enemyId>, bonus:(a stat|"all"|"hp"|"ac"|"encounter"|"dmg"), amount:N }
         curse    : a curse-id string | {id,stat?,class?,amount?} | an array of those (see CURSE_LABEL)
         apparentTier : (CURSED weapons/armor only) the material it MASQUERADES as — drives the masked
                        "unidentified" display + the drop-mismatch rule (high apparent tier on a weak
                        monster reads as too-good-to-be-true → very likely cursed). Owner 2026-06-06.
       HIDDEN-UNTIL-EQUIPPED (owner): an item with magic OR curse stays unidentified (shown only by its
       apparent tier) until you equip it — by which point a curse already has you. Plain gear (no magic/
       curse) has nothing to hide, so it always reads true. Numbers are tunable (tools/equip-check.mjs). */

    /* ---- WEAPONS — TWO axes now (owner 2026-06-07): TIER (rusty→steel→magic+cursed = the "level", a
       flat damage bonus) × TYPE (dagger/hook/spear/sword/axe/hammer = the damage RANGE/die, the flavor,
       and the unlocked SPECIAL). `die` + `dtype` DERIVE from type×tier (setup.weaponDie / weaponDtype /
       TYPE_DIE / TIER_DMG_BONUS) — items just declare type + tier. Type die (variance): dagger 1d4 ·
       hook 1d6 · spear 1d6 · sword 1d8 · axe 1d10 · hammer 1d12; tier flat bonus: rusty +0 · copper +1 ·
       bronze +2 · iron +3 · steel +4. dtype: hammer blunt, the rest edged. Type SPECIALS: sword/spear →
       Sweeping blow (all foes); axe → Cleave (two foes); hammer → Crushing blow (stun); hook → Snag
       (stun); dagger → Flurry (extra cuts). Enemy TYPE-affinities live on the enemy sheet
       (weakTypes/resistTypes). Lint with tools/equip-check.mjs. ---- */
    /* DAGGERS — small/fast, flurry special */
    rusty_shiv:   { name: "rusty shiv",        kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "rusty"  },
    copper_dirk:  { name: "copper dirk",       kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "copper" },
    iron_dagger:  { name: "iron dagger",       kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "iron"   },
    steel_dagger: { name: "steel stiletto",    kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "steel"  },
    /* HOOKS — gaffs/flesh-hooks, snag-stun special */
    rusty_hook:   { name: "bent hook",         kind: "weapon", type: "hook",   tier: "rusty"  },
    bronze_hook:  { name: "bronze flesh-hook", kind: "weapon", type: "hook",   tier: "bronze" },
    iron_hook:    { name: "iron gaff",         kind: "weapon", type: "hook",   tier: "iron"   },
    /* SPEARS — reach, sweep special */
    copper_spear: { name: "copper spear",      kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "copper" },
    bronze_spear: { name: "bronze spear",      kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "bronze" },
    iron_spear:   { name: "iron spear",        kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "iron"   },
    steel_spear:  { name: "steel pike",        kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "steel"  },
    /* SWORDS — balanced, sweep special */
    bronze_sword: { name: "bronze shortsword", kind: "weapon", type: "sword",  tier: "bronze" },
    iron_blade:   { name: "iron blade",        kind: "weapon", type: "sword",  tier: "iron"   },
    steel_blade:  { name: "steel longblade",   kind: "weapon", type: "sword",  tier: "steel"  },
    /* AXES — heavy edged, cleave special */
    copper_axe:   { name: "copper axe",        kind: "weapon", type: "axe",    tier: "copper" },
    bronze_axe:   { name: "bronze axe",        kind: "weapon", type: "axe",    tier: "bronze" },
    iron_axe:     { name: "iron axe",          kind: "weapon", type: "axe",    tier: "iron"   },
    steel_axe:    { name: "steel greataxe",    kind: "weapon", type: "axe",    tier: "steel"  },
    /* HAMMERS/CLUBS — heaviest, BLUNT (scatter golems), crushing-stun special */
    rusty_cudgel: { name: "rusty cudgel",      kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "rusty"  },
    copper_mace:  { name: "copper mace",       kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "copper" },
    bronze_maul:  { name: "bronze maul",       kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "bronze" },
    iron_hammer:  { name: "iron hammer",       kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "iron"   },
    steel_maul:   { name: "steel warmaul",     kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "steel"  },
    /* MAGIC weapons (rare, never sold; per-creature scope = much stronger than "all") */
    ratbane_spike: { name: "rat-bane spike",    kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "magic", magic: { scope: "rat",   bonus: "dmg", amount: 4 }, desc: "an old verminer's spike; it bites rat-things far past its size" },
    golembreaker:  { name: "golem-breaker maul",kind: "weapon", type: "hammer", tier: "magic", magic: { scope: "filth", bonus: "dmg", amount: 4 }, desc: "a maul that scatters aggregate filth like a thrown stone scatters flies" },
    pig_skewer:    { name: "pig-skewer pike",   kind: "weapon", type: "spear",  tier: "magic", magic: { scope: "pig",   bonus: "dmg", amount: 4 }, desc: "a long iron made for the kind of pig that stands upright" },
    bright_blade:  { name: "bright blade",      kind: "weapon", type: "sword",  tier: "magic", magic: { scope: "all",   bonus: "dmg", amount: 2 }, desc: "it keeps an edge of clean daylight no amount of muck can foul" },
    /* CURSED weapons — strong-looking (apparentTier), nasty rider, will not come off */
    hungry_knife:  { name: "hungry knife",      kind: "weapon", type: "dagger", tier: "cursed", apparentTier: "steel", magic: { scope: "all", bonus: "dmg", amount: 3 }, curse: ["irreversible"], taint: { cls: "filth", amt: 2, line: "The hungry knife feeds as it bites — {amt} of you goes down the blade from your {seg}, the part that could still have washed clean, and it does not give anything back." }, desc: "it feeds, and what it feeds on is the part of you that could still wash clean" },
    biting_axe:    { name: "biting axe",        kind: "weapon", type: "axe",    tier: "cursed", apparentTier: "iron",  magic: { bonus: "str", amount: 2 }, curse: [{ id: "stat_down", stat: "wis", amount: 2 }], desc: "it wants to swing, and it dulls the part of you that knows when not to" },

    /* ---- ARMOR — ascending: cursed < rags < clothes < robes < leather < copper < bronze < iron <
       steel < magic. AC ladder (player AC = 10 + DEX + ac): rags 0 / clothes 1 / robes 1 / leather 1
       / copper 2 / bronze 2 / iron 3 / steel 4. `leathers` (above) is the leather rung. ---- */
    rags:          { name: "filthy rags",       kind: "armor", ac: 0, tier: "rags"    },
    clothes:       { name: "dead man's clothes",kind: "armor", ac: 1, tier: "clothes" },
    robes:         { name: "quiet robes",       kind: "armor", ac: 1, tier: "robes", magic: { bonus: "encounter", amount: 1 }, desc: "drab, soft, soundless; the deep's eye slides off the one who wears them (the light/caster line — low AC, a quiet rider)" },
    copper_scale:  { name: "copper scale",      kind: "armor", ac: 2, tier: "copper"  },
    bronze_plate:  { name: "bronze plate",      kind: "armor", ac: 2, tier: "bronze"  },
    iron_plate:    { name: "iron plate",        kind: "armor", ac: 3, tier: "iron"    },
    steel_plate:   { name: "steel plate",       kind: "armor", ac: 4, tier: "steel"   },
    warded_mail:   { name: "warded mail",       kind: "armor", ac: 4, tier: "magic", magic: { bonus: "all", amount: 1 }, desc: "old work, blessed at the forge by someone who is now far below regretting it" },
    /* CURSED armor — looks like the finest plate, fits like a held breath, drops you when it counts */
    comely_coat:   { name: "comely coat",       kind: "armor", ac: 1, tier: "cursed", apparentTier: "steel",
                     magic: { bonus: "ac", amount: 3 }, curse: ["autosurrender"], desc: "the handsomest armor in the deep, and the moment a blade is drawn your knees decide for you" },

    /* ---- ACCESSORIES — four slots (ring/necklace/boots/gloves), each BLESSED (a magic bonus) or
       CURSED (a rider). Together they cover every magic-bonus type and all eleven curses. ---- */
    /* BLESSED */
    quick_boots:   { name: "quick boots",       kind: "accessory", slot: "boots",    blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "dex", amount: 2 }, desc: "light, dry, wrong for this place; your step comes back to you" },
    felted_boots:  { name: "felted boots",      kind: "accessory", slot: "boots",    blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "encounter", amount: 2 }, desc: "they fall soft on the iron; less of the deep turns to look" },
    ward_necklace: { name: "bone-ward charm",   kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "ac", amount: 1 }, desc: "a knot of small bones the blows seem to slide around" },
    corded_teeth:  { name: "corded teeth",      kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "hp", amount: 8 }, desc: "somebody's teeth on a cord; wearing them you are harder to finish" },
    saint_medal:   { name: "old saint's medal", kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "all", amount: 1 }, desc: "worn smooth by a thumb that prayed; all of you stands a little straighter (rare)" },
    will_ring:     { name: "ring of cold will", kind: "accessory", slot: "ring",     blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "wis", amount: 2 }, desc: "it keeps your head your own a moment longer than the deep would like" },
    clear_lens:    { name: "cracked lens", kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace",      blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "int", amount: 2 }, desc: "a monocle on a chain; through it the deep's tricks show their seams" },
    glamour_charm: { name: "glamour charm", kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace",     blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "cha", amount: 2 }, desc: "a little brass thing that makes the deep's bargainers warmer to you than you've earned" },
    dim_ring:      { name: "dim ring",          kind: "accessory", slot: "ring",     blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "encounter", amount: 2 }, desc: "a band that drinks the light; the deep looks past you wearing it" },
    grip_gloves:   { name: "tar-grip gloves",   kind: "accessory", slot: "gloves",   blessed: true, magic: { bonus: "str", amount: 2 }, desc: "the grip they give turns a weak blow into a real one" },
    /* CURSED — strong upside, hard rider, will not come off */
    greed_ring:    { name: "greedfinger ring",  kind: "accessory", slot: "ring",     cursed: true, magic: { bonus: "str", amount: 3 }, curse: ["coinrot"], desc: "it makes the hand strong and the hand ruins money" },
    /* MIXED cursed (boon + rider — the tempting traps; KEEP their magic): lead_boots, greed_ring. */
    lead_boots:    { name: "lead boots",        kind: "accessory", slot: "boots",    cursed: true, magic: { bonus: "con", amount: 3 }, curse: ["norun"], desc: "they root you: nothing gets through and you will never run again" },
    /* PURE-negative cursed (owner 2026-06-07: MOST cursed items are just a curse, no boon — the
       punishment you get tricked into by hidden-until-equipped; only a couple are mixed temptations). */
    manacle_ring:  { name: "manacle ring",      kind: "accessory", slot: "ring",     cursed: true, curse: ["nopickup"], desc: "it sits like a shackle; your fingers forget how to take a thing up" },
    sty_signet:    { name: "sty-signet ring",   kind: "accessory", slot: "ring",     cursed: true, curse: [{ id: "always_class", class: "pig" }], desc: "from the moment it's on, the deep can only ever make you one thing" },
    bound_gaunts:  { name: "bound gauntlets",   kind: "accessory", slot: "gloves",   cursed: true, curse: ["noattack"], desc: "they close over your hands and will not let the hands strike" },
    crown_thorns:  { name: "crown of thorns",   kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", cursed: true, curse: ["stat_down_all"], desc: "it lessens you in every way, and grips like it grew there" },
    silver_muzzle: { name: "silver muzzle",     kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", cursed: true, curse: ["nospeak"], desc: "beautiful on you, and your voice will not come past it" },
    bell_charm:    { name: "brass bell charm",  kind: "accessory", slot: "necklace", cursed: true, curse: ["encounter_up"], desc: "it rings with your every step, and the deep hears, and comes" },

    /* ---- GRAFTS — the Cutter's body-mods (L7 TheSurgery, owner 2026-06-08). Kind "accessory" so the
       modifier pipeline / Equipment screen handle them for free, but they live in their own GRAFT_SLOTS
       (eye/hand/hide/heart), are BOUND (never come off), are NOT carried cross-life (a new life is a
       new body), and are installed ONLY by the Cutter — at a corruption cost (graftSeg/graftAmt, class
       "pig": you are made fitter for the belly by being made more of it). Real mechanical payoff is
       the point — this is the "usable" upgrade the table was missing. The trade is your humanity. ---- */
    graft_eye:   { name: "lamp-eye",        kind: "accessory", slot: "eye",   graft: true, graftSeg: "head",  graftAmt: 12, magic: { bonus: "encounter", amount: 2 }, desc: "a wet amber eye that gathers what little light the deep allows; danger announces itself before it arrives" },
    graft_hand:  { name: "tireless hand",   kind: "accessory", slot: "hand",  graft: true, graftSeg: "armR",  graftAmt: 14, magic: { bonus: "str",       amount: 2 }, desc: "a heavier hand than the one you were born with, and it never tires of the work of hurting" },
    graft_hide:  { name: "turned hide",     kind: "accessory", slot: "hide",  graft: true, graftSeg: "torso", graftAmt: 16, magic: { bonus: "ac",        amount: 2 }, desc: "your skin recut as the belly's own: thick, grey, slick, and a blade slides off it where it would have bitten" },
    graft_heart: { name: "second heart",    kind: "accessory", slot: "heart", graft: true, graftSeg: "torso", graftAmt: 14, magic: { bonus: "hp",        amount: 12 }, desc: "a second slow heart set in beside the first; you are much harder to stop now, having two" }
};

/* tier orders (ascending desirability) — used by the shop, drops, identification, and the
   tools/equip-check.mjs linter. "cursed" sits at the bottom of the TRUE order, but a cursed item
   MASQUERADES as its apparentTier. */
setup.SLOT_LABEL = { weapon: "Weapon", armor: "Armor", ring: "Ring", necklace: "Necklace", boots: "Boots", gloves: "Gloves", eye: "Eye (graft)", hand: "Hand (graft)", hide: "Hide (graft)", heart: "Heart (graft)" };
setup.WEAPON_TIERS = ["cursed", "rusty", "copper", "bronze", "iron", "steel", "magic"];
setup.ARMOR_TIERS  = ["cursed", "rags", "clothes", "robes", "leather", "copper", "bronze", "iron", "steel", "magic"];
/* the rung a metal tier sits on for drop-matching (cursed/magic are off-ladder specials) */
setup.MATERIAL_RANK = { rusty: 1, rags: 1, clothes: 1, robes: 1, copper: 2, leather: 2, bronze: 3, iron: 4, steel: 5 };
setup.itemTier = function (id) { var it = setup.items[id]; return it ? (it.tier || null) : null; };
/* what an item LOOKS like (cursed → its lie; everything else → its real tier) */
setup.apparentTier = function (id) { var it = setup.items[id]; return it ? (it.apparentTier || it.tier || null) : null; };

/* ---- WEAPON TYPES (owner 2026-06-07) — the second axis. TYPE sets the damage RANGE (die) + the
   broad blunt/edged class + the unlocked special; TIER adds a flat damage bonus (the "level"). A
   weapon's `die`/`dtype` DERIVE from type×tier unless the item overrides `die`/`dtype` explicitly. */
setup.WEAPON_TYPES = ["dagger", "hook", "spear", "sword", "axe", "hammer"];
setup.TYPE_DIE    = { dagger: "1d4", hook: "1d6", spear: "1d6", sword: "1d8", axe: "1d10", hammer: "1d12" };
setup.TYPE_DTYPE  = { dagger: "edged", hook: "edged", spear: "edged", sword: "edged", axe: "edged", hammer: "blunt" };
setup.TIER_DMG_BONUS = { rusty: 0, copper: 1, bronze: 2, iron: 3, steel: 4, magic: 4, cursed: 3 };
setup.weaponProfileDie = function (type, tier) {
    var base = setup.TYPE_DIE[type] || "1d6", b = setup.TIER_DMG_BONUS[tier] || 0;
    return b > 0 ? (base + "+" + b) : base;
};
setup.weaponDie = function (id) {                 /* the die a weapon actually rolls */
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it) { return "1d2"; }
    return it.die || setup.weaponProfileDie(it.type, it.tier);
};
setup.weaponDtype = function (id) {               /* blunt / edged */
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it) { return "blunt"; }
    return it.dtype || setup.TYPE_DTYPE[it.type] || "edged";
};
setup.weaponKind = function (id) {                /* the fine type (dagger/hook/…) or null */
    var it = setup.items[id]; return it ? (it.type || null) : null;
};

/* enemy registry — the bestiary (see MAP-ARCHITECTURE "Bestiary"). The sewer is
   MUTAGENIC: the filth of the earth swirls together into a collective evil greater
   than the sum of its parts. Sewer band = rat men + shit golems; the deep hinge
   throws up stranger things; the sulfur castle (L9) is full of pig demons (the
   kidnapper's own kind). */
/* D&D-style schema (see docs/COMBAT.md): statLevel = the flat value of ALL SIX
   ability scores (boss: rat men all 3s, sewage demons all 9s); hd = hit dice
   (size); weaponDie = its natural attack die. HP/AC/to-hit/damage all derive from
   these in setup.startFight — nothing hand-tuned per creature. */
/* `class` = the mutagen this thing carries; it rubs off on a LOSER (setup.loseFight):
   beaten by a pig-demon → you go a little pig, by a rat-man → rat, by the filth → filth. */
/* `weakTo`/`resists` = the broad blunt|edged class (×1.5 / ×0.5 via setup.typeMult); `weakTypes`/
   `resistTypes` = FINE weapon-TYPE affinities (owner 2026-06-07: affinities live on the enemy sheet).
   typeMult merges both (weak-not-resist → 1.5, resist-not-weak → 0.5). Pick the right tool. */
/* `move` = the SIGNATURE move (review R12): the id of a setup.ENEMY_MOVES entry, telegraph-then-
   payoff — every `every` rounds (default 3) the thing spends its attack WINDING UP (the telegraph
   line is your window: Guard blunts the payoff, a stun cancels it, Run leaves before it lands),
   and the payoff auto-lands next round. Moves come from what each thing IS; several take agency
   ON the turn (held / engulfed / dragged toward the shift). Prose + effects in ENEMY_MOVES
   (script block). NOT modeled in tools/combat-sim.mjs (a per-hit probe, disclaimed in-file). */
/* `parleys` (review R16) = the thing has a MIND a mid-fight offer can reach: the minded kinds
   (rat-men run councils; kappa keep courtesies; gorgers/pig-demons literally take tolls at the
   forks; the sty-hand's whole job is recruiting) accept a Yield — coin or labour. The mindless
   (rats, golems, crawler, drowned, grafted) and the Glut do not; offering at them wastes the
   round (telegraphed in the yield submenu). Read via setup.packListens(). */
setup.enemies = {
    /* SEWER — vermin & aggregate filth */
    rat:       { name: "demon rat",     statLevel: 3,  hd: 1, weaponDie: "1d4", coins: 2, class: "rat",   weakTypes: ["dagger"], resistTypes: ["hammer"], move: "squeal" }, /* small & quick: a knife catches it, a maul whiffs */
    ratman:    { name: "rat-man",       statLevel: 3,  hd: 2, weaponDie: "1d4", coins: 3, class: "rat",   weakTypes: ["sword", "dagger"], resistTypes: ["hammer"], move: "squeal", parleys: true }, /* upright, handed, hungry — and clever enough to price you */
    shitgolem: { name: "shit-golem",    statLevel: 9,  hd: 4, weaponDie: "1d8", coins: 5, class: "filth", weakTo: "blunt", resists: "edged", weakTypes: ["hammer"], move: "engulf" }, /* filth swirled into one will; a blade just parts the muck — BLUNT scatters it */
    /* DEEP HINGE / BETWEEN — the stranger things (L3-4) */
    crawler:   { name: "drain-crawler", statLevel: 5,  hd: 2, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 4, class: "filth", weakTypes: ["spear"], resistTypes: ["dagger"], move: "coil" }, /* blind, pale, grown long — reach skewers it */
    drowned:   { name: "the drowned",   statLevel: 6,  hd: 3, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 3, class: "filth", weakTypes: ["spear"], resistTypes: ["hammer"], move: "grapple" }, /* waterlogged: pierce it; blunt just thuds into sodden meat */
    kappa:     { name: "a kappa",        statLevel: 6,  hd: 2, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 3, class: "filth", weakTypes: ["dagger"], resistTypes: ["hammer"], img: "CappaAtendant", move: "pullunder", parleys: true }, /* a sewer-sentō bath-attendant drowner; small, beaked, webbed, a dish of clean water on its skull. The DISH is its real weakness — bow it into spilling (see TheBathhouse) rather than fight; class filth (a loss drowns you into the deep). Portrait: img/enemy/CappaAtendant.png (owner 2026-06-18) */
    /* HELL — the Belly of the Beast (L7) and below */
    grafted:   { name: "the grafted",   statLevel: 8,  hd: 3, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 4, class: "filth", weakTypes: ["axe", "sword"], resistTypes: ["dagger"], move: "manyhands" }, /* assembled from parts — cut the seams; small cuts don't matter */
    gorger:    { name: "a gorger",      statLevel: 9,  hd: 4, weaponDie: "1d8", coins: 5, class: "filth", weakTypes: ["hook"], resistTypes: ["spear"], move: "gulp", parleys: true }, /* bloated flesh-grower — haul it open with a hook; runs a gantry toll when it forecrews */
    pigdemon:  { name: "pig-demon",     statLevel: 10, hd: 4, weaponDie: "1d8", coins: 6, class: "pig",   weakTypes: ["spear"], resistTypes: ["dagger"], move: "gore", parleys: true }, /* a true demon; skewer it (the pig-skewer's whole point); shrugs off small cuts */
    /* THE PRESS-GANG (owner 2026-06-17, art Pig_PressGang.png) — a sty-hand boar with a shovel,
       the recruiter the floor sends to march you to a shift. Mid-tier; class pig (a loss to it
       rubs pig into you). Fronts the job-aware "pigpress" encounter; weak to the spear like its kin. */
    pig_pressgang: { name: "a sty-hand",   statLevel: 6,  hd: 3, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 4, class: "pig",   weakTypes: ["spear"], resistTypes: ["dagger"], img: "Pig_PressGang", move: "drag", parleys: true }, /* shovel-armed; herds bodies to work — an offered shift is its whole errand */
    /* BOSS — THE GLUT (owner 2026-06-17, art demon1.png) — the apex shit-golem: the filth that
       everything drained INTO, at the bottom of the Deep Well (L4), swirled into one will greater
       than the sum of its parts. A named, tougher shit-golem; same nature (BLUNT scatters it, a
       blade just parts the muck), amplified. Lives in TheDeepWell, optional. */
    glut:      { name: "the Glut",      statLevel: 12, hd: 6, weaponDie: "1d10", coins: 0, class: "filth", weakTo: "blunt", resists: "edged", weakTypes: ["hammer"], resistTypes: ["dagger", "sword"], img: "demon1", boss: true, move: "engulf", every: 2 }, /* the drains, woken; winds oftener than its lessers; reward is hand-placed in TheDeepWellCleared */
    /* THE SHORT-WEIGHT (owner 2026-07-03) — the combat form of the WIS-blind ambush (the third
       ledger; see setup.SHORTWEIGHT). Folded into a safe-seeming corner until the oblivious sit;
       a modest but real mid-low threat that, on a failed WIS sense, gets a FREE opening turn
       (setup.ambushFight). Class filth (a deep-hinge trickster). No band gate — the short-weights
       keep score everywhere. No art file (glyph-only until one lands). */
    shortweight: { name: "a short-weight", statLevel: 4, hd: 2, weaponDie: "1d6", coins: 3, class: "filth", img: "shortweight" },
    /* THE SMOKE CREATURES (owner 2026-07-20; Phase 0 of docs/HANDOFF-SMOKE-CREATURES.md — the FOURTH
       nature's first, cheapest slice). Built as class FILTH for now (smoke = the air-phase of filth;
       zero body-model change) so the aesthetic + combat identity can be tested before a 4th class earns
       its keep. Their signature is IDENTITY DAMAGE (idmg): they barely tear flesh (weaponDie 1d2-1d3,
       low statLevel-mod), but every landed touch takes a little of what you ARE — you can win and still
       walk out further gone (dispersed, "less singular"). idmgFlavor "smoke" gives the dispersal voice.
       You can't stab smoke: a blade parts it and it closes (resists edged); fists / a club SCATTER the
       held-together aggregate (weakTo blunt — the shit-golem's physics, applied to air). Low HP: knock
       the shape apart and it comes undone. Den in the FUMING places (the still's reek, L6). */
    shadowperson: { name: "a shadow-person", statLevel: 8, hd: 2, weaponDie: "1d3", coins: 2, class: "filth", idmg: 2, idmgFlavor: "smoke", weakTo: "blunt", resists: "edged", weakTypes: ["hammer"], resistTypes: ["dagger", "sword"], img: "shadowperson", move: "chorus", parleys: true }, /* a person-shaped aggregate of smoke, soot, and flies, holding a human outline out of habit; the "what you're becoming" mirror. Speaks as WE. idmg 2 = a whole (won) fight lands ~12-16 corruption diffuse — real (winning finally costs your SELF) but under a LOSS's ceiling; verified live, tunable. */
    smokewisp:    { name: "a smoke-wisp",    statLevel: 4, hd: 1, weaponDie: "1d2", coins: 0, class: "filth", idmg: 1, idmgFlavor: "smoke", resists: "edged", resistTypes: ["dagger", "sword"], img: "smokewisp" }   /* ignis fatuus — a loose lick of the aggregate, the glow that says THIS WAY; fodder, but each touch takes a wisp of you */
};

setup.has = function (id) { return State.variables.inventory.includes(id); };

/* meta-puzzle: the Unbinding Sigil is complete once all three fragments
   (one per hell layer) are collected. Fragments placed when L7-9 are built. */
setup.SIGIL_FRAGMENTS = ["sigil_warrens", "sigil_rendering", "sigil_deep"];
setup.hasSigil = function () {
    return setup.SIGIL_FRAGMENTS.every(function (f) { return State.variables.sigil.includes(f); });
};

/* ---- Persistent marks (cross-life) ---- */
setup.hasMark = function (id) { return !!recall("marks", {})[id]; };
setup.markCount = function (id) { return recall("marks", {})[id] || 0; };
setup.addMark = function (id) {
    var m = recall("marks", {});
    m[id] = (m[id] || 0) + 1;
    memorize("marks", m);
};
setup.forgetMarks = function () { forget("marks"); forget("runs"); forget("scars"); forget("discovered"); forget("build"); };  /* dev/reset + manual-restart clean slate */
setup.restartCarry = function () { memorize("carryover", true); Engine.restart(); };

/* ---- Discovered rooms (cross-life — survive death, like marks/curses) ----
   The map you carry between lives. Charted rooms stay charted past Engine.restart
   (memorize → localStorage), so a veteran has a fuller map than a first-timer.
   Foundation for an eventual in-game fog-of-war map; for now it's pure data.
   Only real map rooms count: setup.depthOf[name] for L1-9 is truthy; intro/combat
   (depth 0) and non-room passages (undefined) are skipped automatically. */
setup.discover = function (name) {
    if (!name || !setup.depthOf[name]) return;   /* real rooms only (depth >= 1) */
    var d = recall("discovered", {});
    if (!d[name]) { d[name] = 1; memorize("discovered", d); }
};
setup.isDiscovered = function (name) { return !!recall("discovered", {})[name]; };
setup.discoveredSet = function () { return recall("discovered", {}); };
setup.discoveredCount = function (layer) {   /* layer omitted = whole map */
    var d = recall("discovered", {}), n = 0;
    for (var k in d) { if (d[k] && (layer == null || setup.depthOf[k] === layer)) n++; }
    return n;
};
setup.forgetDiscovered = function () { forget("discovered"); };  /* dev/reset */

/* Called once at the end of every run: banks the fate + any bargains taken as
   permanent marks, and increments the run counter. Pure accumulation. */
setup.recordRun = function (fate) {
    var V = State.variables;
    setup.addMark(fate);
    if (V.gaveUpFace)     { setup.addMark("faceless"); }   /* the Understudy's bargain */
    if (V.hasWard)        { setup.addMark("rendered"); }   /* Tallow's ward */
    if (V.tookTheBargain) { setup.addMark("indebted"); }   /* the Whisperer's deal */
    if (setup.bankCursedGear) { setup.bankCursedGear(); }  /* cursed gear carries to the next life */
    memorize("runs", recall("runs", 0) + 1);
};

/* ===================== D&D-STYLE COMBAT ENGINE =====================
   Full spec + design rationale in docs/COMBAT.md. Pure-ish helpers live in
   setup.* so they are testable (mirrored by tools/combat-sim.mjs). Dice use
   Math.random (combat isn't replayed from saves, so save-determinism isn't
   needed here — noted in COMBAT.md). ================================== */

setup.STATS = ["str", "dex", "con", "int", "wis", "cha"];

/* standard 5e ability modifier */
setup.mod = function (score) { return Math.floor((score - 10) / 2); };

/* dice */
setup.d = function (sides) { return Math.floor(Math.random() * sides) + 1; };
setup.rollDie = function (spec) {            /* "1d8", "2d4+1" -> a roll */
    if (!spec) { return 0; }
    var m = /^(\d+)d(\d+)([+-]\d+)?$/.exec(spec);
    if (!m) { return 0; }
    var n = +m[1], sides = +m[2], bonus = m[3] ? +m[3] : 0, total = bonus;
    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) { total += setup.d(sides); }
    return total;
};

setup.PLAYER_PROF = 2;   /* the protagonist's edge (added to player attack rolls); scales with level later */

/* --- PLAYER stats: flat per level (boss: all 7s at L1), shifted by cross-life
   marks. The curses are a BUILD: some harden you even as they cost you. --- */
setup.LEVEL_BASE = { 1: 7 };   /* per-level flat ability value; default growth below */
setup.baseScore = function (lvl) {
    return setup.LEVEL_BASE[lvl] != null ? setup.LEVEL_BASE[lvl] : (7 + (lvl - 1) * 2);
};

/* ---- XP & LEVELING ----
   XP a defeated enemy yields = difficulty (statLevel) × size (hd) × 4. The
   easiest real opponent — the rat-man (sl3/hd2) — is worth 24; the fodder rat
   (sl3/hd1) 12; the pig-demon (sl10/hd4) 160. (Table in docs/COMBAT.md.) */
setup.enemyXP = function (e) { return e.statLevel * e.hd * 4; };

/* cumulative XP needed to REACH a level: xpToReach(2)=120, (3)=360, (4)=720,
   (5)=1200… increments grow by 120 each tier (120/240/360/480), so every level
   is a longer climb than the last — standard scaling. ~5 rat-men (5×24=120)
   take a fresh life to level 2. Resets each life with $xp/$level. */
setup.xpToReach = function (level) { return 60 * (level - 1) * level; };
setup.xpForNext = function () { return setup.xpToReach((State.variables.level || 1) + 1); };

/* award XP and apply any level-ups it earns. Bumps $level, rebuilds the sheet
   (ability scores grow on the per-level curve in baseScore), and adds the
   newly-gained max HP to current vigor (you gain the new hit points — NOT a full
   heal). Loops so a big payout can grant several levels. Returns levels gained
   so the caller can narrate it. */
setup.gainXP = function (amount) {
    var V = State.variables;
    V.xp = (V.xp || 0) + amount;
    var gained = 0;
    while (V.xp >= setup.xpToReach((V.level || 1) + 1)) {
        var oldMax = V.maxhp;
        V.level = (V.level || 1) + 1;
        setup.recomputePlayer();   /* recomputes scores + maxhp from the new level */
        if (V.hp != null) { V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + Math.max(0, V.maxhp - oldMax)); }
        gained++;
    }
    if (gained > 0) {
        /* R10: the deep has been teaching you — and it does not teach for free. Every other
           strength source is priced in self; the lesson is priced in belonging. Flat per level
           (not depth-scaled — CombatVictory sits at depth 0), same seal check as the clock. */
        V.deepTurns = (V.deepTurns || 0) + setup.LEVEL_SEAL * gained;
        if (V.deepTurns >= setup.SEAL_LIMIT) { V.sealed = true; }
    }
    return gained;
};

/* ===================== PER-SEGMENT CORRUPTION & TRANSFORMATION =====================
   The body is six segments; each carries corruption attributed to a MUTAGEN CLASS
   (the filth that touched it). A segment that fills to 100 TRANSFORMS into its
   dominant class for the rest of the life. The single "general corruption" meter
   ($corruption) is a derived MIRROR = the average of the six segment totals, kept in
   sync below so every legacy read still works. Full spec: docs/TRANSFORMATION.md.
   Owner design (2026-06-04): thresholds 30/50/75/100 (tingle/tainted/turning/turned);
   class is set by the SOURCE of the corruption; transformation resets each life; fully
   becoming one creature banks a lingering CREATURE-KIN mark (that species turns friendlier).
   ============================================================================== */
setup.SEGMENTS = ["head", "torso", "armL", "armR", "legL", "legR"];
setup.CLASSES  = ["rat", "pig", "filth"];
setup.SEG_LABEL   = { head: "head", torso: "torso", armL: "L-arm", armR: "R-arm", legL: "L-leg", legR: "R-leg" };
setup.CLASS_LABEL = { rat: "rat", pig: "pig", filth: "filth" };
/* narrative stage by segment total; thresholds are the owner's 30/50/75/100 */
setup.STAGE_AT = [
    { at: 100, key: "turned",  word: "turned"  },
    { at: 75,  key: "turning", word: "turning" },
    { at: 50,  key: "tainted", word: "tainted" },
    { at: 30,  key: "tingle",  word: "a tingle" }
];

setup.freshBody = function () {
    var b = {};
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { b[s] = { rat: 0, pig: 0, filth: 0 }; });
    return b;
};
setup.freshForm = function () {
    var f = {};
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { f[s] = "human"; });
    return f;
};

/* a segment's total corruption (0-100) and its dominant class */
setup.segTotal = function (seg) {
    var v = (State.variables.body || {})[seg]; if (!v) { return 0; }
    return Math.min(100, v.rat + v.pig + v.filth);
};
setup.segClass = function (seg) {
    var v = (State.variables.body || {})[seg]; if (!v) { return null; }
    var best = null, bv = 0;
    setup.CLASSES.forEach(function (c) { if (v[c] > bv) { bv = v[c]; best = c; } });
    return best;
};
setup.segStage = function (seg) {
    if (((State.variables.form || {})[seg] || "human") !== "human") { return "turned"; }
    var t = setup.segTotal(seg);
    for (var i = 0; i < setup.STAGE_AT.length; i++) { if (t >= setup.STAGE_AT[i].at) { return setup.STAGE_AT[i].key; } }
    return "human";
};

/* general meter = AVG of the six segments (owner: "average of all segments"). */
setup.totalCorruption = function () {
    var sum = 0; setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { sum += setup.segTotal(s); });
    return Math.round(sum / setup.SEGMENTS.length);
};

/* worse of a paired limb (for autofail: arms drag your swing, legs your flee) */
setup.limbCorruption = function (which) {
    var segs = which === "arm" ? ["armL", "armR"] : ["legL", "legR"];
    return Math.max(setup.segTotal(segs[0]), setup.segTotal(segs[1]));
};
setup.limbPenalty = function (which) { return Math.floor(setup.limbCorruption(which) / 25); };

setup.fullyTransformed = function () {
    var form = State.variables.form || {};
    return setup.SEGMENTS.every(function (s) { return (form[s] || "human") !== "human"; });
};
/* the single class you've wholly become, or null if mixed / not fully turned */
setup.becameClass = function () {
    var form = State.variables.form || {}, first = form[setup.SEGMENTS[0]];
    if (!first || first === "human") { return null; }
    return setup.SEGMENTS.every(function (s) { return form[s] === first; }) ? first : null;
};

/* graded WHOLE-BODY class read — the missing primitive a partial/mixed body needs (becameClass is
   all-or-nothing). classLimbs(cls) = turned limbs of that class; classLoad(cls) = avg corruption of
   that class across the six segments (0..100). bodyClass() = the class you are MOSTLY becoming,
   { cls, load, limbs }, or null if nothing has a foothold (turned limbs win ties, then load). The
   rat-only ratLimbs/ratLoad below now delegate to these. */
setup.classLimbs = function (cls) {
    var f = State.variables.form || {}, n = 0;
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { if (f[s] === cls) { n++; } });
    return n;
};
setup.classLoad = function (cls) {
    var b = State.variables.body, sum = 0;
    if (!b) { return 0; }
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { sum += (b[s] && b[s][cls]) || 0; });
    return sum / setup.SEGMENTS.length;
};
setup.bodyClass = function () {
    var best = null;
    setup.CLASSES.forEach(function (c) {
        var cand = { cls: c, load: setup.classLoad(c), limbs: setup.classLimbs(c) };
        if (!best || cand.limbs > best.limbs || (cand.limbs === best.limbs && cand.load > best.load)) { best = cand; }
    });
    return (best && (best.load > 0 || best.limbs > 0)) ? best : null;
};

/* transformed-segment ability deltas (per turned limb, by class) — composes with
   MARK_MODS in playerScores. The body you grow fights like what it became. */
setup.FORM_MODS = {
    rat:   { dex: 1 },             /* quick, scurrying, low to the ground */
    pig:   { str: 1, con: 1 },     /* heavy, brutal, hard to put down */
    filth: { con: 1, cha: -1 }     /* tough as sludge, and it shows */
};

/* ---- what each segment LOOKS like as it changes (shown under its row in the
   StoryCaption body readout). The string DATA (setup.BODY_DESC — the full
   part × species × stage matrix) is defined in a raw-JS script block below
   StoryInit's run-block, NOT here — TwineScript desugaring in the run-block mangles
   operator-words ("and"→"&&", "to"→"=", "is"→"===") inside string literals.
   See the script block + HANDOFF §4. (Do not write literal macro tags in comments
   here — a stray one inside the script block breaks its closing-tag match.) ---- */
setup.PART_TYPE = { head: "head", torso: "torso", armL: "arm", armR: "arm", legL: "leg", legR: "leg" };
setup.segDesc = function (seg) {
    var stage = setup.segStage(seg);
    if (stage === "human") { return ""; }
    var form = State.variables.form || {};
    /* a TURNED limb is described by what it BECAME (form); earlier stages by the
       dominant exposure class so the change reads true to its source. */
    var c = (stage === "turned" && form[seg] && form[seg] !== "human")
        ? form[seg]
        : (setup.segClass(seg) || "filth");
    var part = setup.BODY_DESC[setup.PART_TYPE[seg]] || {};
    return ((part[c] || {})[stage]) || "";
};

/* apply corruption of a class to a segment; transform on fill; resync the mirror.
   Returns the segment's NEW stage key so a room can narrate the beat. */
/* apply corruption to ONE segment: fill it toward the 100 cap and return the change record
   plus any OVERFLOW that didn't fit (positive amount only overflows; a negative amount just
   eases and never spills). No proportional haircut — a full limb holds what it holds; the
   rest is handed back to the caller to spill onto a fresh target. */
setup._applyOne = function (seg, cls, amount) {
    var V = State.variables, b = V.body[seg];
    var preStage = setup.segStage(seg), preForm = (V.form[seg] || "human");
    var landed = amount, excess = 0;
    if (amount > 0) {
        var room = Math.max(0, 100 - setup.segTotal(seg));   /* a segment holds a total of 100 */
        landed = Math.min(amount, room);
        excess = amount - landed;                            /* the part that couldn't fit spills on */
    }
    b[cls] = Math.max(0, b[cls] + landed);
    if (preForm === "human" && setup.segTotal(seg) >= 100) {
        V.form[seg] = setup.segClass(seg) || "filth";        /* TRANSFORM: the limb is wholly turned */
    }
    return {
        excess: excess,
        change: { seg: seg, cls: cls, amt: landed, fromStage: preStage, toStage: setup.segStage(seg),
                  turned: (preForm === "human" && (V.form[seg] || "human") !== "human") }
    };
};
/* OVERFLOW TARGET (owner 2026-07-03): when a limb maxes out, the corruption reaches for a new
   one rather than being wasted. Prefers a limb ALREADY carrying this class (so a body turns
   coherently, class by class, toward a whole creature — the aggregate thesis) among those with
   room; else it breaks into fresh flesh at random. Returns null only when the body is wholly full. */
setup._spillTarget = function (fromSeg, cls) {
    var V = State.variables;
    var avail = setup.SEGMENTS.filter(function (s) { return s !== fromSeg && setup.segTotal(s) < 100; });
    if (!avail.length) { return null; }
    var withCls = avail.filter(function (s) { return (V.body[s][cls] || 0) > 0; });
    if (withCls.length) {
        withCls.sort(function (a, b) { return (V.body[b][cls] || 0) - (V.body[a][cls] || 0); });
        return withCls[0];                                   /* finish the limb furthest along in this class */
    }
    return avail.random();                                   /* the mutagen opens a new limb at random */
};
setup.corrupt = function (seg, cls, amount) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.body) { V.body = setup.freshBody(); }
    if (!V.form) { V.form = setup.freshForm(); }
    if (!setup.SEGMENTS.includes(seg)) { seg = "torso"; }
    if (!setup.CLASSES.includes(cls)) { cls = "filth"; }
    /* "transformations are always X type" curse: every taint becomes the cursed class,
       no matter its source (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §D). Resolved ONCE; the cascade carries it. */
    if (setup.hasCurse && setup.hasCurse("always_class")) {
        var forced = setup.curseParam("always_class", "class");
        if (forced && setup.CLASSES.includes(forced)) { cls = forced; }
    }
    var primarySeg = seg;
    setup.lastChangeSpills = [];                             /* reset per corrupt-event; drained by pushChange */
    var res = setup._applyOne(seg, cls, amount);
    /* transient hand-off to setup.pushChange (the <<corrupt>> widget); NOT serialized. Engine-internal
       callers (loseFight, casting, the Cutter, shifts) bypass the widget, so they set this but never
       feed it — they keep their own bespoke prose. lastChange is the PRIMARY beat (backward-compatible
       single record); lastChangeSpills carries any overflow hops for the feed to narrate too. */
    setup.lastChange = res.change;
    /* THE OVERFLOW CASCADE: excess spills to a fresh limb, and again, until it is absorbed or the
       whole body is turned. Each hop fills a segment to 100 (then it's excluded), so the loop
       terminates in at most SEGMENTS.length steps — no runaway. */
    var excess = res.excess, guard = 0;
    while (excess > 0 && guard < setup.SEGMENTS.length) {
        guard++;
        var tgt = setup._spillTarget(seg, cls);
        if (!tgt) { break; }                                /* nowhere left — the body is full; the rest is truly lost */
        var hop = setup._applyOne(tgt, cls, excess);
        setup.lastChangeSpills.push(hop.change);
        excess = hop.excess;
        seg = tgt;
    }
    setup.recomputeBody();
    return setup.segStage(primarySeg);
};

/* rest/wash: eases corruption on segments that haven't fully turned (turned limbs
   don't wash off), and resyncs the mirror. */
setup.soothe = function (amount) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.body) { V.body = setup.freshBody(); }
    /* "transformations irreversible" curse: corruption can only ratchet up — washing,
       resting, the Clean Pool all do nothing while it's worn (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §D). */
    if (setup.hasCurse && setup.hasCurse("irreversible")) { return; }
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) {
        if ((V.form[s] || "human") !== "human") { return; }
        var b = V.body[s], tot = b.rat + b.pig + b.filth;
        if (tot <= 0) { return; }
        var f = Math.max(0, tot - amount) / tot;                                  /* shrink proportionally by `amount` */
        b.rat *= f; b.pig *= f; b.filth *= f;
    });
    setup.recomputeBody();
};

/* keep the derived mirror + the player sheet in step after any body change */
setup.recomputeBody = function () {
    State.variables.corruption = setup.totalCorruption();
    setup.recomputePlayer();
};

/* self-heal/migration: builds the body if a save predates it, seeding each segment
   with any legacy general-corruption value (as filth) so the meter isn't wiped. */
setup.healBody = function () {
    var V = State.variables, legacy = (typeof V.corruption === "number") ? V.corruption : 0;
    V.body = setup.freshBody();
    V.form = setup.freshForm();
    if (legacy > 0) { setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { V.body[s].filth = legacy; }); }
    setup.recomputeBody();
};

/* ---- CREATURE-KIN (cross-life): fully becoming a creature leaves a lingering mark
   that makes that species read you as one of their own. ---- */
setup.isKin = function (cls) { return setup.hasMark("kin_" + cls); };

/* mark -> ability deltas (applied once per mark you carry; NOT always for the
   worse — this is the metaprogression). Keep keys ⊆ setup.STATS. */
setup.MARK_MODS = {
    damned:        { str: 1, con: 1, wis: -1 },   /* the deep hardens the body, dulls the soul */
    faceless:      { dex: 1, cha: -2 },           /* no face: unreadable, and uncharming */
    rendered:      { con: 2, dex: -1 },           /* flesh rendered to ward: tough, but stiff */
    indebted:      { int: 1, wis: 1, cha: -1 },   /* the Whisperer's knowledge, and its lien */
    sovereign:     { str: 1, cha: 2 },            /* you wore a crown down here, once */
    marked_escape: { wis: 1 },                    /* you came out changed, and warier */
    survivor:      { wis: 1 }                     /* you came out clean, and learned the place */
};

setup.playerScores = function () {
    var base = setup.baseScore(State.variables.level || 1);
    var s = { str: base, dex: base, con: base, int: base, wis: base, cha: base };
    /* character-creation spread: per-stat deltas from the default base, set ONCE and carried
       across lives (the "before"); folded into the level-scaling base so the spread grows too. */
    var build = recall("build", null);
    if (build) { setup.STATS.forEach(function (st) { if (build[st] != null) { s[st] += build[st]; } }); }
    var marks = recall("marks", {});
    Object.keys(setup.MARK_MODS).forEach(function (mk) {
        if (marks[mk]) {
            var delta = setup.MARK_MODS[mk];
            Object.keys(delta).forEach(function (st) { s[st] += delta[st]; });
        }
    });
    /* transformed body segments (this life): each turned limb fights like its class */
    var form = State.variables.form || {};
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (seg) {
        var cls = form[seg];
        if (cls && cls !== "human" && setup.FORM_MODS[cls]) {
            var fd = setup.FORM_MODS[cls];
            Object.keys(fd).forEach(function (st) { s[st] += fd[st]; });
        }
    });
    /* equipped gear: magic blessings (+) and curse stat-drains (−), via the pipeline */
    var im = (setup.itemMods ? setup.itemMods() : null);
    if (im) { setup.STATS.forEach(function (st) { s[st] += im.scores[st]; }); }
    /* in-life acquired stat deltas — voluntary/earned changes THIS life (the gutter bones,
       future ordeals); folded like marks but NOT persisted across deaths (reset by StoryInit). */
    var sm = State.variables.statMods;
    if (sm) { Object.keys(sm).forEach(function (st) { if (s[st] != null) { s[st] += sm[st]; } }); }
    setup.STATS.forEach(function (st) { if (s[st] < 1) { s[st] = 1; } });   /* floor at 1 */
    return s;
};

/* max HP = (level+3) "hit dice" of (5 + CON mod). L1 all-7s (con mod -2): 4*3 = 12
   — matches the old hand-tuned value, so existing balance is preserved. */
setup.playerMaxHp = function (scores) {
    var hpMod = (setup.itemMods ? setup.itemMods().hp : 0);   /* magic +health / curse −health */
    return Math.max(1, (State.variables.level + 3) * (5 + setup.mod(scores.con)) + hpMod);
};

/* player Armor Class: 10 + DEX mod + worn-armor ac + gear ac mods (magic/curse) */
setup.playerAC = function (scores) {
    var arm = State.variables.armor ? setup.items[State.variables.armor] : null;
    var acMod = (setup.itemMods ? setup.itemMods().ac : 0);
    return 10 + setup.mod(scores.dex) + (arm && arm.ac ? arm.ac : 0) + acMod;
};

/* corruption drags your aim: -1 to hit per full 25 corruption (0..-4) */
setup.corruptionPenalty = function () {
    return Math.floor(Math.clamp(State.variables.corruption, 0, 100) / 25);
};

/* whether the player's scores differ from the clean base (i.e. marks are at work) */
setup.marksAlterStats = function () {
    var marks = recall("marks", {});
    return Object.keys(setup.MARK_MODS).some(function (mk) { return marks[mk]; });
};

/* (re)compute and store the player's derived block. $level/$scores serialize.
   Call at StoryInit and on any level/mark/armor change. */
setup.recomputePlayer = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    V.scores = setup.playerScores();
    V.maxhp = setup.playerMaxHp(V.scores);
    if (V.hp == null || V.hp > V.maxhp) { V.hp = V.maxhp; }
    /* mana ceiling tracks level + corruption; guarded because setup.recomputeMana is defined in the
       <<script>> block, which runs AFTER this run-block's first StoryInit recompute. */
    if (setup.recomputeMana) { setup.recomputeMana(); }
};

/* ===================== EQUIPMENT & ITEM-MODIFIER PIPELINE =====================
   DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT.md §F infra — the one place that folds every equipped item's
   bonuses/penalties into the player block, combat, and the encounter roll, exactly
   the way MARK_MODS / FORM_MODS already fold into playerScores. Built so that once
   it exists, weapons/armor/accessories/curses/magic are all just DATA on items.
   These helpers are pure logic with single-word string ids only, so they are safe
   in this <<run>> block (no operator-word desugaring on displayed prose). They MUST
   be defined before setup.recomputeBody() runs at the end of this block. ========= */

setup.ACCESSORY_SLOTS = ["ring", "necklace", "boots", "gloves"];
/* GRAFT_SLOTS — the Cutter's body-mods (TheSurgery). In EQUIP_SLOTS so the modifier pipeline,
   equipped(), and the Equipment screen fold them in for free; NOT in ACCESSORY_SLOTS so acquire()
   never auto-equips one (they are installed only by setup.installGraft). */
setup.GRAFT_SLOTS = ["eye", "hand", "hide", "heart"];
setup.EQUIP_SLOTS = ["weapon", "armor", "ring", "necklace", "boots", "gloves", "eye", "hand", "hide", "heart"];

/* item ids currently equipped across every slot (skips empty / unknown) */
setup.equipped = function () {
    var V = State.variables, out = [];
    setup.EQUIP_SLOTS.forEach(function (slot) {
        var id = V[slot];
        if (id && setup.items[id]) { out.push(id); }
    });
    return out;
};

/* ---- CURSES (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §D) ---- */
/* an item's `curse` may be a string id, an object {id, stat?, class?, amount?}, or
   an array mixing both. Normalize to a list of objects. */
setup.itemCurses = function (item) {
    if (!item || !item.curse) { return []; }
    var c = Array.isArray(item.curse) ? item.curse : [item.curse];
    return c.map(function (e) { return (typeof e === "string") ? { id: e } : e; });
};
/* all active curse entries: equipped cursed gear + cross-life cursed-object marks.
   (The cross-life carrier — "cursed items persist as marks and resist removal" —
   reads marks of the form cursed_<curseId>; that DATA is added later, the hook is here.) */
setup.curseEntries = function () {
    var out = [];
    setup.equipped().forEach(function (id) { out = out.concat(setup.itemCurses(setup.items[id])); });
    out = out.concat(setup.scars());     /* permanent personal SCARS (the Fleshcutter's price) — cross-life, bodiless */
    return out;
};
/* ---- SCARS (the curse-cutter's price, owner 2026-06-07) — personal curses with no item behind
   them: permanent, carry between lives (pure accumulation), and fold into curseEntries() so every
   curse hook (capability flags, stat-drains, etc.) treats them like a worn curse. You cannot get
   clean of curses once you've worn cursed gear — only TRADE a known one for a scar. ---- */
setup.scars = function () { return recall("scars", []); };
setup.addScar = function (entry) { var s = recall("scars", []); s.push(entry); memorize("scars", s); };
setup.hasCurse = function (id) {
    return setup.curseEntries().some(function (e) { return e.id === id; });
};
setup.curseParam = function (id, key) {
    var hit = setup.curseEntries().filter(function (e) { return e.id === id; })[0];
    return hit ? hit[key] : null;
};

/* ---- CAPABILITY FLAGS — read by the Combat six-button row, pickup links, and
   future dialogue/CHA-bargain options. Each is true unless a curse forbids it. ---- */
setup.canAttack     = function () { return !setup.hasCurse("noattack"); };
setup.canRun        = function () { return !setup.hasCurse("norun"); };
setup.canSpeak      = function () { return !setup.hasCurse("nospeak"); };
setup.canPickup     = function () { return !setup.hasCurse("nopickup"); };
setup.autoSurrender = function () { return setup.hasCurse("autosurrender"); };

/* ---- THE MODIFIER BLOCK — gather every equipped item's PASSIVE bonus (magic,
   positive) and penalty (curse, negative) into one block. Per-creature DAMAGE
   bonuses are handled separately in combat (itemDamageBonus), not here. ----
   magic schema: { scope:"all"|"rat"|"pig"|"filth"|<enemyId>, bonus:<body>, amount:N }
     bonus body: "str".."cha" (one stat) | "all" (every stat) | "hp" | "ac" | "encounter" | "dmg"
   ("dmg" is the per-creature combat bonus → itemDamageBonus; scope gates it.) */
setup.itemMods = function () {
    var mods = { scores: {}, hp: 0, ac: 0, encounter: 0 };
    setup.STATS.forEach(function (s) { mods.scores[s] = 0; });
    /* magic blessings */
    setup.equipped().forEach(function (id) {
        var mg = setup.items[id] && setup.items[id].magic;
        if (!mg) { return; }
        var amt = mg.amount || 0, b = mg.bonus;
        if (b === "all") { setup.STATS.forEach(function (s) { mods.scores[s] += amt; }); }
        else if (b === "hp") { mods.hp += amt; }
        else if (b === "ac") { mods.ac += amt; }
        else if (b === "encounter") { mods.encounter -= amt; }      /* magic DECREASES encounters */
        else if (setup.STATS.indexOf(b) >= 0) { mods.scores[b] += amt; }
        /* b === "dmg" handled in combat (itemDamageBonus) */
    });
    /* curse penalties (stat drains + encounter increase; capability/corruption/economy
       curses act through flags + hooks, not this passive block) */
    setup.curseEntries().forEach(function (e) {
        if (e.id === "stat_down") { mods.scores[e.stat || "str"] -= (e.amount || 1); }
        else if (e.id === "stat_down_all") { var n = e.amount || 1; setup.STATS.forEach(function (s) { mods.scores[s] -= n; }); }
        else if (e.id === "encounter_up") { mods.encounter += (e.amount || 4); }
    });
    return mods;
};

/* per-creature MAGIC damage bonus on the current target. scope "all" → every foe
   (weaker); a specific class/enemy-id → only that foe (the owner's "much stronger").
   Applied in playerStrike / doSpecial after the type multiplier. */
setup.itemDamageBonus = function (enemy) {
    if (!enemy) { return 0; }
    var bonus = 0;
    setup.equipped().forEach(function (id) {
        var mg = setup.items[id] && setup.items[id].magic;
        if (mg && mg.bonus === "dmg") {
            var sc = mg.scope || "all";
            if (sc === "all" || sc === enemy.cls || sc === enemy.id) { bonus += (mg.amount || 0); }
        }
    });
    return bonus;
};

/* the live encounter rate after gear: base ENCOUNTER_RATE − magic + curse, floored at 0 */
setup.encounterRate = function () {
    return Math.max(0, setup.ENCOUNTER_RATE + setup.itemMods().encounter);
};

/* ---- ECONOMY: route coin gains so the "coins turn to other objects" (coinrot) curse can
   intercept them. Returns the amount actually KEPT (0 when coinrot curdles it to junk), so a
   payline can branch on the return and never claim coin a cursed hand didn't keep. Rooms that
   hand out coin MUST call this instead of $coins += n. Every faucet is now routed (owner
   2026-07-01): combat spoils + FINDS, the wheel (setup.spinWheel), the gutter bones
   (setup.castBones), and all the wage/find sites in the layer files. ---- */
/* ---- ACQUIRE: add an item to the pack + auto-equip into its slot, folding any
   gear mods into the player block. Blocked entirely by the "can't pick up" curse.
   Returns true if taken. The <<acquire>> widget is a thin wrapper over this. ---- */
setup.acquire = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables, it = setup.items[id];
    if (!it || !setup.canPickup()) { return false; }
    if (!V.inventory.includes(id)) { V.inventory.push(id); }
    if (it.kind === "weapon" && !V.weapon) { V.weapon = id; }
    else if (it.kind === "armor" && !V.armor) { V.armor = id; }
    else if (it.kind === "accessory" && it.slot && setup.ACCESSORY_SLOTS.indexOf(it.slot) >= 0 && !V[it.slot]) { V[it.slot] = id; }
    setup.recomputePlayer();
    return true;
};

setup.JUNK = ["junk_hair", "junk_cap", "junk_button"];
setup.gainCoins = function (n) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (n <= 0) { return 0; }
    if (setup.hasCurse("coinrot")) {
        var pick = setup.JUNK[Math.floor(Math.random() * setup.JUNK.length)];
        if (!V.inventory.includes(pick)) { V.inventory.push(pick); }
        return 0;                                  /* the coin curdled into rubbish in your hand */
    }
    V.coins += n;
    return n;
};

/* ===================== IDENTIFICATION / EQUIP / DROPS / SHOP =====================
   The DATA-phase systems on top of the §F pipeline (owner 2026-06-06). All pure logic, so safe in
   this <<run>> block. Forks settled by the owner: hidden-until-equipped; cursed gear is NON-removable
   (a future NPC may strip it — setup.uncurse is the stub) and carries cross-life; gear comes from
   shop + drops, magic stays rare; a drop whose apparent tier outranks the monster is likelier cursed. */

/* ---- IDENTIFICATION — an item with magic OR a curse hides what it does (shown only by its apparent
   tier) until you equip it (too late for a curse) or pay an appraiser. Plain gear reads true always. */
setup.hasHiddenProps = function (id) { var it = setup.items[id]; return !!(it && (it.magic || it.curse)); };
setup.isIdentified = function (id) {
    if (!setup.hasHiddenProps(id)) { return true; }
    return (State.variables.idKnown || []).includes(id);
};
setup.identify = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.idKnown) { V.idKnown = []; }
    if (!V.idKnown.includes(id)) { V.idKnown.push(id); }
};
/* the name to SHOW: true name once identified, else a masked apparent-tier descriptor */
setup.itemDisplayName = function (id) {
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it) { return "something"; }
    if (setup.isIdentified(id)) { return it.name; }
    var ap = setup.apparentTier(id);
    var kindWord = it.kind === "weapon" ? "weapon" : (it.kind === "armor" ? "armor" : (it.slot || "trinket"));
    return (ap ? (ap + "-looking " + kindWord) : ("a strange " + kindWord)) + " (unidentified)";
};

/* ---- EQUIP / UNEQUIP ---- */
setup.slotOf = function (id) {
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it) { return null; }
    if (it.kind === "weapon") { return "weapon"; }
    if (it.kind === "armor") { return "armor"; }   /* includes clothing (motley, overalls) — clothing IS armor, one body slot */
    if (it.kind === "accessory") { return it.slot || null; }
    return null;
};
/* is item `id` currently worn (equipped in its own slot)? — for clothing/gear effect gates */
setup.wearing = function (id) { var s = setup.slotOf(id); return !!(s && State.variables[s] === id); };
setup.isCursed = function (id) { return setup.itemCurses(setup.items[id]).length > 0; };
/* a GRAFT is flesh, not gear — once installed it is part of you and will not come off (the Cutter
   does not give refunds in skin). isBound = cursed OR grafted: both lock their slot. */
setup.isGraft = function (id) { var it = setup.items[id]; return !!(it && it.graft); };
setup.isBound = function (id) { return setup.isCursed(id) || setup.isGraft(id); };
/* a slot whose worn item is bound (cursed or grafted) is LOCKED — nothing can displace it */
setup.slotLocked = function (slot) { var cur = State.variables[slot]; return !!(cur && setup.isBound(cur)); };
setup.equip = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables, slot = setup.slotOf(id);
    if (!slot) { return { ok: false, reason: "noslot" }; }
    if (setup.slotLocked(slot)) { return { ok: false, reason: "locked" }; }
    if (!V.inventory.includes(id)) { V.inventory.push(id); }
    V[slot] = id;
    setup.identify(id);                       /* putting it on reveals it */
    setup.recomputePlayer();
    return { ok: true, cursed: setup.isCursed(id) };
};
setup.unequip = function (slot) {
    var V = State.variables, id = V[slot];
    if (!id) { return { ok: false, reason: "empty" }; }
    if (setup.isGraft(id)) { return { ok: false, reason: "graft" }; }   /* flesh; will not come off */
    if (setup.isCursed(id)) { return { ok: false, reason: "cursed" }; }
    V[slot] = null;
    setup.recomputePlayer();
    return { ok: true };
};
/* THE CUTTER (owner 2026-06-08): install a body-mod. Pays in CORRUPTION (the graft's graftSeg/graftAmt,
   class "pig" — you are made fitter for the belly by being made more of it), seats the part in its
   graft slot permanently, and recomputes. Returns the segment's new stage key for the room to narrate.
   Refuses (returns null) if that slot is already grafted. */
setup.installGraft = function (id, cls) {
    var V = State.variables, it = setup.items[id];
    if (!it || !it.graft) { return null; }
    var slot = it.slot;
    if (!slot || V[slot]) { return null; }                 /* one graft per slot, permanent */
    if (!V.inventory.includes(id)) { V.inventory.push(id); }
    V[slot] = id;
    setup.identify(id);
    var stage = setup.corrupt(it.graftSeg || "torso", cls || "pig", it.graftAmt || 12);   /* this also recomputes the body. cls defaults to "pig" (the Cutter); a non-pig installer (e.g. the L1 Pryer) passes its own band class, e.g. "rat" */
    setup.recomputePlayer();
    return stage;
};
/* grafts the Cutter can still offer (not yet installed) */
setup.graftsAvailable = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    return setup.GRAFT_SLOTS.filter(function (s) { return !V[s]; })
        .map(function (s) { return setup.GRAFT_FOR_SLOT[s]; })
        .filter(function (id) { return !!id; });
};
setup.GRAFT_FOR_SLOT = { eye: "graft_eye", hand: "graft_hand", hide: "graft_hide", heart: "graft_heart" };
/* plain-language effect of a graft, for the Cutter's menu (he shows you, so no identify gate) */
setup.graftBrief = function (id) {
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it || !it.magic) { return ""; }
    var b = it.magic.bonus, a = it.magic.amount;
    if (b === "encounter") { return "+" + a + " to passing unnoticed"; }
    if (b === "ac")        { return "+" + a + " AC"; }
    if (b === "hp")        { return "+" + a + " max vigor"; }
    if (setup.STATS.indexOf(b) >= 0) { return "+" + a + " " + b.toUpperCase(); }
    return "+" + a + " " + b;
};
/* inventory items that could go in this slot (excluding the one already worn there) */
setup.slotItems = function (slot) {
    var V = State.variables;
    return (V.inventory || []).filter(function (id) { return setup.slotOf(id) === slot && V[slot] !== id; });
};
/* the work-curse uniform (owner 2026-06-06): the indenture takes your clothes and puts you in
   rags — "your new work clothes". Better armour you've earned is left alone; only the default
   clothes are replaced, and only if a cursed item isn't already locked into the armour slot.
   Lives in this run-block (not the script-block) because the StoryInit init-call below uses it. */
setup.dressInWorkRags = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.inventory) { V.inventory = []; }
    if (!V.inventory.includes("rags")) { V.inventory.push("rags"); }
    var ci = V.inventory.indexOf("clothes"); if (ci >= 0) { V.inventory.splice(ci, 1); }
    if (!setup.slotLocked("armor") && (!V.armor || V.armor === "clothes" || V.armor === "rags")) {
        V.armor = "rags";
        setup.recomputePlayer();
    }
};
/* strip a cursed item AND clear its cross-life mark so it does not return. Used by the Fleshcutter
   (setup.cutCurse) — never call it bare in a room; cutting must leave a scar (below). */
setup.uncurse = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables, slot = setup.slotOf(id);
    if (slot && V[slot] === id) { V[slot] = null; }
    var ix = (V.inventory || []).indexOf(id);
    if (ix >= 0) { V.inventory.splice(ix, 1); }
    var m = recall("marks", {}); delete m["cursed_" + id]; memorize("marks", m);
    setup.recomputePlayer();
};
/* currently-worn cursed items (what the Fleshcutter can cut) */
setup.cursedEquipped = function () { return setup.equipped().filter(function (id) { return setup.isCursed(id); }); };
/* THE FLESHCUTTER (owner 2026-06-07): cut a cursed item free — but the cut leaves a lasting SCAR,
   permanent + cross-life: ALWAYS a stat-loss, and SOMETIMES a worse curse too (a bad cut / the deep's
   take). You trade a known curse for one you didn't choose; you never leave him clean. Returns the
   scar(s) inflicted, for the room to narrate. */
setup.UNCURSE_COST = 15;   /* the Fleshcutter's coin fee (the real price is the scar); tunable */
setup.SCAR_CURSES = ["norun", "nospeak", "encounter_up", "coinrot", "noattack"];   /* the "bad cut" pool */
setup.cutCurse = function (id) {
    var inflicted = [];
    setup.uncurse(id);                                   /* the cursed thing comes off (and won't return) */
    var stat = setup.STATS[Math.floor(Math.random() * setup.STATS.length)];
    var amt = 1 + (setup.d(100) <= 30 ? 1 : 0);          /* usually −1, sometimes −2 */
    var statScar = { id: "stat_down", stat: stat, amount: amt };
    setup.addScar(statScar); inflicted.push(statScar);
    if (setup.d(100) <= 40) {                            /* the cut goes wrong / the deep takes more */
        var c = setup.SCAR_CURSES[Math.floor(Math.random() * setup.SCAR_CURSES.length)];
        var extra = { id: c };
        setup.addScar(extra); inflicted.push(extra);
    }
    setup.recomputePlayer();
    return inflicted;
};

/* ---- CROSS-LIFE CURSE CARRY — a cursed item worn at a run's end banks a mark; next life it finds
   you again (re-equipped at StoryInit, pure accumulation). ---- */
setup.bankCursedGear = function () {
    setup.EQUIP_SLOTS.forEach(function (slot) {
        var id = State.variables[slot];
        if (id && setup.isCursed(id)) { setup.addMark("cursed_" + id); }
    });
};
setup.seedCursedGear = function () {
    var V = State.variables, marks = recall("marks", {});
    Object.keys(marks).forEach(function (mk) {
        if (mk.indexOf("cursed_") !== 0) { return; }
        var id = mk.slice(7);
        if (!setup.items[id]) { return; }
        var slot = setup.slotOf(id);
        if (slot && !V[slot]) {
            if (!V.inventory.includes(id)) { V.inventory.push(id); }
            V[slot] = id; setup.identify(id);     /* you know this one already, to your sorrow */
        }
    });
};

/* ---- DROPS (owner) — a victory sometimes leaves gear among the remains. The rolled APPARENT tier
   sometimes outranks the monster; the further it outranks, the likelier the find is CURSED (steel off
   a rat = a trap). Dropped magic/cursed gear is UNIDENTIFIED. ---- */
setup.DROP_CHANCE = 30;                      /* % of victories that drop anything (tunable) */
setup.monsterRank = function (statLevel) {
    if (statLevel <= 3) { return 1; }
    if (statLevel <= 6) { return 2; }
    if (statLevel <= 8) { return 4; }
    return 5;
};
setup.gearByPredicate = function (pred) {
    return Object.keys(setup.items).filter(function (id) {
        var it = setup.items[id];
        return (it.kind === "weapon" || it.kind === "armor" || it.kind === "accessory") && pred(id, it);
    });
};
setup.dropPoolMundane = function (rank) {
    return setup.gearByPredicate(function (id, it) { return !it.magic && !it.curse && setup.MATERIAL_RANK[it.tier] === rank; });
};
setup.dropPoolCursed = function (rank) {
    return setup.gearByPredicate(function (id, it) {
        if (!it.curse) { return false; }
        if (it.kind === "accessory") { return true; }           /* cursed trinkets can turn up at any rank */
        return setup.MATERIAL_RANK[setup.apparentTier(id)] === rank;
    });
};
setup.dropPoolMagic = function () {
    return setup.gearByPredicate(function (id, it) { return it.magic && !it.curse && (it.tier === "magic" || it.kind === "accessory"); });
};
setup.rollDrop = function (enemy) {
    if (!enemy || setup.d(100) > setup.DROP_CHANCE) { return null; }
    var mrank = setup.monsterRank(enemy.statLevel || 3), roll = setup.d(100), apRank;
    if (roll <= 55) { apRank = mrank; }                         /* honest find, the monster's own grade */
    else if (roll <= 80) { apRank = mrank + 1; }
    else if (roll <= 93) { apRank = mrank + 2; }
    else { apRank = mrank + 2 + setup.d(2); }                   /* the big, suspicious jump (can hit steel off a rat) */
    if (apRank > 5) { apRank = 5; }
    var gap = Math.max(0, apRank - mrank);
    var curseChance = [8, 30, 65, 90, 95][Math.min(gap, 4)];
    var pool;
    if (setup.d(100) <= curseChance) { pool = setup.dropPoolCursed(apRank); }
    else if (setup.d(100) <= 6) { pool = setup.dropPoolMagic(); }    /* a rare clean magic find */
    else { pool = setup.dropPoolMundane(apRank); }
    if (!pool || !pool.length) { pool = setup.dropPoolMundane(apRank); }
    if (!pool || !pool.length) { return null; }
    return pool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length)];
};
/* grant a dropped item to the pack (no auto-equip — choosing to wear it is the player's risk) */
setup.takeDrop = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (id && setup.items[id] && !V.inventory.includes(id)) { V.inventory.push(id); }
};
/* the toughest fallen enemy in the pack — what a victory's drop rolls against */
setup.dropSourceEnemy = function () {
    /* the biggest thing that actually FELL — a fled enemy (C2 morale) left with its pockets */
    var es = (State.variables.enemies || []).filter(function (e) { return !e.fled; }), best = null;
    es.forEach(function (e) { if (!best || (e.statLevel || 0) > (best.statLevel || 0)) { best = e; } });
    return best;
};

/* ---- SHOP — data-driven market stock (the smith + trinket stalls render these). coins only; some
   cursed bargains are suspiciously cheap (the trap, masked by hidden-until-equipped). Magic NOT sold. */
/* a curated spread across types + tiers (the rest of the catalog comes from drops). */
setup.MARKET_WEAPONS = [
    { id: "rusty_shiv", price: 4 },    { id: "rusty_cudgel", price: 4 },                          /* dagger / hammer */
    { id: "copper_spear", price: 9 },  { id: "copper_axe", price: 10 },  { id: "copper_mace", price: 9 },
    { id: "bronze_sword", price: 18 }, { id: "bronze_hook", price: 16 }, { id: "bronze_maul", price: 18 },
    { id: "iron_blade", price: 32 },   { id: "iron_spear", price: 30 },  { id: "iron_hammer", price: 32 },
    { id: "steel_blade", price: 55 },  { id: "steel_axe", price: 58 },   { id: "steel_maul", price: 55 },
    { id: "hungry_knife", price: 14 }                      /* the "steel" bargain that bites */
];
setup.MARKET_ARMOR = [
    { id: "rags", price: 2 }, { id: "clothes", price: 6 }, { id: "robes", price: 10 },
    { id: "copper_scale", price: 14 }, { id: "bronze_plate", price: 22 },
    { id: "iron_plate", price: 38 },   { id: "steel_plate", price: 62 },
    { id: "comely_coat", price: 16 }                       /* the handsome bargain */
];
setup.MARKET_TRINKETS = [
    { id: "quick_boots", price: 18 }, { id: "ward_necklace", price: 16 }, { id: "will_ring", price: 18 },
    { id: "grip_gloves", price: 18 }, { id: "dim_ring", price: 22 },      { id: "felted_boots", price: 22 },
    { id: "corded_teeth", price: 20 }, { id: "clear_lens", price: 18 }, { id: "glamour_charm", price: 16 },
    { id: "greed_ring", price: 8 },   { id: "lead_boots", price: 8 }      /* cheap cursed bargains */
];
setup.APPRAISE_COST = 6;
/* buy: deduct coin, add to pack. Convenience auto-equips PLAIN gear into an empty slot; anything with
   hidden props just goes to the pack so equipping it stays a deliberate (risky) choice. */
setup.buy = function (id, price) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (V.coins < price || !setup.items[id]) { return false; }
    if (V.inventory.includes(id)) { return false; }
    V.coins -= price;
    V.inventory.push(id);
    var slot = setup.slotOf(id);
    if (slot && !V[slot] && !setup.hasHiddenProps(id)) { V[slot] = id; setup.recomputePlayer(); }
    return true;
};
setup.appraise = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (V.coins < setup.APPRAISE_COST || setup.isIdentified(id)) { return false; }
    V.coins -= setup.APPRAISE_COST; setup.identify(id); return true;
};
/* unidentified items in the pack (what an appraiser can work on) */
setup.unidentifiedItems = function () {
    return (State.variables.inventory || []).filter(function (id) { return !setup.isIdentified(id); });
};
/* compact stat line for a gear item (Equipment screen + shop). Masked to "?" until identified.
   Operator-word-safe (no whole-word and/or/to/is/not) so it's fine in this run-block. */
setup.itemBrief = function (id) {
    var it = setup.items[id]; if (!it) { return ""; }
    if (!setup.isIdentified(id)) { return "?"; }
    var bits = [];
    if (it.kind === "weapon") { bits.push(setup.weaponDie(id) + " " + (it.type || setup.weaponDtype(id))); }
    if (it.kind === "armor")  { bits.push("+" + (it.ac || 0) + " AC"); }
    if (it.magic) {
        var mg = it.magic, b = mg.bonus, a = mg.amount;
        if (b === "encounter")  { bits.push("−" + a + " enc"); }
        else if (b === "dmg")   { bits.push("+" + a + " dmg vs " + mg.scope); }
        else if (b === "ac")    { bits.push("+" + a + " AC"); }
        else if (b === "hp")    { bits.push("+" + a + " HP"); }
        else if (b === "all")   { bits.push("+" + a + " all"); }
        else                    { bits.push("+" + a + " " + b); }
    }
    if (it.curse) {
        setup.itemCurses(it).forEach(function (e) { bits.push("✗ " + setup.curseTag(e)); });
    }
    return bits.join(", ");
};

/* build one enemy actor from its registry entry — flat stats from statLevel */
setup.combatActor = function (enemyId) {
    var e = setup.enemies[enemyId], m = setup.mod(e.statLevel);
    var hp = Math.max(1, e.hd * (5 + m));
    return {
        id: enemyId, name: e.name, statLevel: e.statLevel,
        hp: hp, maxhp: hp, ac: 10 + m, atkMod: m, dmgMod: m,
        weaponDie: e.weaponDie || "1d4", coins: e.coins, xp: setup.enemyXP(e),
        cls: e.class || "filth", weakTo: e.weakTo || null, resists: e.resists || null,
        weakTypes: e.weakTypes || null, resistTypes: e.resistTypes || null, stunned: false,
        idmg: e.idmg || 0, idmgFlavor: e.idmgFlavor || null,                     /* IDENTITY DAMAGE (R/smoke): corrupts the SELF on a landed hit, even a won fight */
        move: e.move || null, every: e.every || 3, rounds: 0, winding: false,   /* signature-move state (R12) */
        parleys: !!e.parleys,                                                   /* a mind an offer can reach (R16) */
        boss: !!e.boss, fled: false, moraleChecked: false,                      /* morale state (C2): one weigh per fight; fled pays nothing */
        img: e.img || enemyId
    };
};
/* start a fight against ONE enemy (string id) or MANY (array of ids) — multi-enemy
   combat (owner 2026-06-05). $enemies[] is the party; $target the aimed index. */
setup.startFight = function (spec, ret) {
    var V = State.variables, ids = Array.isArray(spec) ? spec : [spec];
    V.enemies = ids.map(function (id) { return setup.combatActor(id); });
    V.target = 0;
    V.specialUses = 0;                                  /* specials fired this fight; max = level */
    V.combatSpoils = { coins: 0, xp: 0 };               /* accrues as enemies fall */
    V.combatMenu = "main";
    V.combatReturn = ret;                               /* where VICTORY goes (often a "cleared" lander) */
    V.combatOrigin = State.passage;                     /* the room you fought in — where FLEE / LOSS return you */
    V.combatLog = "";
    V.held = 0;                                         /* a landed grapple/coil/drag: Run is spoken for one round */
    V.engulfed = false;                                 /* a landed engulf: your next action goes to getting out */
};

setup.aliveEnemies = function () {
    return (State.variables.enemies || []).filter(function (e) { return e.hp > 0; });
};
setup.firstAliveIndex = function () {
    var es = State.variables.enemies || [];
    for (var i = 0; i < es.length; i++) { if (es[i].hp > 0) { return i; } }
    return -1;
};
/* does the player have at least one limb fully TURNED to class c? (gates form-specials) */
setup.hasFormLimb = function (c) {
    var form = State.variables.form || {};
    return setup.SEGMENTS.some(function (s) { return form[s] === c; });
};
/* the specials the player can fire right now (base sweep always; form ones once grown) */
setup.availableSpecials = function () {
    var kind = setup.playerWeaponKind();
    return setup.SPECIALS.filter(function (sp) {
        var formOk = !sp.req || setup.hasFormLimb(sp.req);          /* grown-limb gate */
        var weapOk = !sp.wreq || (kind && sp.wreq.indexOf(kind) >= 0);  /* weapon-type gate */
        return formOk && weapOk;
    });
};
setup.specialMax = function () { return State.variables.level || 1; };        /* N per combat = level */
setup.specialsLeft = function () { return setup.specialMax() - (State.variables.specialUses || 0); };
setup.playerWeaponDie = function () { var w = State.variables.weapon; return w ? setup.weaponDie(w) : "1d2"; };
setup.playerWeaponType = function () { var w = State.variables.weapon; return w ? setup.weaponDtype(w) : "blunt"; };   /* dtype: blunt/edged */
setup.playerWeaponKind = function () { var w = State.variables.weapon; return w ? setup.weaponKind(w) : null; };       /* fine type: dagger/hook/… (null = fists) */
/* consumables currently in the pack — what the combat Items menu can use */
setup.usableItems = function () {
    return (State.variables.inventory || []).filter(function (id) {
        return setup.items[id] && setup.items[id].kind === "consumable";
    });
};
/* flee: d20 + DEX mod − leg-corruption ≥ 10 */
setup.fleeRoll = function () {
    var V = State.variables, legPen = Math.max(setup.corruptionPenalty(), setup.limbPenalty("leg"));
    return (setup.d(20) + setup.mod(V.scores.dex) - legPen) >= 10;
};
/* round outcome: "victory" (all down) / "loss" (you're down) / "" */
setup.combatOutcome = function () {
    if (State.variables.hp <= 0) { return "loss"; }
    if (setup.aliveEnemies().length === 0) { return "victory"; }
    return "";
};

/* ---- RANDOM ENCOUNTERS (owner 2026-06-05) — logic here, displayed strings in <<script>> ----
   ~ENCOUNTER_RATE% per real room move (PassageHeader) the local denizens accost you and try to
   send you to work. Extensible pool; the press-gang ("backtowork") is entry #1. */
setup.ENCOUNTER_RATE = 4;                                 /* % per move (owner: 3–5); tunable */
/* weight may be a number OR a function (evaluated each roll) so an encounter's frequency can
   depend on live state. pigpress (owner 2026-06-17): the pig sty-hand recruiter is the MAIN
   encounter when the pig cage is YOUR post (workStation "cage"), and only a RARE cross-poach
   toward pig work when you're bound elsewhere / not yet claimed. */
setup.ENCOUNTERS = [
    { id: "backtowork", weight: 5 },                                                         /* the floor's own denizens */
    { id: "pigpress",   weight: function () { return State.variables.workStation === "cage" ? 12 : 1; } },
    /* THE VAT PRESS-GANG (owner 2026-06-18): the kappa parallel of pigpress. The kappa tend the
       rendering vats the way they tend a bathhouse tub — same instinct, get the guest into the
       water — so a vat-tender kappa is the recruiter for the VATS post. MAIN encounter (12) when
       the vats are YOUR post (workStation "vats"), a rare cross-poach (1) otherwise. */
    { id: "vatpress",   weight: function () { return State.variables.workStation === "vats" ? 12 : 1; } },
    /* POSITIVE events (owner 2026-06-17). goodfind: a coin/item/cleanse waiting in a REAL room on
       this floor — weight scales with how many finds are still untaken here (0 = can't fire), so
       a picked-clean floor stops offering them. kinhelp: a creature of a class you've fully turned
       does you a kindness — only when you carry that kin mark AND it dens this band; kept rare. */
    { id: "goodfind",   weight: function () { return Math.min(10, 3 * setup.eligibleFinds().length); } },
    { id: "kinhelp",    weight: function () { return setup.kinReady() ? 3 : 0; } },
    /* ratcraving (owner 2026-06-18; folded into the vice ledger 2026-07-20): once you've tasted
       the cheese the craving finds you out in the sewer band (the rat in you wants more) — weight
       CLIMBS as you ratten, so the hungrier you get the more it rules you, and past mostly-rat it
       COMPELS (the branch auto-eats, no resist). Sewer-only (rat is the sewer's class; the
       scavenging fits there). Now gated on setup.craving()==="cheese" — the ARBITRATION: if you
       have fed sewer-brew over the top, brew rules and this call goes quiet (brewwithdrawal takes
       its place). Only ever the loudest vice nags. */
    { id: "ratcraving", weight: function () {
        var d = setup.depthOf[State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
        return (setup.craving() === "cheese" && d <= 3) ? Math.min(14, 3 + 3 * setup.ratLimbs()) : 0;
    } },
    /* midgossip (owner 2026-06-18): on the MIDWAY (L6 Shambles) you can overhear two demons
       gossiping — and what they let slip is WHERE the deep hid a primer: the printed roll in the
       sewer privy (TheStallRow). Tips off the grimoire learn-source ($heardOfGrimoire), the parallel
       to the Arrivals tip-off for the arch. Fires only on L6, only while it'd still teach you
       something (not yet tipped, don't already know the Word). A pure eavesdrop — no fight. */
    { id: "midgossip", weight: function () {
        var V = State.variables, d = setup.depthOf[V.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
        return (d === 6 && !V.heardOfGrimoire && !V.magicKnown) ? 4 : 0;
    } },
    /* THE SHORT-WEIGHT MEN (owner 2026-07-03): the deep's opportunists who read your DUMP stat and
       test it (the third ledger — see setup.SHORTWEIGHT). Weight scales with statSpread(): a flat
       "seven all round" build (spread 0) is grey and never hunted; a min-maxer paints a target.
       Any real room (depth ≥ 1); the short-weights keep score on every floor. */
    { id: "shortweight", weight: function () {
        var d = setup.depthOf[State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
        return (d >= 1) ? Math.min(8, Math.max(0, setup.statSpread() - 3)) : 0;
    } },
    /* BREW-WITHDRAWAL (owner 2026-07-20): the dry shakes of the sewer-brew habit. Unlike the
       cheese — a scavenger's craving that forages and feeds ITSELF in the sewer — the still is a
       place you cannot carry, so brew's call follows you ANYWHERE as a withdrawal, not a forage.
       Fires only while brew is the DOMINANT vice past its nag floor (setup.craving), i.e. the
       other half of the arbitration: feed brew over the cheese and this replaces the ratcraving
       as the call you feel. Weight climbs with how hooked you are. */
    { id: "brewwithdrawal", weight: function () {
        return (setup.craving() === "brew") ? Math.min(10, 3 + Math.floor(setup.addictionLevel("brew") / 8)) : 0;
    } },
    /* SLOP-CRAVING (owner 2026-07-20): the pig-slop habit come looking. Like the cheese it FORAGES —
       there is always a trough, a spill of muck, a farrow's leavings in the pig band (hell proper,
       d≥5) — and past mostly-pig it COMPELS (auto-eats, the way the farrow do). Fires only while slop
       is the DOMINANT vice past its nag floor (setup.craving); weight climbs with how far gone you are.
       The pens-only CAPTURE (setup.pennedFatten) lives in TheHolding, NOT here — out in the band there
       is no boar to pen you, only the trough. */
    { id: "slopcraving", weight: function () {
        var d = setup.depthOf[State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
        return (setup.craving() === "slop" && d >= 5) ? Math.min(14, 3 + 3 * setup.pigLimbs()) : 0;
    } },
    /* SMOKE-CRAVING (owner 2026-07-20; Phase 0 of the smoke class). The glow come looking. Unlike the
       cheese/slop (which forage a solid FOOD in their band) the glow is the AIR — so it can find you
       ANYWHERE there's a haze to draw, which down here is everywhere (miasma is everywhere; d≥1). Below
       the compel floor you seek out a wisp and choose to draw; at/above (setup.smokeCompelled) the lungs
       draw on their own. Fires only while smoke is the DOMINANT vice past its nag floor (setup.craving) —
       the arbitration again: feed the glow over the other vices and this is the call you feel. Weight
       climbs with how deep in it you are. */
    { id: "smokecraving", weight: function () {
        var d = setup.depthOf[State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
        return (setup.craving() === "smoke" && d >= 1) ? Math.min(12, 3 + Math.floor(setup.addictionLevel("smoke") / 6)) : 0;
    } }
];
setup.encWeight = function (e) { return (typeof e.weight === "function") ? e.weight() : e.weight; };
setup.pickEncounter = function () {
    var pool = setup.ENCOUNTERS, total = 0, i, w;
    for (i = 0; i < pool.length; i++) { total += setup.encWeight(pool[i]); }
    var r = Math.floor(Math.random() * total);
    for (i = 0; i < pool.length; i++) { w = setup.encWeight(pool[i]); if (r < w) { return pool[i].id; } r -= w; }
    return pool[0].id;
};
/* should a move roll an encounter? only in real rooms (depthOf ≥ 1), and not when arriving
   back from an encounter/combat (so you don't chain straight into another). */
setup.encounterEligible = function () {
    var p = State.passage, prev = (State.passages && State.passages.length > 1) ? State.passages[State.passages.length - 2] : "";
    if (!(setup.depthOf[p] >= 1)) { return false; }
    if (["RandomEncounter", "Combat", "CombatVictory", "CombatLost", "CombatYielded", "ShortWeightDone", "TheHoldingKept", "TheGutteringCleared"].indexOf(prev) !== -1) { return false; }
    return true;
};
/* the local denizens of the floor you were ENTERING (encounterReturn), as a small press-gang
   (1–2; tougher floors send 1). Uses encounterReturn because State.passage is RandomEncounter. */
setup.denizenPack = function () {
    var room = State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage;
    var d = setup.depthOf[room] || 1, id, n;
    if (d <= 3)       { id = "ratman";   n = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2); }
    else if (d === 4) { id = "drowned";  n = 1; }
    else if (d <= 6)  { id = "ratman";   n = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2); }
    else if (d === 7) { id = "pigdemon"; n = 1; }
    else if (d === 8) { id = "gorger";   n = 1; }
    else              { id = "pigdemon"; n = 1; }
    var pack = []; for (var k = 0; k < n; k++) { pack.push(id); }
    /* MIXED presses (review R15) — the hinge floors sometimes send mismatched pairs, so the
       mutagenic thesis (a mixed pack marks you MIXED on a loss) can actually fire in play. */
    if (n > 1 && d <= 3 && Math.random() < 0.5)  { pack[1] = "rat"; }         /* the den's small kin tag along */
    if (d === 4 && Math.random() < 0.35) { pack.push("ratman"); }             /* a rat-thing strayed down the hinge */
    if (d === 7 && Math.random() < 0.25) { pack.push("grafted"); }            /* the belly lends the boar a made thing */
    return pack;
};

/* LOSING a fight no longer kills you (owner): the things that beat you down work their
   own nature into your wounds — SITUATIONAL partial transformation. Two mauled segments
   are marked by the CLASSES OF THE ENEMIES PRESENT (mixed packs mark you mixed), each by
   that enemy's statLevel; you come to at half vigor. A loss that completes a full-body
   transformation tips you into EndingBecome via the usual check. Returns info for prose. */
setup.loseFight = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    var es = (V.enemies && V.enemies.length) ? V.enemies : [];
    var clsPool = es.length ? es.map(function (e) { return e.cls || "filth"; }) : ["filth"];
    /* they rob you while you're down — SOME of your coins, if you have any (owner) */
    var coinsLost = 0;
    if (V.coins > 0) {
        coinsLost = Math.min(V.coins, 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.ceil(V.coins / 2)));
        V.coins -= coinsLost;
    }
    /* and work their nature into you — UP TO 5 corruption on ONE OR MORE limbs (owner),
       of the class of what beat you (mixed packs mark you mixed). Lighter than the old
       statLevel maul: losing costs you, but it doesn't instantly turn you. */
    var nLimbs = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);              /* 1..3 limbs */
    var pool = setup.SEGMENTS.slice(), picks = [], marks = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < nLimbs && pool.length; i++) {
        picks.push(pool.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length), 1)[0]);
    }
    picks.forEach(function (s, k) {
        var cls = clsPool[k % clsPool.length];
        var amt = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);             /* up to 5 */
        setup.corrupt(s, cls, amt);                              /* corrupt() resyncs mirror + sheet */
        marks.push({ seg: s, cls: cls, amt: amt });
    });
    V.hp = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(V.maxhp / 2));                  /* you come to, mauled but alive */
    /* FORCED CHEESE (owner 2026-06-25): if a RAT-thing put you down, the rats cram the larder's cheese
       past your teeth while you're under — so the addiction can be HOOKED involuntarily, even while
       you're too FRESH to ever willingly eat it (the willing larder eat is gated by inuredEnough()).
       That is the agency-loss path onto the rat track: you can be addicted to a thing you never chose
       to taste. Arms $cheeseTasted (the craving will find you in the sewer); the beat fires once, the
       moment it first takes. */
    var forceFed = false;
    if (clsPool.indexOf("rat") >= 0 && !V.cheeseTasted) { V.cheeseTasted = true; setup.feedAddiction("cheese", setup.ADDICTIONS.cheese.nag); forceFed = true; }
    /* the distinct classes that actually LANDED (review R15) — CombatLost branches mixed on this */
    var clsSeen = [];
    marks.forEach(function (m) { if (clsSeen.indexOf(m.cls) < 0) { clsSeen.push(m.cls); } });
    return { cls: clsPool[0], clsSet: clsSeen, segs: picks, marks: marks, coinsLost: coinsLost, forceFedCheese: forceFed, name: es.length ? es[0].name : "the dark" };
};

/* ---- MID-FIGHT PARLEY (review R16) — the middle path between fighting on and Surrender's
   everything (robbed AND corrupted AND marched). Pure logic here; the yield submenu + prose
   live in the Combat passage / CombatYielded. packListens: does anything still standing have
   a mind an offer can reach (actor.parleys)? yieldPurse: the same robbery formula a loss uses
   (loseFight), but VOLUNTARY — they take what they take, you walk out unmauled. */
setup.packListens = function () {
    return setup.aliveEnemies().some(function (e) { return !!e.parleys; });
};
setup.yieldPurse = function () {
    var V = State.variables, took = 0;
    if (V.coins > 0) {
        took = Math.min(V.coins, 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.ceil(V.coins / 2)));
        V.coins -= took;
    }
    return took;
};

/* damage-type effectiveness (owner): the player's weapon-damage multiplier vs this enemy.
   Merges the BROAD blunt|edged class (wtype vs enemy.weakTo/resists) with the FINE weapon-TYPE
   affinity (wkind vs enemy.weakTypes/resistTypes — affinities live on the enemy sheet). A net
   weakness → ×1.5, a net resistance → ×0.5, else ×1. (e.g. golem: weak blunt/hammer, resist
   edged; drowned: weak spear, resist hammer.) Unarmed = blunt, no fine type. */
setup.typeMult = function (wtype, enemy, wkind) {
    if (!enemy) { return 1; }
    var weak = (enemy.weakTo && wtype === enemy.weakTo) ||
               (wkind && enemy.weakTypes && enemy.weakTypes.indexOf(wkind) >= 0);
    var resist = (enemy.resists && wtype === enemy.resists) ||
                 (wkind && enemy.resistTypes && enemy.resistTypes.indexOf(wkind) >= 0);
    if (weak && !resist) { return 1.5; }
    if (resist && !weak) { return 0.5; }
    return 1;
};

/* one attack. d20 + atkMod (+prof) vs AC; nat 20 crits (double weapon dice) and
   always hits, nat 1 always misses. Returns {roll, hit, crit, fumble, dmg}. */
setup.attack = function (atkMod, prof, targetAC, weaponDie, dmgMod) {
    var roll = setup.d(20);
    var crit = (roll === 20), fumble = (roll === 1);
    var hit = !fumble && (crit || (roll + atkMod + prof >= targetAC));
    var dmg = 0;
    if (hit) {
        dmg = Math.max(1, setup.rollDie(weaponDie) + (crit ? setup.rollDie(weaponDie) : 0) + dmgMod);
    }
    return { roll: roll, hit: hit, crit: crit, fumble: fumble, dmg: dmg };
};

/* State-driven music chooser (unchanged; runs silent until audio is cached) */
setup.playNext = function () {
    var c = State.variables.corruption;
    var pool = [];
    pool.push("base", "base");
    if (State.variables.metTheWhisperer) { pool.push("whisper"); }
    if (State.variables.metTallow)       { pool.push("tallow"); }
    if (State.variables.metUnderstudy)   { pool.push("wearer"); }
    if (c >= 35) { for (var i = 0; i < Math.floor(c / 20); i++) { pool.push("corrupt1"); } }
    if (c >= 70) { pool.push("corrupt2", "corrupt2", "corrupt2"); }
    var candidates = pool.filter(function (t) { return t !== setup.lastTrack; });
    var pick = (candidates.length ? candidates : pool).random();
    if (!pick) { return; }
    setup.lastTrack = pick;
    if (!SimpleAudio.tracks.has(pick)) { return; }
    var track = SimpleAudio.tracks.get(pick);
    if (!track) { return; }
    setup.current = track;
    track.one("ended", setup.playNext);
    track.play();
};

/* ===================== THE WHEEL (carnival gambling, L6) =====================
   A repeatable bet. Two modes: "coin" (stake coins, deducted by the caller) and
   "trouble" (a self-bet — no coins, bigger swings, the curse/transformation risk).
   Mechanics + RNG live here; TheWheel passage just narrates the returned kind.
   See docs/TRANSFORMATION.md (kin/curse) and the room for the prose. =========== */
setup.weightedPick = function (list) {
    var total = 0, i;
    for (i = 0; i < list.length; i++) { total += list[i].w; }
    var r = Math.random() * total;
    for (i = 0; i < list.length; i++) { r -= list[i].w; if (r < 0) { return list[i]; } }
    return list[list.length - 1];
};
setup.WHEEL_STAKE = 4;                          /* coins per coin-mode spin */
setup.WHEEL_JACKPOT = { coin: 40, trouble: 60 };
setup.WHEEL = {
    /* coin mode: slim house edge, rare jackpot, a 3% curse. push = lose your bet;
       lose = lose your bet AND a little transformation (owner). */
    coin: [
        { w: 3,  kind: "jackpot" },
        { w: 12, kind: "win" },     /* stake x3 (net +2 stakes) */
        { w: 50, kind: "push" },    /* lose your bet, nothing else */
        { w: 32, kind: "lose" },    /* lose your bet + a little transformation */
        { w: 3,  kind: "curse" }    /* the mouth */
    ],
    /* "asking for trouble": bet yourself. No coin push — you don't get off clean.
       lose = a little transformation; transform = a deep bite. */
    trouble: [
        { w: 10, kind: "jackpot" },
        { w: 15, kind: "win" },      /* a coin consolation */
        { w: 35, kind: "lose" },     /* a little transformation */
        { w: 20, kind: "transform" },/* a deep bite of pig corruption */
        { w: 20, kind: "curse" }
    ]
};
/* spin; applies the effect (coins/corruption/curse) and returns a result for prose.
   coin mode assumes the caller already deducted setup.WHEEL_STAKE (so push/lose/etc.
   simply forfeit it). "lose" costs a little transformation; "transform" a deep one. */
setup.spinWheel = function (mode) {
    var V = State.variables, out = setup.weightedPick(setup.WHEEL[mode]);
    setup.passTime(setup.GAMBLE_TIME);   /* C1: a spin takes an evening's slice — the wheel is no longer clock-free */
    var res = { kind: out.kind, coins: 0, corrupt: 0, cursed: false, alreadyCursed: !!V.mouthCursed };
    switch (out.kind) {
        case "jackpot":   res.coins = setup.WHEEL_JACKPOT[mode]; break;
        case "win":       res.coins = (mode === "coin") ? setup.WHEEL_STAKE * 3 : 15; break;
        case "push":      break;                       /* coin stake already forfeit */
        case "lose":      res.corrupt = random(4, 9); break;   /* a little transformation */
        case "transform": res.corrupt = random(18, 32); break; /* a deep bite */
        case "curse":     res.cursed = true; break;
    }
    if (res.coins)   { res.got = setup.gainCoins(res.coins); }   /* routed so coinrot can curdle a win (res.got = kept; res.coins = rolled) */
    if (res.corrupt) { setup.corrupt(setup.SEGMENTS.random(), "pig", res.corrupt); }
    if (res.cursed)  { V.mouthCursed = true; }
    return res;
};

/* ---- THE GUTTER BONES (L6 carnival INT-gamble; owner spec 2026-06-27). A d12 of arcane
   bones thrown in the gutter; the PUBLISHED table IS the rig — the −1 band (faces 2–5) is
   wider than the +1 band (9–11), so EV ≈ −1/12 INT per throw, and the lone coin face (8) is
   the deliberate counterweight: it pays BONES_PRICE, which makes the bones price a point of
   wit at exactly BONES_PRICE coins (≈0.83 coin/throw ÷ ≈0.083 INT/throw). FREE to throw —
   coins only come OUT, never in; your mind is the only stake. INT moves through $statMods
   (in-life, reset each death) and recomputePlayer() folds it into $scores at once, so the
   side-panel readout drops in real time. You can ride it down to INT 1 and LIVE; the gutter only
   KEEPS you when, already below WITLESS_INT, the ruin (face 1) comes up for wits you can't pay
   (EndingWitless — an EVENT, not a floor). A sharp enough head reads the rig before it throws
   (the appraise statCheck in TheGutterBones — INT's first real non-combat consumer). ---- */
setup.BONES_PRICE = 10;     /* coins the lone coin-face (8) pays — the posted price of a wit */
setup.WITLESS_INT = 3;      /* BELOW this (INT 1–2) the bones can keep you — but only on the ruin (face 1); landing low is otherwise survivable (roam witless / climb back) */
setup.BONES_TABLE = [       /* face 1..12 -> effect; this IS the published board, and by design the rig */
    { dint: -3 },                       /* 1  — the bones take three */
    { dint: -1 }, { dint: -1 }, { dint: -1 }, { dint: -1 },  /* 2–5 — they take one */
    { dint: 0 }, { dint: 0 },           /* 6–7 — they let you be */
    { coins: setup.BONES_PRICE },       /* 8  — ten coins, and a smile */
    { dint: 1 }, { dint: 1 }, { dint: 1 },  /* 9–11 — they give one back */
    { dint: 3 }                         /* 12 — they give three */
];
setup.castBones = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    var intBefore = (V.scores && V.scores.int != null) ? V.scores.int : 7;   /* the wits you walked up with */
    var face = setup.d(12), row = setup.BONES_TABLE[face - 1];
    var dint = row.dint || 0, coins = row.coins || 0;
    if (dint) {
        if (!V.statMods) { V.statMods = {}; }
        V.statMods.int = (V.statMods.int || 0) + dint;
        setup.recomputePlayer();          /* fold $statMods into $scores immediately (panel updates) */
    }
    var gotCoins = coins ? setup.gainCoins(coins) : 0;   /* routed so coinrot can curdle the coin face (got = kept; coins = rolled) */
    V.bonesThrown = (V.bonesThrown || 0) + 1;
    setup.passTime(setup.GAMBLE_TIME);   /* C1: each throw takes time the gutter keeps */
    var nowInt = (V.scores && V.scores.int != null) ? V.scores.int : 7;
    /* The witless END is an EVENT now, not a threshold-crossing: you can ride the bones all the way
       down to INT 1 and LIVE (this is what makes the "simple" tier reachable — walk away, roam
       witless, even climb back up). The gutter only KEEPS you when, already at the floor
       (intBefore < WITLESS_INT, i.e. INT 1–2), the RUIN comes up — face 1, "the bones take three" —
       three wits you no longer have, so they take the rest of you instead. ~1/12 per throw down there. */
    var witless = (intBefore < setup.WITLESS_INT) && (face === 1);
    return { face: face, dint: dint, coins: coins, got: gotCoins, int: nowInt, witless: witless };
};

/* ---- the MOUTH-MISSPEAK curse ("asking for trouble"): when $mouthCursed, ~5% of
   choice-clicks come out as a DIFFERENT choice on the passage — your own mouth saying
   the wrong thing. A single document capture-listener (registered once; survives
   Engine.restart) reads the live flag and redirects the click. Composes everywhere,
   combat included (you go to flee and your hand swings instead). ---- */
setup.MISSPEAK_CHANCE = 0.05;
if (!setup._misspeakWired && typeof document !== "undefined") {
    setup._misspeakWired = true;
    document.addEventListener("click", function (ev) {
        var V = State.variables;
        if (!V || !V.mouthCursed) { return; }
        var a = (ev.target && ev.target.closest) ? ev.target.closest("a.link-internal") : null;
        if (!a) { return; }
        var box = a.closest(".passage"); if (!box) { return; }
        if (a.dataset.misspoke) { delete a.dataset.misspoke; return; }   /* a redirected click — let it pass */
        if (Math.random() >= setup.MISSPEAK_CHANCE) { return; }
        var links = Array.prototype.slice.call(box.querySelectorAll("a.link-internal"))
            .filter(function (x) { return x !== a; });
        if (!links.length) { return; }
        ev.preventDefault(); ev.stopImmediatePropagation();
        var other = links[Math.floor(Math.random() * links.length)];
        other.dataset.misspoke = "1";
        other.click();
    }, true);
}

/* initialize the body now that the segment helpers exist (StoryInit's data section
   ran before this block, so it left $body/$form null for us to build here) */
if (!State.variables.body) { State.variables.body = setup.freshBody(); }
if (!State.variables.form) { State.variables.form = setup.freshForm(); }

/* a cursed item from a past life re-grips before the first recompute folds it in */
setup.seedCursedGear();
/* a returner seeded pre-indentured (work_* mark) starts in their work rags, not the clothes
   the data section just gave — the uniform follows you across lives too (owner 2026-06-06) */
if (State.variables.workCursed) { setup.dressInWorkRags(); }

/* derive the player's combat block now that level + recalled marks + body + gear are set */
setup.recomputeBody();
>>

/* Body-segment appearance text in a RAW-JS script block: TwineScript desugaring in the
   run-block / set-macro mangles operator-words ("and"→"&&", "to"→"=", "is"→"===") inside
   string literals, so any DISPLAYED prose held in setup.* must live here, not in the run-block.
   (Never write a literal macro tag inside this block — even in a comment — it miscounts the
   closing tag and StoryInit fails with "cannot find a closing tag for macro".) */
<<script>>
/* ---- BODY_DESC — the full part × species × stage appearance matrix (DIRECTION §B,
   greenlit by the owner: "vary by species"). 4 part-types × 3 species × 4 stages = 48
   strings, shown as the .bm-desc sub-line under each segment in the StoryCaption body
   readout. Stage logic: TINGLE = a sensation, felt not seen; TAINTED = the first visible
   sign of the change; TURNING = the change well underway; TURNED = the finished anatomy.
   FIRST DRAFT (the builder's serviceable body-horror) — flagged for the owner's voice-pass;
   the systems are solid, this is prose. Keep each line one clause, matched in register. ---- */
setup.BODY_DESC = {
    head: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "an itch deep in the jaw and a twitch at the cheek, the teeth aching to gnaw",
                 tainted: "the face narrowing, whiskers pricking from the lip, the front teeth crowding forward",
                 turning: "the jaw drawn out and whiskered, the ears risen raw, the eyes gone small and side-set",
                 turned:  "pushed out into a long whiskered muzzle, ears risen raw, teeth gone to chisels" },
        pig:   { tingle:  "a heavy dull pressure behind the face, the nose stuffed and broadening, a want to root",
                 tainted: "the nose flattening and tipping up, the jaw thickening, bristle coming in at the jowl",
                 turning: "the face shoved forward to a blunt snout, small-eyed, the jaw heavying toward tusk",
                 turned:  "a hog's head now, snouted and small-eyed, the jaw heavy with tusk" },
        filth: { tingle:  "a numb softening across the face, the features feeling vague, hard to keep arranged",
                 tainted: "the features slackening and running, the skin going grey and wet at the edges",
                 turning: "the face mostly smoothed away, a wet grey mass with the suggestion of where eyes were",
                 turned:  "a smooth, near-eyeless lump of packed filth — a face only by where one would be" }
    },
    torso: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "a hollow gnawing in the belly that food won't touch, the ribs feeling light and quick",
                 tainted: "the chest narrowing, grey fur pricking along the breastbone, the ribs sharpening",
                 turning: "the trunk drawn to a narrow barrel under coarse grey fur, a vermin's restless ribcage",
                 turned:  "a quick narrow barrel under grey fur, a vermin's hungry ribcage" },
        pig:   { tingle:  "a deep warm heaviness settling in the gut, a slow swelling want to be still and fed",
                 tainted: "the trunk thickening and lowering, the skin coarsening pink, cold fat laid on under it",
                 turning: "the body slung heavy and broad, pink and bristled, the spine dropping toward all fours",
                 turned:  "a sow's heavy trunk, pink and bristled and slung with cold fat" },
        filth: { tingle:  "a soft crawling looseness in the core, as if the middle of you were no longer packed",
                 tainted: "the trunk softening out of true, the surface weeping a thin grey grease, held by habit",
                 turning: "the body a sagging grey aggregate in a person's outline, sloughing slowly where it sits",
                 turned:  "a sodden heap held in a person's outline by habit, sloughing where it sits" }
    },
    arm: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "a restless prickle down the forearm, the fingers wanting to scrabble and dig",
                 tainted: "fur coming in to the wrist, the fingers lengthening and tipping with little black claws",
                 turning: "the arm furred to the elbow, the hand drawn long, the fingers hooking to claws",
                 turned:  "ended in a long black-clawed paw, fur to the shoulder, the fingers gone to hooks" },
        pig:   { tingle:  "a thick clumsy heaviness in the hand, the fingers stiff and disinclined to part",
                 tainted: "the hand broadening and hardening, the fingers fusing two-and-two, bristle at the wrist",
                 turning: "the arm shortened and forelegged, the hand closing toward a split, weight-bearing trotter",
                 turned:  "a short foreleg now, the hand closed to a split trotter, walking-built" },
        filth: { tingle:  "a soft numbness in the fingers, the grip uncertain, as if the hand might flow off",
                 tainted: "the fingers blurring together, the hand going soft and grey, weeping where it grips",
                 turning: "the hand lost to a dripping grey paddle that takes a thing by closing around it",
                 turned:  "a fingerless dripping pseudopod that holds a thing by flowing around it" }
    },
    leg: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "a twitchy lightness in the foot, the heel wanting to lift, a readiness to bolt",
                 tainted: "the foot narrowing and clawing, the heel rising, the leg quickening under you",
                 turning: "the leg drawn to a runner's spring, heel high, the foot clawed to squeeze through gaps",
                 turned:  "a clawed runner's foot, the heel lifted, built to scurry and squeeze" },
        pig:   { tingle:  "a dull heaviness in the leg, the foot wanting to plant and stay, slow to lift",
                 tainted: "the foot hardening and narrowing toward a hoof, the heel rising, the ankle thickening",
                 turning: "the leg shortened and hard, the foot gone mostly to trotter, made for standing not running",
                 turned:  "down to the trotter, the heel risen, a hog's short hard walking-leg" },
        filth: { tingle:  "a soft give in the knee and ankle, the leg feeling unreliable, apt to spread underfoot",
                 tainted: "the leg softening grey, the foot flattening and spreading where it takes your weight",
                 turning: "the leg a grey column that splays where it bears down, then gathers slowly back to shape",
                 turned:  "a slumping grey column that spreads where it bears weight, then pulls back to shape" }
    }
};

/* ---- THE TRANSFORMATION FEED — body-change BEATS narrated AT THE MOMENT corruption lands
   (owner 2026-06-24: "a more detailed description of the changes as they happen"). Distinct
   from BODY_DESC: that is the STATE readout in the side-bar (what a segment looks like NOW);
   this is the TRANSITION beat (what just happened to you), surfaced in the main column.
   setup.corrupt records the before/after on setup.lastChange; the <<corrupt>> widget calls
   setup.pushChange to queue a beat onto $pendingChanges; PassageHeader flushes the queue at
   the top of the next room (so a <<corrupt>> inside a link still narrates where you land).
   Lives in THIS raw-JS block, not the run-block, because the prose carries operator-words
   ("to"/"and"/"not") that the StoryInit desugaring would mangle inside string literals.
   ---- */
setup.SEG_PROSE = { head: "head", torso: "body", armL: "left arm", armR: "right arm", legL: "left leg", legR: "right leg" };

/* what to print when a BIG hit (>= CHANGE_MIN_AMT) lands inside a stage already entered —
   no new threshold crossed, so a short "it works deeper" beat instead of repeating the full one */
setup.CHANGE_DEEPEN = {
    rat:   "The rat digs further into your ",
    pig:   "The pig roots deeper into your ",
    filth: "The filth seeps further into your "
};

/* the predicate that follows "Your <part> " — part-type × class × the stage just REACHED.
   4 part-types × 3 classes × 4 stages. Written as transition beats (present tense, felt then
   seen), one register with CombatLost's maul-prose. The 'turned' cells take a finality tag. */
/* VOICE-PASS 2026-06-24: the feed leans FELT/INVOLUNTARY — what it is like to have the change
   happen TO you (the body wanting things, acting without you, the loss of self) — and leaves the
   anatomical inventory (whiskers, ribs, snout, grey grease) to BODY_DESC. Run tools/feed-inspect.mjs
   --overlap: the two channels now share almost nothing. */
setup.CHANGE_DESC = {
    head: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "won't quit gnawing at nothing — an itch in the jaw that arrives with a borrowed hunger, a want to bite down that began without you.",
                 tainted: "keeps doing what you didn't ask: testing the air, flinching at sounds, an alertness that isn't yours running it from underneath.",
                 turning: "thinks lower and quicker than you do now; you reach for a word and it has already listened, already cringed, already gone.",
                 turned:  "answers only to the gnaw — it reads the dark with a flat hungry attention and you ride along behind it, a passenger in your own skull." },
        pig:   { tingle:  "goes thick and slow, a low crowding weight behind the eyes, and a stupid ease leaks in — a want to quit thinking and just feed.",
                 tainted: "keeps tipping toward the ground without your leave, the thoughts coming heavier and fewer, the world shrinking to what can be rooted up.",
                 turning: "has mostly stopped arguing; it wants the trough and the warm crush of the herd, and wants them with a placid certainty louder than you.",
                 turned:  "is the hog's now, slung low and patient and content, and what's left of you watches its small dull wants get met and minds them less each hour." },
        filth: { tingle:  "stops holding its shape quite right — a numb vagueness, the sense the face you wear is a habit you might forget partway through.",
                 tainted: "won't stay arranged; whatever you mean to show slides off half-made, and you grow unsure, from the inside, of where you end.",
                 turning: "is mostly given over — no fixed place the 'you' looks out from anymore, only a wet grey patience that was a head this morning.",
                 turned:  "is the aggregate's now, a packed dimness with no face to it; whatever did the looking has thinned into the general filth and stilled." }
    },
    torso: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "hollows out around a hunger food won't fill, and goes light, quick, wrong — a readiness to run you never decided on.",
                 tainted: "carries itself narrow and tense and ready to bolt; the breath comes fast and shallow whether or not you're afraid.",
                 turning: "moves before you do — a flinch, a freeze, a dart for cover — run by an old vermin caution that has moved in under your skin.",
                 turned:  "is the rat's quick frightened engine now, all hunger and flight; you feel it want to flee and to feed in equal measure, and you go along." },
        pig:   { tingle:  "settles a warm heavy ease low in you, a sweet sinking weight, a want to lie down right here and be fed and troubled by nothing.",
                 tainted: "wants the ground more than the upright; it sags and broadens and grows patient, and two legs start to feel like a thing you're owed a rest from.",
                 turning: "is going down toward all fours by degrees, heavy and placid, and the part of you that minds goes quieter each time it sinks.",
                 turned:  "is the sow's slow contented bulk now, built to wallow and feed; it asks so little, and you find to your horror that you can give it that." },
        filth: { tingle:  "loosens at the core — a soft creeping give, as if the packed center of you had quietly agreed to come apart.",
                 tainted: "won't keep its edges; you feel yourself spreading at the seams, held in the shape of a person mostly by the memory of being one.",
                 turning: "is more given than kept — it slumps and re-gathers when you shift, taking your outline back slowly, like a courtesy it may stop doing.",
                 turned:  "is the aggregate now, a sodden patient heap in the rough idea of a person; it holds together from habit and would let go if you asked." }
    },
    arm: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "won't hold still — the fingers itch to dig and pry and turn things over, a frantic small industry in the hand that has nothing to do with you.",
                 tainted: "does quick wrong things on its own: snatches, hoards, worries at seams; you look down and it is already busy at something verminous.",
                 turning: "has mostly stopped taking orders — it grips and tears with a clawed eagerness, ahead of your intent, hungry on its own account.",
                 turned:  "is the rat's tool now, quick and grasping; it takes what it wants before you have decided that you wanted it." },
        pig:   { tingle:  "goes heavy and dull, the hand slow and clumsy and disinclined, as though it would rather not stay a hand much longer.",
                 tainted: "stops being good for fine work; it thickens toward something that pushes and bears weight, and fingers begin to feel like an indulgence.",
                 turning: "is folding down toward a foreleg, made for walking now and not for holding; reaching for a thing instead of leaning on it becomes the odd request.",
                 turned:  "is a forelimb built to carry the hog's weight; it has forgotten how to hold, and you have nearly forgotten you ever asked it to." },
        filth: { tingle:  "goes soft and uncertain at the grip — a numbness, a sense that if you stopped minding it the hand would run clean off the end of your wrist.",
                 tainted: "loses its sureness; to hold a thing now you must mean it, gather yourself around it on purpose, or feel it slip the softening fingers.",
                 turning: "takes things only by closing slowly over them — no fingers left to speak of, just a willing grey eagerness to engulf.",
                 turned:  "is a grey reaching softness now, fingerless and patient; it holds by flowing around a thing and lets go by forgetting it held." }
    },
    leg: {
        rat:   { tingle:  "won't stand easy — the heel keeps lifting, the foot keeps testing the way out, a bolt-readiness humming where your weight should rest.",
                 tainted: "wants to run more than to walk; it quickens and lightens under you and aims itself at every gap and shadow without consulting you.",
                 turning: "is mostly given to flight now — coiled, sprung, listening through the floor; you mean to stand and it has by then picked the way to go.",
                 turned:  "is the rat's runner now, made for the low quick dash and the gap nothing should fit through; it carries you toward every exit whether or not you meant to leave." },
        pig:   { tingle:  "goes heavy and reluctant, every step a small argument it is losing; it would sooner set down where it stands and never be asked to lift again.",
                 tainted: "would rather bear than travel; it hardens toward standing, and each step begins to feel like effort the body quietly resents.",
                 turning: "is built for the sty now, not the road — short, hard, planted; to walk any distance becomes a thing it simply declines to do.",
                 turned:  "is down to the hog's hard standing-leg; it holds you up well and takes you nowhere fast, and minds that not at all." },
        filth: { tingle:  "goes unreliable beneath you — a soft give in the knee, a sense the leg might spread like wet ground if you trust it with your weight.",
                 tainted: "won't quite bear you the same way twice; it softens and splays where you press down and gathers back a beat too slow to feel safe.",
                 turning: "is more column than leg now, spreading under the load and drawing itself back into shape like a favour it is tiring of.",
                 turned:  "is a slumping grey support that spreads and re-gathers with every step; it keeps you upright the way a habit keeps a thing going." }
    }
};

/* build the one-line beat for a queued change (a part, a class, and the stage just reached).
   deepen = a big within-stage hit (no new threshold) → the short "works deeper" line. */
setup.describeChange = function (ch) {
    if (!ch) { return ""; }
    var who = setup.SEG_PROSE[ch.seg] || "body";
    if (ch.deepen) {
        return (setup.CHANGE_DEEPEN[ch.cls] || "The change works deeper into your ") + who + ".";
    }
    var part = setup.PART_TYPE[ch.seg] || "torso";
    var pred = ((setup.CHANGE_DESC[part] || {})[ch.cls] || {})[ch.toStage] || "";
    if (!pred) { return ""; }
    /* no appended finality tag: the turned cells already enact irreversibility in-voice, and
       the bold cf-turned styling marks the lock — a flat refrain would only blunt it. */
    return "Your " + who + " " + pred;
};

/* called by the <<corrupt>> widget right after setup.corrupt. Reads the transient
   setup.lastChange and queues a beat onto $pendingChanges IF it is worth narrating:
   a fresh threshold cross, a finished turn, or a single hit big enough to feel. The
   small ambient +2/+3 ticks that cross no line stay silent, so the feed keeps its bite. */
setup.CHANGE_MIN_AMT = 8;
setup.pushChange = function () {
    setup._queueBeat(setup.lastChange);
    setup.lastChange = null;                              /* consume once */
    var spills = setup.lastChangeSpills || [];            /* + any overflow hops (owner 2026-07-03) */
    setup.lastChangeSpills = [];
    spills.forEach(function (ch) { setup._queueBeat(ch); });
};
/* queue ONE change beat IF it's worth narrating — a fresh threshold cross, a finished turn, or a
   single hit big enough to feel. Shared by the primary landing and each overflow-spill hop, so a
   corruption that maxes one limb and floods the next narrates BOTH (the small ambient ticks that
   cross no line still stay silent, keeping the feed's bite). */
setup._queueBeat = function (ch) {
    if (!ch || !(ch.amt > 0)) { return; }
    if (ch.toStage === "human") { return; }              /* still below the first sign — nothing to show */
    var crossed = ch.fromStage !== ch.toStage;
    if (!(ch.turned || crossed || ch.amt >= setup.CHANGE_MIN_AMT)) { return; }
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.pendingChanges) { V.pendingChanges = []; }
    V.pendingChanges.push({ seg: ch.seg, cls: ch.cls, fromStage: ch.fromStage, toStage: ch.toStage, deepen: !crossed && !ch.turned });
};

/* ---- SYSTEMIC REGARD prose (owner 2026-06-24) — the world's standing verdict on the body you
   wear. Keyed [relation][floorClass][tier 1..3]. MATCHED = this band's denizens read you as their
   own; the horror is being CLAIMED, expected, accounted for — no vote asked (and in the pig
   carnival it is seductive, the welcome that is also the trap). MISMATCHED = a place that gets to
   define "wrong" has decided you are it: marked, weighed, measured. Tone is per-band (pig =
   seductive welcome / contempt; rat = feral acceptance / heavy-intruder; filth = claimed-by-the-
   swarm / read-as-meat). Built by setup.regardOf; surfaced by the PassageHeader regard beat. Lives
   here (script block) because the prose carries operator-words the run-block desugaring would mangle. */
/* OLFACTORY PASS 2026-06-25: the world's verdict is a SCENT-read — kin/intruder recognition is the
   most animal sense there is, and this game's horror is bromidrophobia (the stink you can't wash off or
   smell on yourself). Every read is now the world's NOSE — giving the social cost of a corrupt body a
   voice (the filth FORM_MOD's CHA−1, "and it shows", bites loudest in the MISMATCHED reads, where a
   wrong-classed body is read as repellent). Filth is the purest: the aggregate cannot tell you from
   itself by smell. */
setup.REGARD = {
    matched: {
        pig: {
            1: "The carnival's pigs catch the sty-smell coming up in you and hold on it a beat too long as you pass, and there is a fondness in the snuffle that has already settled on you the way a place settles on where a thing belongs.",
            2: "The pigs greet you by scent now — a snuffle, a nod, a space made at the rail — reading the mud and slop of their own kind on you, and nobody thought to ask whether you wanted to belong to it.",
            3: "You cross the pig-court and not one snout even turns: you smell exactly as you ought, of sty and feed and warm crowded bodies, which is to say of nothing remarkable at all. You are expected. You are accounted for. You are theirs."
        },
        rat: {
            1: "The drains go quiet as you pass — the rat-things catching a musk coming off you that they know, and choosing, for now, not to scatter from one of their own.",
            2: "The vermin den around you without fear now, noses working, reading the runs on you as kin, and not one of them startles at a thing that smells exactly as it ought.",
            3: "The rats do not run from you anymore. They thread close to scent-mark and be marked, and under the alarm of it sits a low animal ease at smelling, at last, like a thing that belongs in the dark."
        },
        filth: {
            1: "The filth of this place stops resisting you as you go through it; it has caught its own reek rising off you, and what smells of the aggregate, the aggregate does not refuse.",
            2: "The slow grey mass no longer reaches for you the way it reaches for meat — meat smells of blood and panic, and you have stopped smelling of either. You smell of it now; it reaches the way a thing reaches for more of itself.",
            3: "Nothing here hunts you, because nothing here can tell you apart: the drowned, the rendered, the swarm read one undifferentiated stink and you are simply part of it — claimed not by any welcome but by the plain failure of the place to find an edge where you stop and it starts."
        }
    },
    mismatched: {
        pig: {
            1: "The carnival's pigs catch a wrong note in your scent and the fondness curdles to suspicion; you do not smell of the sty, and a snout does not forget a thing like that.",
            2: "You smell of vermin here, or of rot — the wrong reek in the wrong house — and the pig-things track the offence of you the way a kept sty watches what crawled in stinking of the drains.",
            3: "The pig-court has your scent and it is not kin. Wherever you go the wrongness of you arrives a step ahead, a smell already judged — the attention a fastidious place turns on a thing it can smell does not belong."
        },
        rat: {
            1: "The drains do not quiet for you; the rat-things catch a scent too rich, too heavy — not vermin, not theirs — and keep their distance, noses working the wrongness of you and finding no kin in it.",
            2: "You smell wrong for the runs — too warm, too large-lunged, the reek of a thing that lives up in the light and the open air — and the vermin read you from the dark as no business of this deep.",
            3: "Nothing here takes your scent for kin. The rat-things hold their breath as you pass, noses shut against the wrongness of you — and you are marked, in the one place that should have been beneath notice, by a sense that does not lie and cannot be argued with."
        },
        filth: {
            1: "The filth of this place does not know your smell, and a scent it cannot place it weighs; you feel yourself sniffed over, assessed.",
            2: "You smell of meat here — of blood still moving, of a thing not yet gone over — and the slow grey patience of the place turns toward that freshness with an attention that is its own kind of threat.",
            3: "The drowned and the rendered read you by scent as raw stock come in early, still sweet, still whole. Nothing greets you; everything leans toward the smell of you. To this place you are a smell not yet broken down."
        }
    }
};

/* ---- NOSE-BLIND prose (owner 2026-06-25) — the one-time per-class realization that you've gone
   anosmic to what you're becoming (olfactory adaptation: you stop smelling the thing once there's no
   "you" apart from it to smell it with). Filth is home (the rot); rat/pig generalize. Surfaced once per
   class per life by the PassageHeader nose-blind beat against $noseBlind. ---- */
setup.NOSE_BLIND = {
    filth: "It takes you a while to notice what you have stopped noticing: the reek. The rot, the wet grey stink that turned your stomach on the way down — it is simply gone. Not washed off. You have lost the place you stood apart from it to smell it from. It is not on you any longer. It is you, and a thing does not smell itself.",
    rat:   "Somewhere back in the dark the sour animal musk of the runs — the piss-and-pellet reek that warned you what denned down here — stopped reaching you. It has not faded. The smell that kept you wary is your own now, and you cannot find the edge of yourself it used to warn you back from: there is no longer a you for it to warn.",
    pig:   "You cannot say when the sty stopped stinking. The hot fug of mud and dung and crowded bodies that gagged you at the gate is only the smell of home now, which is to say no smell at all. You have been breathing yourself for some time without once noticing."
};

/* ---- ROOM-SCENT prose (owner 2026-06-25) — the THIRD olfactory system. REGARD = the world smells
   YOU; NOSE_BLIND = you stop smelling YOURSELF; ROOM-SCENT = your reaction to the WORLD's stink, and
   how it erodes as you corrupt — the full olfactory-ADAPTATION curve. THREE spoken tiers: `recoil` (a
   FRESH human's involuntary revolt — gorging, gagging, eyes streaming, ~corruption ≤10), `accept` (the
   disgust-alarm gone quiet, ~75), `relish` (worse — the body WANTS it, ~90). The EXTREMES speak; the
   habituated middle (11–74) stays SILENT (the room's own prose carries the dulled disgust there). Recoil
   is the voiced baseline the later tiers betray — the same smell rejected in full alarm, then calmly
   tolerated, then wanted. Each kind carries a `class` for the species-affinity bonus: a TURNED limb of
   the matching class makes you comfortable with that smell sooner (a rat-man eases into the den, not the
   sulphur). Stench-class is set by what the SMELL is, not the floor's faction — the sewer smells of the
   aggregate FILTH that mutated the rats, so a rat-man's home-smell is the den (rat), while the mains
   read filth. Surfaced by the PassageHeader room-scent beat; built by setup.scentTier. Lives here (script
   block) — the prose carries operator-words the run-block desugaring would mangle. ---- */
setup.ROOM_SCENT = {
    sewage: { class: "filth",   /* L1–3 mains: ammonia, chemical wrongness, rot — the aggregate's medium */
        recoil: "The sewer-stink hits you like a hand clapped over your face — ammonia sharp enough to wring tears from you, rot beneath it, and beneath THAT a chemical wrongness with no name — and your whole body recoils at once: gorge climbing, the back of your throat slamming shut, a hand at your nose and mouth before thought catches up. Everything in you says get out, get up, get to air.",
        accept: "The sewer-stink — ammonia and rot and the chemical wrongness under it — reaches you now the way weather reaches you: a fact of the air, not an assault. Somewhere on the way down you stopped holding your breath against it, and you cannot remember deciding to.",
        relish: "You draw the drain-reek in deep and easy, and under the chemistry there is a richness the body leans toward — wet and close and fed, the smell of things coming apart into something simpler and more patient. It smells, you catch yourself thinking, like settling in." },
    denMusk: { class: "rat",    /* TheCrawl: piss, pellet, the sour milk-and-rot of a thing that whelps in the dark */
        recoil: "The den-stink rolls out of the dark and your stomach turns clean over — a hot animal reek of piss and pellet and sour milk-rot, the smell of too many bodies whelping in too little air. You gag on it, the back of your hand jammed to your mouth, every nerve telling you that whatever makes a smell like this is a thing you do not want to find in the dark with you.",
        accept: "The den-musk — piss and pellet and the sour milk-and-rot of a thing that litters in the dark — used to put the hair up on your neck. It doesn't now. It reads as occupancy. As somewhere lived-in. As somewhere a body could lie down.",
        relish: "The musk of the runs goes through you warm, and the animal in you answers it before the rest of you can object: this is den, this is close bodies and no light and nothing that hunts you here. You want, very simply, to be further in." },
    offal: { class: "pig",      /* L7 belly: hot blood, opened organ, the wet heat of a place that is all inside */
        recoil: "The belly's heat breathes up into your face and you nearly lose what little is in your stomach — hot blood and opened organ, the wet close reek of a place that is all inside, all wound. Your eyes flood, your throat clamps, and you stand there fighting your own gorge, every animal part of you appalled to be somewhere that smells like the inside of the dying.",
        accept: "The belly's smell — hot blood and opened organ and the wet animal heat of a place that is all inside — was the worst thing you'd ever stood in. Now it is only the air in here. Close. Warm. The smell of being somewhere alive, even if the alive thing is not quite you.",
        relish: "The organ-heat fills you, rich and close, and the body takes it not as horror but as nearness — blood and meat and warmth, the inside of things, where it is dark and fed and nothing is ever cold. You have wanted, for longer than you would admit, to be somewhere the cold could never reach. This is that somewhere." },
    pork: { class: "pig",       /* TheSty / TheGutway: wet pork, dung, penned bodies. accept stays sensory-present
                                   (the kidnap callback lives in relish; "stopped noticing" is NOSE_BLIND.pig's job) */
        recoil: "The sty-reek closes over your face and your body knows it before your mind will say so — wet pork and dung and the hot crush of penned bodies, the smell that was the last thing you breathed as a free creature. You lurch back from it on instinct, not the gorge so much as the deeper animal certainty that this smell is the door of the cage swinging open, and you would do anything — anything — not to be walked back through it.",
        accept: "The sty-smell — wet pork and dung and the close heat of penned bodies — was unbearable once, a thing to gag and turn from. It isn't now. It is only the air in here: the smell of where the pigs are, where bodies are kept warm and close and crowded. The smell, by now, of where you are.",
        relish: "The hot fug of the sty goes into you and something answers it as home — mud and feed and crowded warmth, the smell of belonging to a body among bodies, of being kept and never again alone. The horror of the night they took you has worn through to something nearly like relief. They were only bringing you here." },
    privy: { class: "filth",    /* TheLatrine / ThePrivyShrine: the Šulak's cathedral, the oldest undefended thing a body does */
        recoil: "The latrine-stench is a solid thing and it walks straight into you — the heaped reek of the oldest, least defended thing a body does, multiplied past all counting, ankle-deep and patient. Your stomach heaves. You breathe through your sleeve, through your fingers, through anything, eyes streaming, the whole animal of you desperate not to be here, not to be caught here, not to add to it.",
        accept: "The latrine-reek — the heaped stink of the oldest and least defended thing a body does — used to be a smell you escaped. Now you stand in it and your shoulders come down. There is a strange privacy to it. A permission. No one is watching here who has not always been watching.",
        relish: "The reek of the great latrine settles over you like a held breath let out, and the part of you that was always braced — always half-listening at the stall door — lets go at last. There is no one here to be ashamed in front of; there never was. To smell of this is to have nothing left worth hiding. You could stay, the deep part of you decides. You could stay and stay." },
    tallow: { class: "filth",   /* L8 Works: scorched hair, hot fat, bodies going to product — and the broth-lie */
        recoil: "The tallow-stink of the Works hits you as a solid wall — hot fat and scorched hair and the unmistakable reek of bodies cooked down to product — and your gorge surges up to meet it. You double over, retching on nothing, eyes pouring, one hand flat on the wall and the other clamped over your face, and you cannot make it stop: the stomach trying to turn itself out over a smell it understands far too well.",
        accept: "The tallow-stink of the Works — scorched hair, hot fat, the reek of bodies going to product — sits in your throat and no longer turns your stomach. It is the smell of work being done. You have stopped flinching from it the way you stopped flinching from the heat off the vats.",
        relish: "The rendering-smell reaches you and something in you answers before thought can catch up — broth, warm and rich and nearly ready, the old animal certainty that this is food. That the word rises in you and you do not recoil from it is the worst of it. The fat heart of the place smells like supper. You are hungry, and you have stopped minding what for." },
    sulfur: { class: "pig",     /* L9 Deep: brimstone, the bottom of the world. class:pig — the throne-ward is the
                                   pig-court's own ground (MAP: "wet pork under the brimstone — Their smell"), so a
                                   pig-bodied player is at home in it; it is not a neutral mineral reek. */
        recoil: "The brimstone hits the back of your throat like a blow and every breath after is a small wound — sulphur thick enough to taste, to choke on, to feel scorching the wet of your eyes. You cough, you gag, you turn your face away hunting for air that isn't anywhere down here — and there is none, only the raw chemical reek of the actual bottom of the world, going into you with every breath you cannot help but take.",
        accept: "The brimstone scrapes your throat the way it should, and you breathe through it the way you breathe through everything now. It is only air. Bad air, but air, and you have lived in worse on the way down than the smell of the bottom of the world.",
        relish: "You draw the next breath of sulphur deliberately, all the way down, and it is — bracing. Clean, almost, the way a struck match is clean, the way the air goes clean before a storm. Some animal certainty in you has decided this is the smell of arriving. Of getting, at last, where all of this was always going." }
};

/* ---- THE WORK-CURSE (DIRECTION §C) — the indenture / respawn mechanic ----
   Take the curse (WILLINGLY at the Arrivals → you pick your post; or ASSIGNED, hell
   picks by floor) and you respawn at your WORKSTATION after a lost fight, owing one
   shift of work before the station will let you leave. The station's class is worked
   into you each shift: cage → pig, vats → filth. The curse banks as a PERMANENT
   cross-life mark (work_<station>) — take it once and every future life starts
   pre-indentured at that post (pure accumulation; it never washes off). Held in this
   raw-JS block (not the StoryInit run-block) because the labels are DISPLAYED, which the
   operator-word desugaring would mangle. */
setup.WORKSTATIONS = {
    cage: { room: "TheCageAct",   cls: "pig",   floor: 6, label: "the carnival cage",  post: "the menagerie row" },
    vats: { room: "TheBoilHouse", cls: "filth", floor: 8, label: "the rendering vats", post: "the boil-house floor" }
};
setup.workRoom = function () {
    var st = setup.WORKSTATIONS[State.variables.workStation];
    return st ? st.room : null;
};
setup.workLabel = function () {
    var st = setup.WORKSTATIONS[State.variables.workStation];
    return st ? st.label : "";
};
/* take the curse: set the in-life state AND bank the permanent mark (so it carries even
   if this run ends badly). station defaults to cage if unknown. */
setup.takeWorkCurse = function (station) {
    if (!setup.WORKSTATIONS[station]) { station = "cage"; }
    var V = State.variables;
    V.workCursed = true;
    V.workStation = station;
    setup.addMark("work_" + station);
    setup.dressInWorkRags();                 /* the indenture issues you your uniform (defined in the run-block) */
    return setup.WORKSTATIONS[station];
};
/* ASSIGNED path: hell picks the post by the floor you're on (deep → vats, else cage).
   Reserved for involuntary sources (cross-life seeding uses the banked station directly;
   future snares/helpers can call inflictWorkCurse). Combat-loss does NOT auto-conscript —
   an UNCURSED loss stays a plain CombatLost maul, so sneaking out keeps you yourself. */
setup.assignStation = function () {
    return (setup.depthOf[State.passage] || 0) >= 7 ? "vats" : "cage";
};
setup.inflictWorkCurse = function (station) {
    return setup.takeWorkCurse(station || setup.assignStation());
};
/* one shift: the station's class worked into a random segment (4..8); clears the debt.
   Coin/flavor is the room's business — this is just the corruption + the unlock. */
setup.WORK_LEATHER_AT = 5;     /* shifts worked before the job issues you free leather (owner 2026-06-06) */
setup.WORK_COOLDOWN = 20;      /* encounter-eligible moves of grace after ANY shift before the floor accosts you again (owner 2026-06-17) */
setup.doShift = function () {
    var V = State.variables, st = setup.WORKSTATIONS[V.workStation];
    if (!st) { V.workOwed = false; return null; }
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), amt = 4 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);
    setup.corrupt(seg, st.cls, amt);
    setup.passTime(setup.SHIFT_TIME);        /* C1: a shift is hours — it books belonging as well as corruption */
    V.workOwed = false;
    V.workCooldown = setup.WORK_COOLDOWN;    /* just clocked out — left alone for a while */
    V.shiftsWorked = (V.shiftsWorked || 0) + 1;
    /* long service is rewarded: at WORK_LEATHER_AT shifts the job hands you leather armour */
    var earnedLeather = false;
    if (V.shiftsWorked >= setup.WORK_LEATHER_AT && !V.inventory.includes("leathers")) {
        V.inventory.push("leathers");
        if (!setup.slotLocked("armor") && (!V.armor || V.armor === "rags" || V.armor === "clothes")) { V.armor = "leathers"; }
        setup.recomputePlayer();
        earnedLeather = true;
    }
    return { cls: st.cls, seg: seg, amt: amt, shifts: V.shiftsWorked, leather: earnedLeather };
};

/* RANDOM-ENCOUNTER press-gang work (owner 2026-06-05): a ONE-OFF shift at a random work
   location — corruption of that work's class, but NO permanent curse (distinct from doShift,
   which is the indenture). Labels are DISPLAYED so they live in this block. */
setup.PRESSWORK = [
    { label: "the carnival cage, to caper for the crowd", cls: "pig" },
    { label: "the rendering vats, to stir the boil",       cls: "filth" },
    { label: "the screen-rakes, to comb the slow flow",    cls: "filth" },
    { label: "the meat-haul, to fetch and carry for the belly", cls: "pig" },
    { label: "the rat-runs, to gnaw the choked cables clear",    cls: "rat" }
];
setup.pressedToWork = function () {
    var w = setup.PRESSWORK[Math.floor(Math.random() * setup.PRESSWORK.length)];
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), amt = 4 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);
    setup.corrupt(seg, w.cls, amt);
    setup.passTime(setup.SHIFT_TIME);   /* C1: pressed or not, the hours pass */
    return { label: w.label, cls: w.cls, seg: seg, amt: amt };
};
/* ONE-OFF FORCED SHIFT (owner 2026-06-07): an UNCLAIMED player who submits — surrenders/loses a
   fight, or goes quietly with the press-gang — is marched to a RANDOM real workstation (cage L6 /
   vats L8), works a single shift there, and is then let go (NO curse, NO recurring debt). Distinct
   from the work-curse binding (which reels a CLAIMED player to their own post owing shifts).
   pressGangTo stashes where to return; the station room renders the pressed branch + calls
   doPressedShift, which works the shift (station-class corruption) and hands back the return room. */
setup.pressGangTo = function (returnRoom, station) {
    var V = State.variables;
    var st = setup.WORKSTATIONS[station] ? station : ((Math.random() < 0.5) ? "cage" : "vats");
    V.pressedReturn = returnRoom || V.combatOrigin || "Hellmouth";
    V.pressedStation = st;
    return setup.WORKSTATIONS[st].room;           /* "TheCageAct" or "TheBoilHouse" */
};
setup.doPressedShift = function () {
    var V = State.variables, st = setup.WORKSTATIONS[V.pressedStation] || setup.WORKSTATIONS.cage;
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), amt = 4 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);
    setup.corrupt(seg, st.cls, amt);
    setup.passTime(setup.SHIFT_TIME);        /* C1: pressed or not, the hours pass */
    V.workCooldown = setup.WORK_COOLDOWN;    /* a pressed shift earns the same grace as an owed one */
    V.pressedStation = "";   /* $pressedReturn is cleared by the room's "back" link, not here */
    return { cls: st.cls, seg: seg, amt: amt };
};

/* ===== POSITIVE RANDOM EVENTS — "finds" (owner 2026-06-17) =====================
   Some random events are GOOD. The per-room coin pickups were THINNED out of the rooms and
   relocated here, surfaced as random events that still NAME the real room on the current floor
   they belong to — you catch word of / glimpse / recall the coin still lying two pitches over,
   in a real place on this level, and slip off to fetch it though you aren't standing in it.
   Each find is ONE-SHOT, gated by the room's own *Looted flag (REUSED — same flag the room used),
   so a find can fire from anywhere on its floor but only once, and the loot economy is unchanged:
   only the DELIVERY changed, from guaranteed-on-visit to discovered-on-the-move. (These strings
   are DISPLAYED, so the table lives in this raw-JS block — the run-block would desugar "to"/"and".)
   type: "coins" | "item" | "cleanse". cost (optional) = a little corruption you accept to grab it
   (its class is the band's, via setup.findCostClass). blurb = the offer (names the room); take = the
   line shown once you go for it. Add a floor's finds + thin its rooms together to avoid double-dip. */
setup.findCostClass = { 1: "filth", 2: "filth", 3: "filth", 4: "filth", 5: "pig", 6: "pig", 7: "pig", 8: "filth", 9: "pig" };
setup.FINDS = [
    /* --- SEWER · L1 Storm Drains — the surface's small change, washed down to the dark economy --- */
    { layer: 1, room: "TheStreetCatch", flag: "streetCatchLooted", type: "coins", min: 4, max: 8,
      blurb: "It comes to you on the next cold draught: the street-catch a way back, that sump under the kerb where the gutters drop the surface's small change — coin among the bottle-caps and the lost keys, the bright world's pennies fed down into the dark one, still lying there for whoever goes back for them.",
      take: "You go back to the catch and pick the spendable out of the sad, and leave the keys and the barrette and the swollen book to go on being the surface's quiet sediment in the dark." },
    { layer: 1, room: "TheGulley", flag: "gulleyLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 3, max: 6,
      blurb: "You picture the silt-gulley off the catch, shin-deep in the grey paste the storm-water drops when it slows, and the duller glint you half-saw down in it — something that was worth more before the gutter had it, still there for the combing.",
      take: "You go back and comb the silt, and come up with coin and a fistful of grit, while the storm-water moves on past your ankles toward the light, carrying its endless freight of small lost things, of which you are now, technically, one." },
    { layer: 1, room: "TheStrainer", flag: "strainerLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 5, max: 9,
      blurb: "The trash-screen comes back to you — that century-built wall of branch and bottle and worse dammed against the iron bars, and the things wedged in it just out of reach, that the current was carrying when someone might still have wanted them back.",
      take: "You go back and work your arm into the screen's wall to the shoulder; it closes around you wet and total, and lets you come back out with coin and a long cold moment of not being at all sure it was going to let go." },
    { layer: 1, room: "TheRainShaft", flag: "rainCleanseUsed", type: "cleanse", min: 8, max: 14,
      blurb: "Something almost good surfaces in your memory of the rain-shaft — the one place down here where clean water falls, the storm coming straight down out of the surface grey, cold and real and not yet anything's but the sky's. You could go back and stand under it a while.",
      take: "You go back and stand under the falling rain with your face turned up, and for a few breaths it sluices some of the filth off you and out of you — clean surface water carrying a little of the dark back down the drain it came from." },
    /* --- SEWER · L2 Trunk Mains --- */
    { layer: 2, room: "TheGritTrap", flag: "gritLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 2, max: 5, cost: 2,
      blurb: "You remember the grit-trap back by the screening hall — the sunken bay where the heavy flow drops its load, rings and coin and a wristwatch stopped at a time that mattered to someone, half-glimpsed in the muck, diggable if you don't mind what your hands come up wearing.",
      take: "You go back and dig through the grit, and come up with cold coin and a smear of something that stings and the old certainty that you should wash your hands and never will." },
    { layer: 2, room: "TheLostConduit", flag: "conduitLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 3, max: 6,
      blurb: "The abandoned conduit surfaces in your mind — the silted dry-ish run where things wash in and never wash back out, half-buried coin among a previous optimist's patient bones, worth a look if your nerve holds the trip back.",
      take: "You go back and search the silt, and turn up coin and a fist of corroded oddments, and leave the bones where they lie, because coin spends down here — especially down here." },
    /* --- SEWER · L3 Old Drains --- */
    { layer: 3, room: "TheVotiveDrain", flag: "votiveLooted", type: "coins", min: 4, max: 7,
      blurb: "It rises with the smell of wet mortar: the votive drain, that side-passage someone made a wishing-well, coin pressed into the walls and knotted to old nails and dropped in its hundreds into the silt — wishes addressed downward, to a god that lived in the right direction, which is to say down.",
      take: "You go back and work the coin loose from the mortar, and each one comes away with a small wet reluctance, as though you are not collecting the offerings so much as receiving them — a thought you put down quickly and do not pick back up." },
    { layer: 3, room: "TheDeadLetterDrain", flag: "deadLetterLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 3, max: 6,
      blurb: "The dead-letter drain comes to mind — the silted dead-end where the old system gave up its current and let the water stand, a strata of the lost with coin salted all through it, a hundred years of what the city flushed and forgot it owed an answer to.",
      take: "You go back and dig the strata of the lost, and come up with coin and a brass button and a fistful of something that crumbles before you can name it, and you do not, this time either, read the addresses on the fused grey loaf of letters." },
    /* --- BETWEEN · L4 Drowned Galleries — votive coin & grave-goods under the flood --- */
    { layer: 4, room: "TheStillFont", flag: "fontLooted", type: "coins", min: 4, max: 7,
      blurb: "You remember the still-font back off the reflecting hall — the offerings ringed around its lip, coin pressed edgewise into the carving by a thousand kneeling drowned, cold as the black water and just sitting there above it.",
      take: "You go back and gather the coin from the font's lip; it comes loose into your palm cold as the water, each piece stamped with a face that watched a great many people kneel here and never rise." },
    { layer: 4, room: "TheReliquary", flag: "reliquaryLooted", type: "coins", min: 5, max: 9,
      blurb: "The drowned vestry surfaces — the burst cupboards and their litter of the holy and the looted settled under a hand's depth of still water, votive coin by the fistful, wavering and doubled where the water keeps a copy of everything and is reluctant to give the copy up.",
      take: "You go back and gather the coin from the flooded floor, grasping twice before you close on each piece, and something under the silt closes soft and shy around your wrist as you reach, and lets go before you can be sure it was ever there." },
    { layer: 4, room: "TheSiltKings", flag: "siltKingsLooted", type: "coins", min: 6, max: 10, cost: 3,
      blurb: "The silt-kings come back to you — that ring of half-drowned thrones, the seated shapes of silt and bone in the rotted last of their finery, and the toll-coin glinting in their laps, grave-goods for a ferryman, if you've the nerve to lift it from the lap of a king.",
      take: "You go back and lift the toll-coin from the kings' laps; none of them moves, and that is the worst of it — the not-moving feels less like death than a courtesy they are extending, on the understanding that you are only visiting, for now." },
    { layer: 4, room: "TheTombIsland", flag: "tombSalveFound", type: "item", item: "salve",
      blurb: "The tomb-island comes back to you — the one dry slab in all the drowned dark, where the dead are only dead — and the pale grave-moss you saw furring the old stone there, the kind the renderers swear knits a wound shut and asks no questions.",
      take: "You go back to the dry island and gather a wad of the pale grave-moss off the tombs; it smells of cold stone and clean rot, and it is, down here, very nearly medicine." },
    /* --- CARNIVAL · L6 Shambles — spilled winnings & the unclaimed --- */
    { layer: 6, room: "TheLostAndFound", flag: "lostFoundLooted", type: "coins", min: 5, max: 9,
      blurb: "Word drifts back to you of the lost-and-found booth on the midway — the jar of unclaimed coin behind the counter, the change that falls out of a mark when the carnival turns him upside down, nobody minding the till of it.",
      take: "You slip back to the lost-and-found and lift the coin from the jar, among the single shoes and the orphaned keys and the small sad things nobody is ever, now, coming back to claim." },
    { layer: 6, room: "TheTill", flag: "tillLooted", type: "coins", min: 4, max: 8,
      blurb: "The open till comes to mind — the games-stall drawer you saw gaping, the barker three pitches off and busy fleecing somebody else, the coin in it just sitting there gathering nobody's attention but yours.",
      take: "You slip back and lift what's loose from the open till, quick and quiet, and are three stalls gone before the barker turns round to a drawer he could have sworn held more." },
    { layer: 6, room: "TheBigTop", flag: "bigTopRopeFound", type: "item", item: "rope",
      blurb: "The big top comes back to you — all that rigging holding the great tent against the dark, and the coil of good rope you saw slung loose on a stay-peg, spare line nobody'd miss from a tent that has all the rope in hell.",
      take: "You slip back under the big top and work the coil of rigging-rope off its peg; it's sound, and long, and the kind of thing that gets a body up a shaft or across a gap that wanted to keep it." },

    /* --- HELL · L7 Belly of the Beast — coin gleaned off the meat trade --- */
    { layer: 7, room: "TheMeatRow", flag: "meatRowLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 6, max: 11,
      blurb: "A hand grabs your sleeve out of the dark and points: back along the shambles, at the meat-row, a coin is lying in the stall-gutter where a butcher dropped it and was too busy bleeding something to stoop. It is two rows over and it is real.",
      take: "You slip back to the meat-row, cut the loose coin out of the clotted gutter, and are gone before anyone looks up from the work." },
    { layer: 7, room: "TheOrganTrove", flag: "organTroveLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 7, max: 12, cost: 2, costClass: "filth",
      blurb: "You remember the racked organs hung in rows back at the organ-trove, and the coin you saw bedded among them — payment, or part of someone who carried payment. It's worth going back for. It will also want a little of your arm to reach in among that.",
      take: "You go back and glean the coin from between the slung organs; something in there is still warm, and a little of it works into your reaching arm." },
    { layer: 7, room: "TheToothWell", flag: "toothWellLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 5, max: 9,
      blurb: "Word reaches you, the way things do down here, of the tooth-well a few turns back — that ring of shed teeth with a coin sifted somewhere down in the enamel, if you've the stomach to go sift it.",
      take: "You go back and sift the coin out of the well of teeth, and try not to count how many of the teeth are the right size to be yours." },
    /* --- HELL · L8 Rendering Works — coin settled in the fat & lye --- */
    { layer: 8, room: "TheTallowStore", flag: "tallowStoreLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 7, max: 12,
      blurb: "A reek of rendered fat reminds you: back in the tallow-store, between the great casks, there was loose coin gleaming in the grease. Nobody's counting it. Nobody down here counts anything but bodies.",
      take: "You slip back among the casks and glean the coin out of the grease, wiping it on your rags until it almost looks like money again." },
    { layer: 8, room: "TheCandleWorks", flag: "candleWorksLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 6, max: 10, cost: 2,
      blurb: "You picture the cooling-trays back at the candle-works, the coin you saw set into a half-poured tray of tallow. Prising it free means putting your arm into what they pour the candles from — but it's coin, and it's there.",
      take: "You go back and pick the coin from the cooling tray; the part of the rendering that hasn't set yet takes the chance to work a little of itself into your arm." },
    { layer: 8, room: "TheSoapVat", flag: "soapVatLooted", fresh: true, type: "coins", min: 5, max: 9,
      blurb: "The thought of the soap-vat's spilled overflow comes back to you — coin skimmed up in the scum where the lye runs over, a few turns back the way you came, free to anyone who'll reach into the slick for it.",
      take: "You go back and skim the coin off the soap-spill, and your fingers come away clean in a way the rest of you can't remember being." },
    /* --- HELL · L9 Sulphur Deep — coin among the brimstone & tribute --- */
    { layer: 9, room: "TheSulphurHoard", flag: "sulphurHoardLooted", type: "coins", min: 8, max: 13,
      blurb: "It rises in you with the brimstone stink: the sulphur-hoard back along the shore, coin lying bright among the canary-yellow jewels of crusted sulphur, nobody guarding what nobody down here can spend.",
      take: "You go back and take the coin from among the sulphur-jewels, and it is warm, and it stays warm in your fist longer than coin should." },
    { layer: 9, room: "TheVentMouth", flag: "ventMouthLooted", type: "coins", min: 6, max: 11, cost: 2,
      blurb: "You remember the vent-mouth a way back, and the coin cooling on its lip — close enough to snatch, if you don't mind the breath of the vent getting into your arm while you do it.",
      take: "You go back and snatch the cooling coin off the vent's lip; the vent exhales while you reach, and a little of what it breathes settles in your arm." },
    { layer: 9, room: "TheTribute", flag: "tributeLooted", type: "coins", min: 7, max: 12,
      blurb: "The tribute-heap comes to mind — the pile of offerings left for the things that rule down here, coin among it, and nobody's counted the tribute in a long age. A little less of it would never be missed.",
      take: "You go back to the tribute-heap and lift a little coin off the top, quietly, the way you'd take from a god you didn't quite believe was watching." },

    /* --- ITEM finds (NEW, not migrated): hell drops useful things too --- */
    { layer: 7, room: "TheStillborn", flag: "bellySalveFound", type: "item", item: "salve",
      blurb: "You recall the still place back at the stillborn — and the small clay pot you half-noticed and didn't take, the kind the renderers keep their burn-salve in. It would still be there. Things are, down here.",
      take: "You go back and take the little pot of salve; it smells of fat and herbs and the faint hope of not hurting for a moment." },
    { layer: 8, room: "TheHooks", flag: "hooksGaffFound", type: "item", item: "hook",
      blurb: "The hooks. You remember the rows of them back at the hanging-hooks, and one gaff among them loose on its chain — a real tool, a real reach, just hung there waiting for a hand that wasn't a hook itself.",
      take: "You go back and work the loose gaff off its chain. It's pitted and old, but it's iron, and it's yours, and it has a point on it." },

    /* --- CLEANSE find (NEW): rare grace, even here --- */
    { layer: 9, room: "TheCrust", flag: "crustCleanseUsed", type: "cleanse", min: 8, max: 14,
      blurb: "Something improbable surfaces in your memory of the crust — that one fumarole back there breathed not brimstone but clean steam, hot and pure, the only honest water in all of hell. You could go back and stand in it a moment.",
      take: "You go back and stand in the clean steam with your eyes shut, and for a few breaths some of what hell has put on you simply lifts off and is gone." }
];
/* finds available to surface ON THE FLOOR YOU'RE ENTERING (encounterReturn) that you haven't taken */
setup.eligibleFinds = function () {
    var V = State.variables, L = setup.depthOf[V.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
    var inured = setup.inuredEnough();
    return setup.FINDS.filter(function (f) {
        if (f.layer !== L || V[f.flag]) { return false; }
        if (f.fresh && !inured) { return false; }   /* a `fresh`-gated find is a too-gross-to-reach-into coin: a FRESH body (corruption <= SCENT_RECOIL_AT) won't put a hand in it. It stops being offered while fresh and surfaces once you've inured — delaying easy coin at low levels. (The goodfind encounter weight scales with this count, so a fresh player also gets fewer find-offers overall.) */
        return true;
    });
};
setup.pickFind = function () {
    var pool = setup.eligibleFinds();
    return pool.length ? pool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length)] : null;
};
/* take a find: set its one-shot flag, grant the reward, pay any cost. returns info for prose. */
setup.takeFind = function (f) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!f || V[f.flag]) { return null; }
    V[f.flag] = true;
    var out = { type: f.type, room: f.room };
    if (f.type === "coins") { var c = f.min + Math.floor(Math.random() * (f.max - f.min + 1)); setup.gainCoins ? setup.gainCoins(c) : (V.coins += c); out.coins = c; }
    else if (f.type === "item") { setup.acquire(f.item); out.item = f.item; out.itemName = (setup.items[f.item] || {}).name || f.item; }
    else if (f.type === "cleanse") { var s = f.min + Math.floor(Math.random() * (f.max - f.min + 1)); setup.soothe(s); out.soothe = s; }
    if (f.cost) { var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), cls = f.costClass || setup.findCostClass[f.layer] || "filth"; setup.corrupt(seg, cls, f.cost); out.cost = f.cost; out.costSeg = seg; out.costClass = cls; }
    return out;
};

/* KIN HELPER (owner 2026-06-17; spends the under-used kin_<class> marks). If you have wholly
   turned a limb-class in a past life, a creature of that class on this floor reads you as one of
   its own and DOES YOU A KINDNESS — coin slipped to you, a wound licked closed, or simply waved
   past. classOnFloor() = which mutagen class denizens this band; kinReady() = you're kin to it.
   R17: the kinhelp ARM branches on bloodOf(class) — at BLOOD_FELT the kindness curdles (the
   beat still fires, showing the withdrawal; no coin, no heal). kinReady itself stays blood-blind
   so the encounter can fire and be SEEN to curdle rather than silently stopping. */
setup.classOnFloor = function (passage) {
    var d = setup.depthOf[passage || State.variables.encounterReturn || State.passage] || 0;
    if (d <= 3) { return "rat"; }      /* sewer vermin */
    if (d === 4) { return "filth"; }   /* the drowned / aggregate */
    if (d === 8) { return "filth"; }   /* the renderers */
    return "pig";                      /* L5 mouth · L6 carnival · L7 belly · L9 castle — pig-ruled */
};
setup.kinReady = function () {
    var c = setup.classOnFloor();
    return setup.isKin(c) ? c : null;
};
setup.KIN_FLAVOR = {
    rat:   { who: "A rat-thing", deed: "drops a gnawed-bright coin at your feet and is gone into the pipes before you can refuse it" },
    pig:   { who: "A pig-demon", deed: "looks at the pig in you, grunts something that is almost a greeting, and presses coin into your hand the way kin slip each other money at a wake" },
    filth: { who: "The aggregate", deed: "parts around you instead of closing on you, and where it touched the worst of your hurts it draws the ache out and keeps it, the way family takes a share of a burden" }
};
setup.takeKinHelp = function () {
    var V = State.variables, c = setup.classOnFloor();
    var coin = 4 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 7), heal = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);
    if (setup.gainCoins) { setup.gainCoins(coin); } else { V.coins += coin; }
    V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + heal);
    return { cls: c, coin: coin, heal: heal };
};

/* ===== THE BLOOD LEDGER (review R17) — victory finally leaves residue. Losing writes itself
   into your body; winning used to write NOTHING, so the murderhobo stance was the cheapest and
   cleanest path — the exact inversion of the horror canon. Now every body that FALLS (not fled —
   a broken enemy takes nothing of you with it, in both directions) is tallied by mutagen class
   in $blood, and the world reads the ledger the way it reads everything else about you: by
   smell. Cost is REGARD/ATTENTION, never meter points (a clean run structurally requires
   fighting): at BLOOD_FELT the kin of the killed stop being kind (kinhelp curdles, the
   kin-claim pass closes, morale DC +2 — its kind's blood on you argues for running); at
   BLOOD_FEARED the floor's own denizens stop offering labour (go-quietly withdrawn — a known
   killer of their kind is not pressed, he is handled). The work-curse binding-reel stays
   reachable at any blood: a ledger has no nose. Per-life (deeds, not marks). */
setup.BLOOD_FELT   = 3;   /* kills of a class at which its kin smell the blood on you */
setup.BLOOD_FEARED = 5;   /* ...at which its floor stops offering you the shift */
setup.bloodOf = function (cls) {
    var b = State.variables.blood || {};
    return b[cls] || 0;
};
setup.tallyBlood = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    V.blood = V.blood || { rat: 0, pig: 0, filth: 0 };
    (V.enemies || []).forEach(function (e) {
        if (!e.fled) { V.blood[e.cls] = (V.blood[e.cls] || 0) + 1; }
    });
};

/* ===== THE SHORT-WEIGHT MEN (owner 2026-07-03) — the THIRD ledger. Regard reads what you ARE
   (the body), blood reads what you DID (the kills); the short-weights read what you CHOSE NEVER
   TO BE — the ability you dumped at creation, the door left unlocked that you walk past in every
   life. "The denizens keep score." A short-weight is a grey opportunist that has weighed you and
   found you wanting in one specific pan, and comes to collect the difference — it reads dumpStat()
   and runs a check against your WEAKEST number, never a fair one. Fail-forward always (coin/
   corruption/a shove/an ambush — never a wall). Two things give it teeth: the FRESH −2 rides the
   check (statCheck folds it), so the deep hunts the unhardened hardest; and the encounter WEIGHT
   scales with statSpread() — a min-maxer paints a target, a flat "seven all round" build is grey
   and safe and never hunted, which finally makes creation's spread a real risk curve. Six faces,
   dispatched by which stat is lowest; WIS is the outlier — its gap is passive (you don't get a
   sidle-up, you get AMBUSHED: a failed sense = the fight starts with the enemy already having
   hit you, review R9). Prose here (script block = desugar-safe). ===== */
setup.SHORTWEIGHT_DC = 10;              /* the check DC; the test is on your DUMP stat, so failure is common by design (tunable) */
setup.SHORTWEIGHT_PRIORITY = ["wis", "int", "cha", "con", "dex", "str"];  /* tie-break: the trickster prefers the cleverest cruelty (WIS ambush first) */
setup.dumpStat = function () {
    var sc = State.variables.scores || setup.playerScores();
    var lo = null, loScore = 999;
    setup.SHORTWEIGHT_PRIORITY.forEach(function (st) {
        var v = (sc[st] == null) ? 10 : sc[st];
        if (v < loScore) { loScore = v; lo = st; }   /* strict < → earliest-in-priority wins a tie */
    });
    return { stat: lo, score: loScore };
};
setup.statSpread = function () {
    var sc = State.variables.scores || setup.playerScores();
    var vals = setup.STATS.map(function (st) { return (sc[st] == null) ? 10 : sc[st]; });
    return Math.max.apply(null, vals) - Math.min.apply(null, vals);
};

/* the ambush primitive (review R9): start a fight AND let the enemy take one free opening turn,
   so the Combat screen opens with the enemy having ALREADY hit you. Returns the opening log for
   the caller to set as $combatLog; the caller checks combatOutcome() (a free hit can't drop a
   full-HP player, but the tri-check is cheap and honest). Reusable for any future ambush. */
setup.ambushFight = function (spec, ret) {
    var V = State.variables;
    setup.startFight(spec, ret);
    V.combatOrigin = V.encounterReturn || State.passage;
    V.encounterFight = true;                            /* a lost ambush still rolls CombatLost's work-check */
    return setup.enemyTurn(false);                      /* THE FREE TURN */
};

/* the shared sidle-up (the 5 social faces; WIS writes its own — a lurker gives no warning) */
setup.SHORTWEIGHT_LEAD = "You've an audience. One of the deep's //short-weight men// — the grey clerks that keep the other scales, the ones that weigh not what you carry but what you //lack// — has watched you long enough to have your number, and steps out of a dark that should not have held anything, to collect on it.";
setup.SHORTWEIGHT = {
    str: {
        face: "a leaner",
        intro: "It found the strength wanting in you, and so it simply //leans// — peels off the wall and puts the whole dead weight of itself against you like a door that wants shutting, and while you are bent under it its hands are already in your coat.",
        tryLabel: "Set your feet and throw it off",
        pass: "You get under the weight and //heave//, and the grey thing staggers back off you with a sound like a sigh — reassessing, letting you by. Not this one.",
        fail: "You push, and the push goes nowhere; there was always more of it than there was of you, and by the time it steps off you of its own accord your purse is lighter and it is folding back into the wall.",
        failShove: "You push, and the push goes nowhere; there was always more of it than there was of you — and finding no purse worth the lifting, it takes its difference another way, one short hard shove into the brick that rattles your teeth, before it folds back into the wall.",
        cedeLabel: "Just pay it to shove off",
        cede: "You press a coin into the leaning weight and it lifts, businesslike, and lets you past. Cheaper than learning what it would have taken."
    },
    dex: {
        face: "a flicker",
        intro: "You feel it before you see it — a fast cold nothing against your hip — and then it //is// there, a lean thing with too many fingers already halfway through your pockets, grinning at how slow you turned. It weighed the quickness in your hands a street ago and posted itself accordingly.",
        tryLabel: "Catch its wrist",
        pass: "Your hand closes on the wrist — faster than it banked on — and it goes still, then melts backward empty-handed, filing the correction away for next time.",
        fail: "You grab where it was. It is already three feet off and folding your coin into itself, unhurried, because it knew before you did that your hand would arrive late.",
        failShove: "You grab where it was — too late, always too late — and it comes up out of your empty pockets with nothing, and flicks you hard across the ear for the waste of its time before it's gone.",
        cedeLabel: "Let it have the loose coin and go",
        cede: "You stop grabbing and just let it. It lifts a coin off the top, almost polite, and is gone. The ones who don't grab lose less."
    },
    con: {
        face: "a breather",
        intro: "It sidles closer than anything should want to and //breathes// on you — a long wet exhale thick with the place, the rot and the damp and whatever lives in both — full in your face before you can turn. It read the softness in your chest and came to make a deposit.",
        tryLabel: "Weather it — lock your throat, breathe shallow",
        pass: "You take it flat and whatever it put on the air finds no purchase; your chest, for once, holds. It watches you not-sicken with something like professional disappointment, and withdraws.",
        fail: "You breathe it in because you have to breathe, and it goes down into you and //settles//, warm and wrong, somewhere a fresh body cannot defend. The grey thing nods, its deposit made.",
        cedeLabel: "Back off holding your breath",
        cede: "You clamp your mouth and retreat before the worst of the cloud; only a little gets in — a taste, a tightness, less than it meant to give you."
    },
    int: {
        face: "a sharp",
        intro: "This one sits, with a little folding table and three cups and a pea it wants to show you — or a paper it needs signed, or a wager it swears is in your favour; the shape changes, the smile does not. It weighed your wits at a glance and dealt itself in. //Follow the pea. It's the easy one. It's always the easy one.//",
        tryLabel: "Play — you can see the trick, surely",
        pass: "You watch the cups instead of the patter, and the pea is where it should not be able to be, and you say so, and the sharp's smile does not slip so much as //set//. It slides the pot to you and packs up. Some marks are more trouble than the mark is worth.",
        fail: "You follow the pea, and the pea was never in it, and the cups are empty — and so, a breath later, is your purse. The sharp is already resetting for the next slow one. //You were sure. That is the whole of the trick: you were sure.//",
        failShove: "You follow the pea, and the pea was never in it — and when your purse turns up empty there is nothing in it to win off you, and the sharp cuffs you off its stool like a debt it cannot collect and packs the table away. //You were sure. That is the whole of the trick.//",
        cedeLabel: "Want no part of it — walk",
        cede: "You keep walking. The sharp does not even look up; there is no game in a mark who will not sit down, and no shame in being the one who wouldn't. //The wise leave the table.//"
    },
    cha: {
        face: "a shunner",
        intro: "It looks at you the way a doorman looks at the wrong coat — a long weighing look that finds you not worth the trouble, that has already settled that you are no one anybody would miss — and it plants itself in the way and names a price for passing it would never name to someone with standing.",
        tryLabel: "Face it down — carry yourself like you matter",
        pass: "You meet the weighing look and do not drop it, and give it nothing to grip, and after a moment the grey thing shrugs and unblocks the way. You weren't worth a scene either. Standing is mostly the refusal to have none.",
        fail: "You open your mouth and nothing in it lands; the look was right and you both know it, and to get past you make yourself //smaller//, agree to be the no-one it decided on — and something in you settles a little further toward belonging here.",
        cedeLabel: "Lower your eyes and slip past small",
        cede: "You don't fight it. You make yourself little and unremarkable and beneath its notice, and it lets the nothing-you by — and being nothing gets a fraction easier each time you choose it."
    },
    wis: { face: "a lurker" }   /* WIS is passive/ambush — the RandomEncounter branch writes it, no sidle-up */
};
/* resolve the GAMBLE (stat check on your dump); applies the fail-cost, returns the outcome object.
   A robbery with no coin to take lands a shove instead, so the fail always costs SOMETHING. */
setup.shortweightTry = function (stat) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (setup.statCheck(stat, setup.SHORTWEIGHT_DC)) { return { passed: true }; }
    var out = { passed: false };
    if (stat === "str" || stat === "dex" || stat === "int") {
        var base = (stat === "int") ? 2 : 1;           /* the sharp fleeces a little deeper */
        var took = 0;
        if (V.coins > 0) { took = Math.min(V.coins, base + Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.ceil(V.coins / 2))); V.coins -= took; }
        if (took > 0) { out.took = took; } else { V.hp = Math.max(1, V.hp - 1); out.shove = 1; }
    } else if (stat === "con") {
        out.seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(); out.cls = "filth"; out.amt = 5; setup.corrupt(out.seg, out.cls, out.amt);
    } else if (stat === "cha") {
        out.seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(); out.cls = setup.classOnFloor(); out.amt = 4; setup.corrupt(out.seg, out.cls, out.amt);
    }
    return out;
};
/* resolve the CONCEDE (a certain smaller toll instead of the gamble); INT's is a free walk. */
setup.shortweightCede = function (stat) {
    var V = State.variables, out = { ceded: true };
    if (stat === "str") { if (V.coins > 0) { out.took = Math.min(V.coins, 2); V.coins -= out.took; } }
    else if (stat === "dex") { if (V.coins > 0) { out.took = 1; V.coins -= 1; } }
    else if (stat === "con") { out.seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(); out.cls = "filth"; out.amt = 2; setup.corrupt(out.seg, out.cls, out.amt); }
    else if (stat === "cha") { out.seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(); out.cls = setup.classOnFloor(); out.amt = 2; setup.corrupt(out.seg, out.cls, out.amt); }
    /* int: the wise decline — no cost */
    return out;
};

/* ===== BESPOKE CAPTURE / LOSS SCENES (owner 2026-07-03) — most lost fights end the same way:
   the deep hauls the fallen off to a WORK SHIFT (the pig cage / kappa vats). But some places don't
   run shifts — they KEEP their catches, and marching a rat-run loss to a pig cage reads wrong. This
   registry, keyed by $combatOrigin (the room the fight started in), lets a set-piece override the
   generic press-gang TAIL of CombatLost with its own capture beat + destination. The shared top
   (maul / class-taint / coins) still runs; the work-curse binding still takes priority over any of
   this (signed property is collected first). Prose here = desugar-safe (script block). Extensible:
   add an entry per den that takes rather than employs. ===== */
setup.CAPTURE_SCENE = {
    TheRatRun: {
        label: "Be dragged down into the run",
        dest: "TheRatKing",
        prose: "But the deep does not haul you off to a shift this time — the rats have first claim, and rats do not share. They swarm you where you fell, dozens of them, not biting so much as //gathering//, a hundred small grips in your clothes and your hair and your skin, and they //pull// — not up and out the way you came, but down, deeper into the warm dark of the run, toward the heat and the hush at the bottom of it that even they go quiet approaching. You are stock now, not a crawler passing through: something the household caught, and is bringing home to show the thing it keeps. You do not get to leave the way you came. You get dragged the other way."
    },
    TheRatKing: {
        label: "Crawl back out, kept for later",
        dest: "TheRatRun",
        prose: "But the den does not clock its catches in — it //keeps// them. The rat-men take you up under the arms, unhurried, proprietary, and carry you the last few feet to the nest, and hold you up while the vast pale king looks you over the way a man looks over stores laid in against a hard winter. Then some slow rat-thought moves behind its wet little eyes — //not yet//, or //not this one//, or only //later// — and the grip loosens, and you are half-carried, half-spilled back out the way you were brought in, marked now, known, a thing the den has handled and set aside. You crawl up out of the king's dark certain of one thing: that it was a postponement, not a pardon."
    }
};

/* ===== SYSTEMIC REGARD (owner 2026-06-24) — the world reads the body you wear, AS A RULE.
   The transformation FEED narrates your body CHANGING; regard narrates the world ANSWERING it.
   Compare bodyClass() (what you are MOSTLY becoming) against classOnFloor() (which class rules this
   band): MATCHED = the denizens read you as one of their own and claim you, no vote asked;
   MISMATCHED = a place that gets to define "wrong" has decided you are it. This is the OUTWARD face
   of the agency-horror — not who you were, but what they have settled on your being. Prose lives in
   setup.REGARD (script block); surfaced as a cooldown-gated ambient PassageHeader beat so it's a
   rule, not a nag. kinReady's cross-life mark, if you hold it, escalates a matched read. */
setup.REGARD_MIN_LOAD = 35;     /* below this you read as still mostly yourself — the world lets it pass */
setup.REGARD_COOLDOWN = 8;      /* eligible-moves of grace after a regard beat (a change refreshes sooner) */

/* ---- BELONGING / the settling mind (owner 2026-07-01): the seal clock ($deepTurns → $sealed) is not
   only the way-up closing — it is the MIND getting comfortable in the dark, and in the shape the deep is
   making of you, as the clock climbs. Comfort is the corruption. sealTier() grades it 0-3 off the same
   knobs; SEAL_MIND carries the prose. The caption's .seal-state shows the standing state (from ≥ WARN); a
   .settle-line beat fires ONCE per tier escalation (monotonic $sealNoticed) as a milestone stinger.
   The tier-3 line is deliberately SCOPED: a whole-Sigil holder still walks out the front (layer5
   EndingUnbound is NOT $sealed-gated), so it denies only the climb up and the WANT to leave, never all
   exit — feelings, not a mechanical no-exit claim. ---- */
setup.sealTier = function () {
    var V = State.variables, d = V.deepTurns || 0;
    if (V.sealed || d >= setup.SEAL_LIMIT) { return 3; }
    if (d >= (setup.SEAL_WARN + setup.SEAL_LIMIT) / 2) { return 2; }   /* ~290: settling in */
    if (d >= setup.SEAL_WARN) { return 1; }                            /* 220: the first ease */
    return 0;
};
setup.SEAL_MIND = {          /* [t1, t2, t3] — indexed by sealTier() - 1 */
    caption: [
        "The way back up has stopped nagging at you.",
        "This shape, this dark — they've started to feel like yours.",
        "You live here now. You've stopped reaching for the way out."
    ],
    beat: [
        "You catch yourself not listening for the way out. The worry that used to sit behind your teeth has gone quiet, and you do not miss it.",
        "Somewhere above, the climb stopped being yours. You notice it the way you'd notice weather, and turn back to what you were doing. The dark isn't where you ended up anymore — it's where you're from.",
        "You had a reason to go up, once; you're sure of it the way you're sure of a dream at noon. Whatever leaves here now goes out the front, or not at all — and the part of you that would have minded has finished settling in."
    ],
    /* the un-settling: your dominant nature has changed (rat → pig), so the shape you were easing into is
       not the shape you're becoming anymore, and the comfort resets. Fired on a form switch; the clock
       goes back to SEAL_RESET_TO and the deep starts claiming the new you from nothing. */
    switched: function (oldCls, newCls) {
        return "Something in you turns over. The " + setup.CLASS_LABEL[oldCls] + " in you is giving way to the " +
            setup.CLASS_LABEL[newCls] + ", and the comfort of almost-belonging goes out like a pinched wick. " +
            "The dark is strange again — and you are strange in it. Whatever you were settling into being, " +
            "the settling starts over from nothing.";
    }
};

/* ---- THE HONEST TOLL (owner trust pass, R4): pay-with-yourself prices in the REAL currency.
   Posted prices used to read "(+20 corruption)" — but that lands in ONE segment bucket, so the
   visible meter (avg of six) moves a sixth of the number, and the label said nothing about WHERE
   it lands, WHAT it makes you, or whether it would FINISH the part. This is the label a player
   reads before selling a piece of themselves, so it tells the whole truth: amount, class, segment
   (the bodymap's own words), escalating when the price would turn the part for good (soothe skips
   turned segments — that sale is forever). Mirrors corrupt()'s always_class curse resolution so
   the tag never lies about what would actually land. Returns the bare clause, no parens: toll
   links wrap it, the Cutter/Pryer graft labels splice it mid-sentence. */
setup.tollTag = function (seg, cls, amt) {
    if (!setup.SEGMENTS.includes(seg)) { seg = "torso"; }
    if (!setup.CLASSES.includes(cls)) { cls = "filth"; }
    if (setup.hasCurse && setup.hasCurse("always_class")) {
        var forced = setup.curseParam("always_class", "class");
        if (forced && setup.CLASSES.includes(forced)) { cls = forced; }
    }
    var s = "pays " + amt + " " + setup.CLASS_LABEL[cls] + " into your " + setup.SEG_LABEL[seg];
    if (((State.variables.form || {})[seg] || "human") !== "human") {
        s += " — turned already; it scarcely matters now";
    } else if (setup.segTotal(seg) + amt >= 100) {
        s += " — enough to turn it for good";
    }
    return s;
};

setup.regardTier = function (bc) {            /* 1 tingeing · 2 mostly · 3 wholly — turned limbs first, then load */
    if (!bc) { return 0; }
    if (setup.becameClass() === bc.cls || bc.limbs >= 4) { return 3; }
    if (bc.limbs >= 2 || bc.load >= 60) { return 2; }
    return 1;
};
setup.regardOf = function (passage) {
    var bc = setup.bodyClass();
    if (!bc || bc.load < setup.REGARD_MIN_LOAD) { return null; }      /* still mostly yourself */
    var floor = setup.classOnFloor(passage);
    if (!floor) { return null; }
    var relation = (bc.cls === floor) ? "matched" : "mismatched";
    var tier = setup.regardTier(bc);
    var kin = !!(setup.isKin && setup.isKin(floor));
    if (relation === "matched" && kin && tier < 3) { tier += 1; }    /* the deep has always known you */
    var line = (((setup.REGARD[relation] || {})[floor] || {})[tier]) || "";
    return { relation: relation, floor: floor, body: bc.cls, tier: tier, kin: kin, line: line,
             key: relation + ":" + floor + ":" + bc.cls + ":" + tier };
};

/* NOSE-BLIND (owner 2026-06-25) — olfactory adaptation made a mechanic, the bromidrophobia motif's
   sharpest point: once you are MOSTLY a class, you stop being able to smell it — there is no longer a
   "you" standing apart from it to smell it with. The realization that you've stopped noticing means you
   are further gone than the meter says (the agency-horror by way of the nose). Fires ONCE per class per
   life. Home is filth (the rot you become); generalizes to rat/pig. Prose: setup.NOSE_BLIND (script
   block); checked + flagged in PassageHeader against $noseBlind. */
setup.NOSE_BLIND_LOAD = 50;     /* a class's avg body-load (or 3 turned limbs) at which its smell becomes your own neutral */
setup.noseBlindReady = function (cls) {
    return setup.classLoad(cls) >= setup.NOSE_BLIND_LOAD || setup.classLimbs(cls) >= 3;
};

/* ===== ROOM-SCENT (owner 2026-06-25) — the world's stink, and your eroding disgust at it ============
   The THIRD olfactory system (with REGARD / NOSE_BLIND). A stinky room has an intrinsic stench-KIND
   (setup.scentOf: a band default by depth, plus per-room overrides — a clean rest-room opts OUT, a
   special room reskins). Your reaction to it is the full olfactory-ADAPTATION curve, sliding with
   GENERAL corruption: `recoil` (a FRESH body in violent revolt, ~0-10) -> [silent middle: revulsion
   has habituated to "bad but survivable" — the room's own prose carries it] -> `accept` (the alarm gone
   quiet, ~75) -> `relish` (the body wants it, ~90). The extremes SPEAK (the fresh recoil and the late
   acceptance/craving), the habituated middle stays silent — and the recoil baseline is what the later
   erosion betrays (you remember how unbearable it was). LIVE / reversible: re-derived each room from the
   current meter, so washing off restores the disgust — the continuous slide, where NOSE_BLIND is the
   latched once-per-life milestone. Plus a SPECIES AFFINITY (owner): each TURNED limb whose class matches
   the smell adds SCENT_AFFINITY_PER_LIMB to the effective corruption, so you go comfortable in your own
   kind's places first (a rat-man eases into the den before a fresh body would; sulphur, a pig smell,
   gives him nothing). Additive-only, matching-class-only — no penalty for a rival's smell. Prose:
   setup.ROOM_SCENT; surfaced as a cooldown-gated PassageHeader beat (reuses REGARD_COOLDOWN). ========= */
setup.SCENT_RECOIL_AT = 10;        /* at/below this a FRESH body is in violent revolt — the extreme human reaction (recoil) */
setup.SCENT_EASE_AT = 75;          /* effective corruption at which the disgust-alarm has gone quiet (acceptance) */
setup.SCENT_RELISH_AT = 90;        /* ...and at which it inverts — the body wants the stink (relish) */
setup.SCENT_AFFINITY_PER_LIMB = 5; /* +this to effective corruption per TURNED limb whose class matches the smell */
setup.SCENT_BAND = { 1: "sewage", 2: "sewage", 3: "sewage", 7: "offal", 8: "tallow", 9: "sulfur" };
                                   /* uniform-stench bands; L4–6 (drowned galleries / hellmouth / carnival) have no
                                      intrinsic single reek, so they use per-room overrides only. */
setup.SCENT_OVERRIDE = {           /* a reskin, or null to OPT OUT (a deliberately clean/dry room in a stinky band) */
    TheCrawl: "denMusk", TheSumpGalleries: "denMusk", /* L3 the two rat dens — the rat smell (the den, not the chemical mains) */
    TheSty: "pork", TheGutway: "pork",                /* L7 the sty proper */
    TheLatrine: "privy", ThePrivyShrine: "privy",     /* L7 the Šulak's latrine */
    TheChute: "tallow",                               /* L7→L8 descent: the Works breathe up the chute */
    ThePumpRoom: null, TheCleanPool: null, TheLimeVault: null,  /* L2/L3 dry/clean rest-rooms */
    TheStillborn: null,                               /* L7 grey, inert */
    TheCooling: null,                                 /* L8 set tallow, almost clean */
    TheCrust: null                                    /* L9 cold yellow shelf */
};
setup.scentOf = function (passage) {
    var p = passage || State.passage;
    if (setup.SCENT_OVERRIDE.hasOwnProperty(p)) { return setup.SCENT_OVERRIDE[p]; }   /* reskin or explicit opt-out */
    return setup.SCENT_BAND[setup.depthOf[p] || 0] || null;
};
setup.scentTier = function (passage) {
    var kind = setup.scentOf(passage);
    if (!kind || !setup.ROOM_SCENT[kind]) { return null; }
    var entry = setup.ROOM_SCENT[kind], cls = entry.class;
    var eff = (State.variables.corruption || 0) + setup.SCENT_AFFINITY_PER_LIMB * setup.classLimbs(cls);
    var tier = "";
    if (eff >= setup.SCENT_RELISH_AT) { tier = "relish"; }
    else if (eff >= setup.SCENT_EASE_AT) { tier = "accept"; }
    else if (eff <= setup.SCENT_RECOIL_AT) { tier = "recoil"; }   /* a fresh body recoils hard at the reek */
    else { return null; }          /* the habituated silent middle — the room's own prose carries the dulled disgust */
    return { kind: kind, cls: cls, tier: tier, eff: eff, line: entry[tier] || "", key: kind + ":" + tier };
};

/* FRESH-REVULSION gates + penalty (owner 2026-06-25) — the recoil band (corruption ≤ SCENT_RECOIL_AT)
   isn't only flavour; a FRESH body's disgust has mechanical teeth, and the horror is the INVERSION it
   sets up: at the very start the WORLD penalises you for staying human, and a little corruption is the
   relief (the agency-loss motif, mechanised — the game rewards giving in).
   (1) setup.inuredEnough() — gates foul interactions a fresh human can't make themselves do (the privy
       shrine's deliberate unguarding, reaching into rendered-human tallow, …). You must have given a
       little before the body will give the rest. It is the EXACT INVERSE of setup.composedEnoughToBow
       (which locks once you're too CORRUPTED to bend like a person) — the two bracket the range: too
       fresh to kneel at the filth-shrine, too far gone to bow to the kappa.
   (2) Non-combat STAT CHECKS take setup.freshCheckPenalty() while fresh — queasy, flinching, unsteady,
       the reek souring every deliberate act — so the world's non-combat demands come harder until you
       inure. Route future non-combat checks through setup.statCheck(stat, dc) and the penalty is
       automatic. (Combat keeps its own corruption/limb penalties; this is non-combat only.) */
setup.SCENT_FRESH_CHECK_PENALTY = 2;   /* −this to a non-combat stat-check roll while fresh — a "slight" hit on a d20 */
setup.inuredEnough = function () { return (State.variables.corruption || 0) > setup.SCENT_RECOIL_AT; };
setup.freshCheckPenalty = function () { return setup.inuredEnough() ? 0 : setup.SCENT_FRESH_CHECK_PENALTY; };
setup.statCheck = function (stat, dc) {  /* d20 + the stat's mod − the fresh penalty ≥ dc. The convention for ALL non-combat checks. */
    var sc = State.variables.scores || setup.playerScores();
    var roll = setup.d(20), mod = setup.mod(sc[stat] || 10), pen = setup.freshCheckPenalty();
    var total = roll + mod - pen, ok = total >= dc;
    /* R7 fingerprint (delivered with the short-weights, 2026-07-03): stash the last roll so callers
       can narrate the MARGIN (a hair / clearly / the reek made it worse) without re-rolling. Still
       returns a plain boolean — coercion never calls .valueOf, so old callers are untouched. */
    setup.lastCheck = { stat: stat, roll: roll, mod: mod, pen: pen, dc: dc, total: total, margin: total - dc, fresh: pen > 0, passed: ok };
    return ok;
};
/* a word for how the last check went (for narration); "" if none has run */
setup.checkMargin = function () {
    var c = setup.lastCheck; if (!c) { return ""; }
    if (c.passed) { return c.margin >= 6 ? "easily" : (c.margin >= 3 ? "well enough" : "by a hair"); }
    return c.margin <= -6 ? "not remotely" : (c.margin <= -3 ? "clearly" : "by a hair");
};

/* ---- THE MIND REGISTER (the gutter-bones' downstream; how the WORLD reads your wits).
   Tiers by current INT (folds $statMods/marks/forms/gear via $scores). Base INT is 7 — the
   unmarked everyman is "dull", NOT dim. Three ways down/up from there:
     • "dim"  (INT ≤ 5): the gutter has taken real pieces — the world MOCKS or MISreads you
       (the reaction beats: the bone-man's look, the tout, the fly's read, the inscription),
       and a mind too simple to con or frighten is, in two places, the only one that gets
       through (the Hall of Mirrors, the Fortune-teller).
     • "simple" (INT ≤ 1, the floor): smart NPCs openly DUMB-DOWN and condescend, REPLACING
       their normal dialogue with small words "for your own good." The likelihood scales with
       the NPC's OWN intelligence — the articulate ones (the Fly, the appraiser, the beadle)
       talk down to you; a rat-man or a shit-golem wouldn't notice or care. (Reachable in play:
       gamble the bones down to the floor — the witless ending is an EVENT now, not a hard floor —
       or build a fool at character-creation. INT 1 is a livable state, not an instant death.)
     • "sharp" (INT ≥ 10): the deep's tricks show their seams.
   Gate prose with setup.isSimple() / setup.isDim() / setup.isSharp() (CUMULATIVE thresholds —
   isDim is true in the simple range too, so the dim beats still fire at the floor; a passage
   with BOTH a simple and a dim variant checks isSimple FIRST). setup.mind() = the exclusive tier. */
setup.MIND_SIMPLE_AT = 1;   /* INT <= this (the floor): smart NPCs talk down to you, replacing their dialogue */
setup.MIND_DIM_AT = 5;      /* INT <= this reads as "dim" (you've lost real ground from base 7; includes simple) */
setup.MIND_SHARP_AT = 10;   /* INT >= this reads as "sharp" (the deep's tricks show their seams) */
setup.playerInt = function () { var s = State.variables.scores; return (s && s.int != null) ? s.int : 7; };
setup.mind = function () { var i = setup.playerInt(); return (i <= setup.MIND_SIMPLE_AT) ? "simple" : ((i <= setup.MIND_DIM_AT) ? "dim" : ((i >= setup.MIND_SHARP_AT) ? "sharp" : "dull")); };
setup.isSimple = function () { return setup.playerInt() <= setup.MIND_SIMPLE_AT; };  /* INT 1: smart NPCs condescend (replaces their dialogue) */
setup.isDim = function () { return setup.playerInt() <= setup.MIND_DIM_AT; };         /* INT ≤ 5: dim or worse (incl. simple) — the reaction beats */
setup.isSharp = function () { return setup.playerInt() >= setup.MIND_SHARP_AT; };

/* ---- CHARACTER CREATION (owner 2026-06-27): the player distributes the DEFAULT character's
   own point total across the six abilities. Budget = 6 × baseScore(1) (= 42 at L1; all-sevens
   IS today's default, so an untouched "Begin" is backward-compatible). Min 1 per stat (INT 1
   drops you straight into the "simple" tier); max CC_MAX. The chosen spread is stored as per-stat
   DELTAS from the default base in persistent memory ("build") — set ONCE, carried across lives
   (marks then layer on top), wiped only on a true fresh start (StoryInit / forgetMarks).
   playerScores folds it into the LEVEL-scaling base, so the spread is preserved AND grows. ---- */
setup.CC_MAX = 14;   /* per-stat ceiling at creation (mod +2 — gifted, not breaking; the 42-pt budget already bounds spikes) */
setup.CC_STATS = [
    { key: "str", label: "STRENGTH",     blurb: "the strength in your arms and back",
      does: "how often your blows land, and how deep" },
    { key: "dex", label: "DEXTERITY",    blurb: "the quickness in your hands and feet",
      does: "your armour, and your chance to get away" },
    { key: "con", label: "CONSTITUTION", blurb: "the toughness that keeps you on your feet",
      does: "your vigour — and nothing else feeds it; set it low and you wake frail" },
    { key: "int", label: "INTELLIGENCE", blurb: "the wit you think with — and the thing the deep most likes to take",
      does: "how plainly the world deals with you, and the fuel for what magic you learn" },
    { key: "wis", label: "WISDOM",       blurb: "the sense that smells a wrong thing coming",
      does: "what you notice before it's on you" },
    { key: "cha", label: "CHARISMA",     blurb: "the way people warmed to you, or didn't",
      does: "how others take to you — though little down here turns on it yet" }
];
setup.ccDescribe = function (v) {
    if (v <= 1) { return "next to nothing"; }
    if (v <= 4) { return "poor"; }
    if (v <= 6) { return "below the common run"; }
    if (v === 7) { return "ordinary"; }
    if (v <= 9) { return "better than most"; }
    if (v <= 13) { return "gifted"; }
    return "rare in any life";
};
setup.hasBuild = function () { return recall("build", null) !== null; };
setup.commitBuild = function () {
    var V = State.variables, a = V.ccAssign || {}, b1 = setup.baseScore(1), build = {};
    setup.STATS.forEach(function (st) { build[st] = (a[st] != null ? a[st] : b1) - b1; });
    memorize("build", build);
    V.hp = null;                 /* re-heal to the new CON-derived max */
    setup.recomputePlayer();
};

/* ===== THE VICES — the addiction ledger (owner 2026-07-20) ==========================
   Every corrupting CONSUMABLE feeds an ADDICTION, tallied per-substance in $addiction
   (id -> intensity). The prose has long promised plural vices ("the cheese, a smoke"); this
   is the ledger that finally makes them real, and the frame the owner drew: each transform
   class gets a food (rat=the cheese, pig=the trough/slop, filth=sewer-brew) that hooks you
   toward it. THE RULE (owner): all of them are kept, but you only feel the CALL of the
   STRONGEST — the dominant vice is the one whose craving finds you out in the world. A
   different one can SEIZE dominance only by strictly EXCEEDING the reigning tally (feed it
   over the top — "spam it over ... if you needed to"), so a player being COMPELLED by one
   master (the cheese, which past mostly-rat eats without asking) can deliberately drown it
   under another (drink brew until brew rules) — trading one leash for a lesser one, and
   paying in the second vice's own coin to do it. Ties keep the incumbent: the override is a
   real, paid effort, not a coin-flip. Competing addictions thus fail GRACEFULLY — never two
   calls at once, always exactly the loudest. Cheese is the first tenant (folded in below),
   sewer-brew the second (THE STILL, further down); slop / a smoke are one-liners from here. */
setup.ADDICTIONS = {
    cheese: { id: "cheese", name: "the cheese", cls: "rat",   crave: "ratcraving",     nag: 5, dose: 5 },
    brew:   { id: "brew",   name: "sewer-brew", cls: "filth", crave: "brewwithdrawal", nag: 6, dose: 5, compelAt: 30 },
    slop:   { id: "slop",   name: "pig-slop",   cls: "pig",   crave: "slopcraving",    nag: 5, dose: 5 },
    /* THE GLOW — the smoke vice (owner 2026-07-20; Phase 0 of HANDOFF-SMOKE-CREATURES.md). The
       back-alley barkers' glowing smoke, made a real tenant. Feeds FILTH for now (smoke = the
       air-phase of filth; Phase 1 re-points it to a 4th "smoke" class if it earns one). It is the
       ODD vice: the others concentrate — a limb turns, you get a claw, a build. The glow DIFFUSES
       (setup.drawSmoke) — a thin film of filth across several segments at once, no single limb
       turning. You don't become a thing; you become vaguer. Pure loss, no build — dispersal's whole
       point. Bait = calm / the ache eased (analgesia — the barker's high, an opium-den reading).
       Faucet: the back alleys (L6) + the smoke creatures' den off the still. Compels when deep in it. */
    smoke:  { id: "smoke",  name: "the glow",   cls: "filth", crave: "smokecraving",   nag: 5, dose: 5, compelAt: 30 }
};
/* recompute the reigning dominant id from the tallies (argmax; the incumbent wins ties, so
   dominance only changes on a STRICT exceed). Cached in $addictionTop so feedAddiction can
   enforce the override rule cheaply and the craving-encounters can read it in O(1). */
setup._recomputeTop = function () {
    var V = State.variables, a = V.addiction || {}, top = V.addictionTop || "", best = (top && a[top]) || 0, id;
    for (id in a) { if (a.hasOwnProperty(id) && a[id] > best) { best = a[id]; top = id; } }
    V.addictionTop = (best > 0) ? top : "";
    return V.addictionTop;
};
setup.addictionLevel = function (id) { var a = State.variables.addiction || {}; return a[id] || 0; };
/* feed a vice: raise its tally, and let it take dominance ONLY by strictly exceeding the
   reigning master (the paid "push it over"). Returns the new tally. */
setup.feedAddiction = function (id, amt) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.addiction) { V.addiction = {}; }
    V.addiction[id] = (V.addiction[id] || 0) + (amt || 0);
    var top = V.addictionTop || "";
    if (!top || V.addiction[id] > (V.addiction[top] || 0)) { V.addictionTop = id; }
    return V.addiction[id];
};
setup.dominantAddiction = function () { return State.variables.addictionTop || setup._recomputeTop(); };
/* the vice whose CALL you feel: the dominant one, but only once it is past its nag floor (a
   single taste does not yet rule you). "" = no call at all. The craving ENCOUNTERS gate on
   this, so exactly the loudest addiction ever nags — the graceful-failure rule, centralised. */
setup.craving = function () {
    var top = setup.dominantAddiction();
    if (!top) { return ""; }
    var meta = setup.ADDICTIONS[top];
    return (meta && setup.addictionLevel(top) >= meta.nag) ? top : "";
};
setup.brewCompelled = function () { return setup.addictionLevel("brew") >= (setup.ADDICTIONS.brew.compelAt || 30); };
setup.smokeCompelled = function () { return setup.addictionLevel("smoke") >= (setup.ADDICTIONS.smoke.compelAt || 30); };   /* deep in the glow: the lungs draw on their own */
/* THE GLOW — the smoke vice's consumable (owner 2026-07-20). Distinct from every other food: it does
   NOT concentrate into one turning limb. It DIFFUSES — a thin film of filth worked into SEVERAL
   segments at once (dispersal), so the overall meter climbs but no single part turns; you go vaguer all
   over instead of sprouting a claw. Bait = the ache eased (a small heal — analgesia, the opium-den
   calm), less than the brew/cheese. No mana (unlike brew/cheese — the glow is detachment, not the
   Word). Feeds the smoke addiction. In Phase 0 the corruption is "filth"; Phase 1 re-points to "smoke". */
setup.drawSmoke = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    var heal = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);                       /* 2-4 HP — the ache eases (the bait), thinner than the other vices */
    var each = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2);                       /* 1-2 filth into EACH touched segment */
    var segs = setup.SEGMENTS.slice(), n = 3, touched = [];             /* spread across 3 segments — diffuse, not concentrated */
    for (var i = 0; i < n && segs.length; i++) {
        var s = segs.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * segs.length), 1)[0];
        setup.corrupt(s, "filth", each);
        touched.push(s);
    }
    V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + heal);
    setup.feedAddiction("smoke", setup.ADDICTIONS.smoke.dose);
    return { heal: heal, each: each, n: touched.length, total: each * touched.length, compelled: setup.smokeCompelled() };
};
/* THE SCATTER-TOLL (owner 2026-07-20) — you cannot DESTROY smoke, only give it back to the air, and the
   air is what you are breathing. Scattering a shadow-person (winning the Guttering fight) means taking
   some of it IN — a GUARANTEED diffuse corruption on the WIN, so a well-equipped player who ends the
   fight in three rounds still walks out a little more dispersed. This is the load-bearing half of "you
   can win and still lose yourself": the in-fight idmg scales with how long you struggle, but the toll is
   the floor under it. No heal, and NO addiction feed — breathing it in a scrap is not the same CHOICE as
   drawing the glow, so the vice stays opt-in (unlike the rats' forced cheese). Phase 0 corruption = filth. */
setup.scatterToll = function () {
    var V = State.variables, each = Math.max(1, 2 - setup.identityResist("filth")), n = 3, segs = setup.SEGMENTS.slice(), touched = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < n && segs.length; i++) {
        var s = segs.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * segs.length), 1)[0];
        setup.corrupt(s, "filth", each);
        touched.push(s);
    }
    return { each: each, n: touched.length, total: each * touched.length };
};
/* migrate/heal: build $addiction if a save predates the ledger, seeding cheese from the
   legacy $cheeseTasted flag so an already-hooked save still feels the pull. Idempotent. */
setup.healAddiction = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.addiction || typeof V.addiction !== "object") { V.addiction = {}; }
    if (V.cheeseTasted && !(V.addiction.cheese > 0)) { V.addiction.cheese = setup.ADDICTIONS.cheese.nag; }
    if (V.addictionTop == null) { V.addictionTop = ""; }
    setup._recomputeTop();
};

/* ===== THE RAT PATH — transformative cheese (owner 2026-06-18) =====================
   Rat was the dead third of the body: pig had 27 corruption sources, filth 32, RAT ZERO — you
   could only fall into rat by LOSING to rat-things, never choose it, so the +DEX / clawing-flurry
   / rat-kin build was unwalkable. The cheese is the on-ramp. Food-as-corruption already feeds you
   PIG at the carnival (TheConfectioner / TheButchersStall: heal a little, rub the class in); the
   stinky-cheese pallet in the sewer (TheLarder, L1) is the RAT twin of that — the bait is hunger
   (it heals HP), the cost is the rat working into you, and it COMPOSES with the kin event: cheese
   -> rat -> the sewer rats stop seeing prey and see family. ratLimbs/ratLoad measure how far gone
   you are; past mostly-rat the craving COMPELS (owner) — the body eats before you decide. */
setup.ratLimbs = function () { return setup.classLimbs("rat"); };       /* delegates to the general whole-body read */
setup.ratLoad  = function () { return setup.classLoad("rat"); };        /* average rat-corruption across the six segments, 0..100 */
setup.cheeseCompelled = function () { return setup.ratLimbs() >= 3; };   /* mostly-rat: the body eats on its own */
/* ONE helping: the cheese heals (the bait) and works rat into a random segment (the cost). The
   rattier you already are, the deeper each helping bites — the body converts what it is becoming
   faster. Arms $cheeseTasted (which lets the craving find you out in the sewer, the recurring pull). */
setup.eatCheese = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    var heal = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);                        /* 3-6 HP back — the bait */
    var bite = 5 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4) + setup.ratLimbs();     /* 5-8 rat, + the pull of every limb already turned */
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random();
    V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + heal);
    var stage = setup.corrupt(seg, "rat", bite);
    var mana = setup.restoreMana(3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3));     /* the vice feeds the Word too (0 unless learned) */
    V.cheeseTasted = true;
    setup.feedAddiction("cheese", setup.ADDICTIONS.cheese.dose);         /* the ledger: a nibble deepens the cheese habit */
    return { heal: heal, bite: bite, seg: seg, stage: stage, mana: mana, compelled: setup.cheeseCompelled() };
};
/* bedding down in the rats' nest among the pallet: a real rest (heal to FULL — the bait) while
   they groom you into one of their own in your sleep (a deeper rat bite — the cost). */
setup.ratNestRest = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    V.hp = V.maxhp;
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), bite = 6 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5);   /* 6-10 rat */
    var stage = setup.corrupt(seg, "rat", bite);
    var mana = (V.maxmana || 0) - (V.mana || 0); setup.restoreMana(mana);           /* a true rest fills the well too */
    V.cheeseTasted = true;
    setup.feedAddiction("cheese", setup.ADDICTIONS.cheese.dose + 2);     /* a whole night among them hooks deeper than a nibble */
    return { seg: seg, bite: bite, stage: stage, mana: mana };
};
/* THE CURDWORKS — the rat JOB that cures the cheese (owner 2026-07-20; the rat column's JOB — the LAST
   cell of the food×class matrix, the twin of the still). The rats have built a whole curing operation
   around the fallen pallet: wheels aging in the warm dark, rinds washed in the sewer-wash, the ripening
   tended (cave-aging, casu marzu, cheese-mites — real, and foul). Poorly paid in COIN — a cheese-cave is
   not a bank — so, like the still, it pays in what it MAKES: take your wage in the WHEEL. Two vectors
   kept distinct: plain LABOUR corrupts the BODY (rat — the wash, the reek, the mites in the skin); only
   the in-kind wage (a cured round, setup.eatCheese) feeds the cheese ADDICTION. Work the vice's source,
   get paid in the vice. Matches the tavern bar-work / the still (voluntary room-job; no passTime; one
   linkreplace per visit rate-limits it). */
setup.CHEESE_WAGE = { light: [1, 2], hard: [3, 5] };   /* coin ranges — below the topside market (a poor cave) */
setup.cheeseShift = function (mode) {
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), out = { mode: mode, seg: seg };
    if (mode === "light") {
        out.rat = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);                         /* 2-4 */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "rat", out.rat);
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2));        /* 1-2 — a cheese-cave is not a bank */
    } else if (mode === "hard") {
        out.rat = 5 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);                         /* 5-8 — down in the wash and the mites */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "rat", out.rat);
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3));        /* 3-5 — still under the topside wage */
    } else { /* inkind — paid in the wheel: the hook. You still worked the shift (the reek), AND you eat your wage. */
        out.rat = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2);                         /* 2-3 labour rat — the curing gets into you */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "rat", out.rat);
        out.ration = setup.eatCheese();                                      /* a cured round as wages — feeds the cheese vice + heals + arms the craving */
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : 0);             /* a token coin, if that — coin's for topside */
    }
    return out;
};

/* ===== THE STILL — sewer-brew, the filth vice (owner 2026-07-20) ====================
   The rats have their pallet and the pig court its trough; the FILTH has its DRINK. Down in
   the wet the deep runs a still and sells what it draws off the sewer warm across the
   Hellmouth Inn's taps: SEWER-BREW. Third mouth of the food-as-corruption engine
   (cheese->rat, slop/trough->pig, brew->filth). The bait is Dutch courage — it steadies a
   fresh gut and wells the Word — the cost is the filth settling into that same gut, deeper
   the more of the deep you already carry (mirrors eatCheese scaling with ratLimbs). Bought
   with COIN, unlike the barkeep's free belonging-cup (which is PIG); feeds the "brew" vice. */
setup.SEWERBREW_PRICE = 3;
/* one measure. potency k scales BOTH the bite and the dose — the drinking-contest pours a big
   one (k>1). Heals a little (bait), works filth into the gut (cost), wells mana, feeds brew. */
setup.drinkBrew = function (potency) {
    var V = State.variables, k = potency || 1;
    var heal = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);                                    /* 2-4 vigor — the steadying */
    var bite = Math.round((4 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3)) * k) + setup.classLimbs("filth");  /* filth into the gut, deeper the filthier you already are */
    V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + heal);
    var stage = setup.corrupt("torso", "filth", bite);
    var mana = setup.restoreMana(2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3));                 /* the vice feeds the Word too (0 unless learned) */
    setup.feedAddiction("brew", Math.round(setup.ADDICTIONS.brew.dose * k));
    return { heal: heal, bite: bite, seg: "torso", stage: stage, mana: mana, level: setup.addictionLevel("brew") };
};
/* THE DRINKING CONTEST (owner 2026-07-20): a challenger cons you into a bout for coin. An EASY
   con check — but the cruelty is the payoff table is INVERTED. WIN and you drank the whole
   contest to do it: you take the purse AND the big dose (brew rules you fastest). LOSE and you
   only had the one measure — a smaller forfeit, and no coin. So the better you hold your drink,
   the harder you are hooked; the coin is bait, not reward (EV: contest is a WORSE coin faucet
   than honest bar-work — see docs/COMBAT.md "The drinking contest"). No ante — the deep does
   not want your coin, it wants YOU; only your flesh is staked. */
setup.CONTEST_DC = 8;                 /* easy — CON is exactly the stat that should win a drinking bout */
setup.CONTEST_PRIZE = 7;              /* the purse (before coinrot); + random(0,2) */
setup.CONTEST_WIN_POTENCY = 2.5;      /* winning = drinking the whole contest — the big dose */
setup.CONTEST_LOSE_POTENCY = 1;       /* losing = you only had the one */
/* once you are mostly-filth the bout stops being offered — nobody bets against the barrel you
   have become — which also caps any attempt to farm the purse (you turn filth long before it pays). */
setup.contestOffered = function () { return setup.classLimbs("filth") < 4; };
setup.drinkingContest = function () {
    var won = setup.statCheck("con", setup.CONTEST_DC);   /* stashes setup.lastCheck for checkMargin() */
    var margin = setup.checkMargin();
    var res = setup.drinkBrew(won ? setup.CONTEST_WIN_POTENCY : setup.CONTEST_LOSE_POTENCY);
    var prize = won ? setup.gainCoins(setup.CONTEST_PRIZE + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3)) : 0;
    return { won: won, margin: margin, prize: prize, bite: res.bite, heal: res.heal, mana: res.mana, level: res.level };
};
/* the DRY pang — brew-withdrawal out where there is nothing to drink. The still is a place you
   cannot carry; away from the taps the body just gnaws at itself for the missing measure, and a
   little filth settles in to fill the absence (the deep is patient). Far lighter than a drink —
   holding out still beats giving in — but being hooked bleeds you even when you resist. */
setup.brewPang = function () {
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), bite = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2);   /* 2-3 filth — a minor bleed, nothing like a measure */
    var stage = setup.corrupt(seg, "filth", bite);
    return { seg: seg, bite: bite, stage: stage };
};
/* THE STILL — the filth JOB that makes the brew (owner 2026-07-20, the matrix's filth column: FOOD
   + JOB). Down in the wet you cook the sewer's own water into the drink the tavern sells. Grueling,
   and POORLY paid in coin — a still is not a bank — so its standing offer is the owner's
   payment-in-kind: take your wage in the DRINK. Two vectors kept distinct (the twentieth-letter
   thesis): LABOR marks the BODY with `filth` (the fumes, the mash on your skin); only the in-kind
   wage feeds the brew ADDICTION (consuming hooks the vice). The spiral made literal — work the
   vice's source, get paid in the vice. Matches the tavern bar-work (voluntary room-job; no passTime;
   one of each linkreplace per visit rate-limits it). */
setup.STILL_WAGE = { light: [1, 2], hard: [3, 5] };   /* coin ranges — deliberately below the bar (poor still) */
setup.stillShift = function (mode) {
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), out = { mode: mode, seg: seg };
    if (mode === "light") {
        out.filth = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);                       /* 2-4 */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "filth", out.filth);
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2));        /* 1-2 — a still is not a bank */
    } else if (mode === "hard") {
        out.filth = 5 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);                       /* 5-8 — the fumes off the mash */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "filth", out.filth);
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3));        /* 3-5 — still under the bar's wage */
    } else { /* inkind — paid in the drink: the hook. You still worked the shift (fumes), AND you drink your wage. */
        out.filth = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2);                       /* 2-3 labor filth — you breathed it all shift */
        setup.corrupt(seg, "filth", out.filth);
        out.ration = setup.drinkBrew(2);                                     /* a double ration as wages — feeds brew (dominance!), + the drink's bait */
        out.coin = setup.gainCoins(Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : 0);             /* a token coin, if that — coin's for them upstairs */
    }
    return out;
};

/* ===== THE PENS — pig-slop, the pig vice (owner 2026-07-20, the pig column's FOOD) ==========
   The rats have their pallet and the filth its still; the PIG has its TROUGH. Down in the Belly the
   taken are fattened for the row — the Breeder already tells you so ("you'll keep, a while ... rushing
   spoils the meat"), and the slop that fattens them will fatten you. Third food of the matrix
   (cheese→rat, brew→filth, slop→pig; pig is a well-sourced class, so this DEEPENS the pig-court build
   rather than opening a dead one). BAIT: the cheapest calories in hell — free food, worth most when
   you are hurt and broke (like the cheese, but pig). COST: pig worked into the GUT, deeper the more
   pig you already are. Eaten at the trough in `TheHolding` (the pens); the craving forages the pig
   band once tasted. COMPELS at pigLimbs≥3 — you go to the trough the way the farrow do. And there, at
   the pens, the fattening turns on YOU: the capture (setup.pennedFatten). */
setup.pigLimbs = function () { return setup.classLimbs("pig"); };       /* how-far-gone, in TURNED pig segments */
setup.pigLoad  = function () { return setup.classLoad("pig"); };
setup.slopCompelled = function () { return setup.pigLimbs() >= 3; };    /* mostly-pig: you feed on your own */
setup.eatSlop = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    var heal = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);                        /* 3-6 HP — the cheapest calories in hell */
    var bite = 5 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4) + setup.pigLimbs();     /* 5-8 pig + the pull of every limb already turned */
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random();                                   /* random seg (like the cheese): the trough spreads the pig, so slop ALONE can reach the compulsion */
    V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + heal);
    var stage = setup.corrupt(seg, "pig", bite);
    setup.feedAddiction("slop", setup.ADDICTIONS.slop.dose);
    return { heal: heal, bite: bite, seg: seg, stage: stage, compelled: setup.slopCompelled() };
};
/* THE FATTENING (the pens-only capture). Once you feed at the trough mostly-pig, the pen-boars stop
   seeing a hand come to work and see stock come to feed — and the belly finishes what it starts.
   Heavy pig across two–three segments (they fatten you), and you come to at half vigor, penned, and
   claw back out heavier and more theirs. If it completes a full-body turn, PassageHeader's global
   corruption check tips you into EndingBecome as usual — no extra wiring. The trough also deepens
   the slop habit (you fed, hard). Returns the marks for prose. */
setup.pennedFatten = function () {
    var V = State.variables, segs = setup.SEGMENTS.slice(), n = 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 2), marks = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < n && segs.length; i++) {
        var s = segs.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * segs.length), 1)[0];
        var amt = 8 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 6);                     /* 8-13 pig — they finish you a little */
        setup.corrupt(s, "pig", amt);
        marks.push({ seg: s, amt: amt });
    }
    setup.feedAddiction("slop", setup.ADDICTIONS.slop.nag);
    V.hp = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(V.maxhp / 2));                          /* you come to, fattened, mauled but alive */
    return { marks: marks };
};

/* ===== MAGIC — the Word (owner-goal 2026-06-18) ==========================================
   Magic is, mostly, a COMBAT skill drawn out of the deep itself. MANA is the channel, and its
   ceiling rises with your MAGIC LEVEL (= your character level, once you've learned) AND with your
   CORRUPTION — the more of the deep is worked into you, the more of it you can call back out. So
   casting, which corrupts you, slowly widens its own well: the vice. Mana refills at a true rest,
   and (the owner's hook) by feeding an ADDICTION — the cheese, a smoke — the same vices that taint
   you. A cast lands about TWICE as hard as a weapon strike at the same level (it auto-finds the
   flesh and ignores blunt/edged armor), but it CORRUPTS BOTH: a taint of the floor's own class
   settles in your HEAD each time, and the deep you pour through the victim eats its guard away (its
   AC sloughs). Learned three ways, all live: a CHARACTER (the rat Cantor at TheLarder), an ITEM
   (the Drowned Catechism at TheArchive), and a LOCATION (the named-script on the Hellmouth arch).
   Tuning knobs are SPELL_DIE / SPELL_FLAT (verified ~2× in tools/combat-sim.mjs MAGIC row). ====== */
setup.SPELL_DIE = 8;     /* base cast rolls one dN (the variance) ... */
setup.SPELL_FLAT = 2;    /* ... + this per magic level (the scaling). Tuned so a cast ≈ 2× a weapon strike at level (sim) */
setup.MANA_PER_LEVEL = 4;
/* magic level = character level once learned, else 0 (no magic). Leveling lifts mana AND power. */
setup.magicLevel = function () { return State.variables.magicKnown ? (State.variables.level || 1) : 0; };
/* mana ceiling: MANA_PER_LEVEL per magic level + 1 per 10 corruption (the deep in you is the fuel). */
setup.maxMana = function () {
    if (!State.variables.magicKnown) { return 0; }
    return setup.magicLevel() * setup.MANA_PER_LEVEL + Math.floor(Math.clamp(State.variables.corruption || 0, 0, 100) / 10);
};
/* keep $maxmana in step + clamp current mana. Called from recomputePlayer (guarded there, since
   this script-block defines it AFTER the run-block's first recompute fires at StoryInit). */
setup.recomputeMana = function () {
    var V = State.variables;
    V.maxmana = setup.maxMana();
    if (V.mana == null) { V.mana = 0; }
    if (!V.magicKnown) { V.mana = 0; }
    if (V.mana > V.maxmana) { V.mana = V.maxmana; }
};
/* restore mana (a rest, or an addiction hit). No-op unless magic is known. Returns amount restored. */
setup.restoreMana = function (n) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (!V.magicKnown || n <= 0) { return 0; }
    var before = V.mana || 0;
    V.mana = Math.min(V.maxmana, before + n);
    return V.mana - before;
};
/* the Hellmouth arch (the LOCATION source) sits at the spawn, so it must NOT hand you magic on turn
   one. The incised script is unreadable UNLESS you're sharp enough to find its sense unaided (a
   passive WIS/perception check — reachable by level or WIS-marks, not by a fresh L1) OR you've HEARD
   from someone that it can be read (the newly-taken at TheArrivals plant $heardOfWord). Either opens
   the trace-it-and-learn action. DC tunable. */
setup.PERCEIVE_INSCRIPTION_DC = 11;
setup.passivePerception = function () { return 10 + setup.mod((State.variables.scores || { wis: 7 }).wis); };
setup.canReadInscription = function () {
    return !!State.variables.heardOfWord || setup.passivePerception() >= setup.PERCEIVE_INSCRIPTION_DC;
};
/* the privy roll (the ITEM source, TheStallRow) is a grimoire in disguise — you won't think to READ
   printed bog-paper unless you're sharp enough to clock the script (the same passive perception) OR
   the midway demons tipped you off ($heardOfGrimoire). Separate from the stall being physically free
   (a 20% per-visit roll in the room itself). Parallels canReadInscription. */
setup.canReadGrimoire = function () {
    return !!State.variables.heardOfGrimoire || setup.passivePerception() >= setup.PERCEIVE_INSCRIPTION_DC;
};

/* THE KAPPA BOW (TheBathhouse, L4). Folklore: a kappa must bow back when bowed to, and bowing tips
   the water-dish off its crown, undoing it. The catch is YOURS: simple human courtesy needs a body
   that can still bend like a person's — so the deep worked into you locks the graceful path. Below
   BOW_CORRUPTION_MAX you can manage the bow (it bows back, the dish spills, it folds); at/above it the
   thing in you will not bend and the courtesy curdles into threat → a fight. The spilled dish holds
   the only clean water in hell, so either way you best it, DISH_CLEANSE of the deep washes off. */
setup.BOW_CORRUPTION_MAX = 50;
setup.DISH_CLEANSE = 12;
setup.composedEnoughToBow = function () { return (State.variables.corruption || 0) < setup.BOW_CORRUPTION_MAX; };

/* learn the Word. source ∈ "cantor" (a character) / "grimoire" (an item) / "wall" (a location) —
   all three set the one flag and fill the well. Returns false if you already know it. */
setup.learnMagic = function (source) {
    var V = State.variables;
    if (V.magicKnown) { return false; }
    V.magicKnown = true;
    V.magicSource = source || "the deep";
    setup.recomputeMana();
    V.mana = V.maxmana;                 /* you come away with a full well */
    return true;
};

/* THE SPELL BOOK. Each spell is a combat action: a mana cost, a power MULTIPLE of the base cast
   (so leveling — which lifts the base — lifts every spell), how hard it taints YOU (`self`, head)
   and how hard it eats the VICTIM (`bite`, AC). `behavior`: "bolt" = the aimed foe; "sweep" = all
   living foes. Higher spells unlock with magic level. */
setup.SPELLS = [
    { id: "hex",    name: "The Hex",         cost: 3, behavior: "bolt",  power: 1.0, self: 3, bite: 1, minLevel: 1,
      flavor: "you speak the close wet syllable and the deep answers through the thing in front of you" },
    { id: "wither", name: "Withering Word",  cost: 5, behavior: "bolt",  power: 1.5, self: 4, bite: 2, minLevel: 3,
      flavor: "a longer word, one that costs a human mouth to hold, and it rots whatever it lands on" },
    { id: "rot",    name: "Spreading Rot",   cost: 7, behavior: "sweep", power: 0.7, self: 6, bite: 1, minLevel: 4,
      flavor: "you breathe the Word out flat across the whole rank and let the deep have all of them at once" }
];
/* base cast power at the current magic level, before a spell's `power` multiple. Scales PURELY with
   magic level (not the diminished body stats — this power is the deep's, not yours). Auto-hits and
   ignores type resistance, which is what makes a cast worth ~2× a weapon strike (sim MAGIC row). */
setup.spellBase = function () {
    var L = setup.magicLevel();
    if (L <= 0) { return 0; }
    return setup.d(setup.SPELL_DIE) + L * setup.SPELL_FLAT;     /* 1dN (variance) + flat·level (scaling) */
};
setup.knownSpells = function () {
    if (!State.variables.magicKnown) { return []; }
    var L = setup.magicLevel();
    return setup.SPELLS.filter(function (s) { return L >= (s.minLevel || 1); });
};
setup.castableSpells = function () {
    var mana = State.variables.mana || 0;
    return setup.knownSpells().filter(function (s) { return mana >= s.cost; });
};
/* can the player open the Cast menu at all? (knows magic, can act, has a spell it can pay for) */
setup.canCastAny = function () {
    return !!State.variables.magicKnown && setup.canAttack() && setup.castableSpells().length > 0;
};
/* cast a spell. Spends mana; deals spellBase×power (auto-hit, no type mult); CORRUPTS THE VICTIM
   (its AC sloughs by `bite`, floored at 6) and THE CASTER (`self` of the floor's class, in the head).
   Returns the log clause. */
setup.castSpell = function (spId) {
    var V = State.variables;
    var sp = setup.SPELLS.filter(function (x) { return x.id === spId; })[0] || setup.SPELLS[0];
    if ((V.mana || 0) < sp.cost) { return "The well in you is dry — you cannot hold " + sp.name + "."; }
    V.mana -= sp.cost;
    var alive = setup.aliveEnemies();
    var focus = (V.enemies[V.target] && V.enemies[V.target].hp > 0) ? V.enemies[V.target] : alive[0];
    var log = "You cast " + sp.name + " — " + sp.flavor + ".", kills = "";
    function strike(e) {
        var idx = V.enemies.indexOf(e);
        var dmg = Math.max(1, Math.round(setup.spellBase() * sp.power));
        kills += setup.hurtEnemy(idx, dmg);
        if (e.hp > 0) {                                   /* corrupt the VICTIM — the deep eats its guard */
            e.corrupted = (e.corrupted || 0) + sp.bite;
            e.ac = Math.max(6, e.ac - sp.bite);
        }
        log += " The Word finds " + setup.theName(e.name) + " for " + dmg + (e.hp > 0 ? " — its guard sloughs where it lands" : "") + ".";
    }
    if (sp.behavior === "sweep") { alive.forEach(strike); } else if (focus) { strike(focus); }
    if (kills) { log += " —" + kills; }
    /* corrupt the CASTER: a taint of this floor's own class settles in the head — and widens, a
       little, the very well the Word is drawn from. (Floor = where the fight is, not "Combat".) */
    var stage = setup.corrupt("head", setup.classOnFloor(V.combatOrigin), sp.self);
    log += " Speaking it leaves its mark behind your eyes" + (stage === "turning" || stage === "turned" ? ", and you feel it taking hold" : "") + ".";
    return log;
};

/* ===== MULTI-ENEMY COMBAT — strings live here (raw JS, no operator-word desugaring) =====
   The combat SCREEN + six actions (owner 2026-06-05). SPECIALS are sweep attacks hitting
   ALL living enemies for slightly-reduced damage; usable a number of times per fight equal
   to the player's LEVEL. Form specials appear once you've grown a limb of that class. */
/* SPECIALS (owner 2026-06-07): two sources. WEAPON-TYPE specials (wreq = the weapon types that
   grant them) and FORM specials (req = a grown limb-class). `behavior`: "sweep" = hit all foes ×mult;
   "stun" = one foe ×mult + it loses its next turn; "flurry" = several quick strikes on one foe ×mult;
   "cleave" = the two toughest living foes ×mult. N uses per fight = level. */
setup.SPECIALS = [
    /* weapon-type specials */
    { id: "sweep",  name: "Sweeping blow",  behavior: "sweep",  mult: 0.6,  wreq: ["sword", "spear"],
      flavor: "a wide arc that catches the whole rank" },
    { id: "cleave", name: "Cleaving blow",  behavior: "cleave", mult: 0.85, wreq: ["axe"],
      flavor: "a heavy chop that bites clean through into the next of them" },
    { id: "crush",  name: "Crushing blow",  behavior: "stun",   mult: 1.3,  wreq: ["hammer"],
      flavor: "a downward smash meant to put something on the floor and keep it there" },
    { id: "snag",   name: "Snag and haul",  behavior: "stun",   mult: 1.1,  wreq: ["hook"],
      flavor: "the hook bites and hauls, and the thing folds and cannot right itself" },
    { id: "flurry", name: "Knife flurry",   behavior: "flurry", mult: 0.7,  wreq: ["dagger"],
      flavor: "three quick cuts before it can answer even one" },
    /* form (grown-limb) specials — sweep the pack */
    { id: "claw",  name: "Clawing flurry",  behavior: "sweep",  mult: 0.66, req: "rat",   dtype: "edged",
      flavor: "the rat in your hands taking over, a blur of black-clawed strikes" },
    { id: "gore",  name: "Goring charge",   behavior: "sweep",  mult: 0.72, req: "pig",   dtype: "blunt",
      flavor: "the pig's weight bulling through them, tusk-first" },
    { id: "lash",  name: "Filth lash",      behavior: "sweep",  mult: 0.62, req: "filth", dtype: "blunt",
      flavor: "a slung rope of your own dissolving self flung across them" }
];
/* placeholder portrait glyph by mutagen class (covered by real art when img/enemy/ID.png exists) */
setup.CLASS_GLYPH = { rat: "🐀", pig: "🐗", filth: "☣" };

/* ---- EQUIPMENT readout strings (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT) — held here in the raw-JS block
   because some carry operator-words ("coin curdles to rubbish" → "to") that the run-block
   would desugar. Used by the StoryCaption kit panel. ---- */
setup.CURSE_LABEL = {
    autosurrender: "your knees give at the first blow",
    stat_down:     "a strength bled out of you",
    stat_down_all: "all of you diminished",
    nopickup:      "your hands will not close on things",
    coinrot:       "coin curdles to rubbish in your grip",
    irreversible:  "what changes in you cannot change back",
    always_class:  "you only ever turn one way now",
    norun:         "you cannot make yourself run",
    noattack:      "you cannot raise a hand to strike",
    nospeak:       "your voice will not come",
    encounter_up:  "the deep notices you more"
};
setup.activeCurseLabels = function () {
    return setup.curseEntries().map(function (e) { return setup.scarLabel(e); });
};
/* SHORT curse tags for the item brief (so a cursed item READS its specific downside once identified,
   not just "CURSED" — owner 2026-06-07). stat-scars name the stat inline. */
setup.CURSE_TAG = {
    autosurrender: "drops you at the first blow",
    stat_down_all: "−1 all stats",
    nopickup:      "can't take up items",
    coinrot:       "coin rots in hand",
    irreversible:  "no cleansing",
    always_class:  "only ever turns one way",
    norun:         "can't run in combat",
    noattack:      "can't attack",
    nospeak:       "can't speak",
    encounter_up:  "draws the deep's eye"
};
setup.curseTag = function (e) {
    if (e.id === "stat_down") { return "−" + (e.amount || 1) + " " + (e.stat || "str"); }
    return setup.CURSE_TAG[e.id] || e.id;
};
/* a specific label for a curse/scar entry — stat-scars name the stat + amount; the rest use CURSE_LABEL */
setup.scarLabel = function (e) {
    if (e.id === "stat_down") { return "a lasting weakness — your " + (e.stat || "str").toUpperCase() + " is " + (e.amount || 1) + " less, for good"; }
    if (e.id === "stat_down_all") { return "all of you lessened, for good"; }
    return setup.CURSE_LABEL[e.id] || e.id;
};
/* equipped accessories as "slot: name" fragments for the kit panel */
setup.accessoryNotes = function () {
    var V = State.variables, out = [];
    setup.ACCESSORY_SLOTS.forEach(function (slot) {
        var id = V[slot];
        if (id && setup.items[id]) { out.push(slot + ": " + setup.items[id].name); }
    });
    return out;
};

/* an enemy NAME with its definite article, without doubling it when the name already carries
   one (owner 2026-06-17 — "the Glut"/"the drowned" were reading "the the …"). cap=true for
   sentence-start. */
setup.theName = function (name, cap) {
    if (/^(the|a|an) /i.test(name)) { return cap ? name.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + name.slice(1) : name; }
    return (cap ? "The " : "the ") + name;
};
/* apply dmg to enemy index i; bank its spoils if it falls. returns a kill-clause or "". */
setup.hurtEnemy = function (i, dmg) {
    var V = State.variables, e = V.enemies[i];
    e.hp -= dmg;
    if (e.hp <= 0) {
        e.hp = 0;
        V.combatSpoils.coins += (e.coins || 0);
        V.combatSpoils.xp += (e.xp != null ? e.xp : 0);
        return " " + setup.theName(e.name) + " comes apart;";
    }
    return "";
};
/* the player's focused strike on a single target index. returns the log clause. */
setup.playerStrike = function (i) {
    var V = State.variables, e = V.enemies[i];
    if (!e || e.hp <= 0) { return "There is nothing there to hit."; }
    var dtype = setup.playerWeaponType(), wdie = setup.playerWeaponDie(), wkind = setup.playerWeaponKind();
    var strMod = setup.mod(V.scores.str);
    var armPen = Math.max(setup.corruptionPenalty(), setup.limbPenalty("arm"));
    var tmult = setup.typeMult(dtype, e, wkind);
    var roll = setup.attack(strMod - armPen, setup.PLAYER_PROF, e.ac, wdie, strMod);
    if (!roll.hit) {
        return "You roll " + roll.roll + (roll.fumble ? " (a fumble) and your blow goes wide." : " and miss " + setup.theName(e.name) + ".");
    }
    var dmg = Math.max(1, Math.round(roll.dmg * tmult) + setup.itemDamageBonus(e));
    var killed = setup.hurtEnemy(i, dmg);
    var tail = tmult > 1 ? " — it bursts where you hit it" : (tmult < 1 ? " — but the blade barely tells" : "");
    return "You roll " + roll.roll + (roll.crit ? " (a critical) and rend " : " and strike ") + setup.theName(e.name) + " for " + dmg + tail + "." + (killed ? " It comes apart." : "") + setup.weaponTaint();
};
/* a SPECIAL: behavior decides the shape (sweep all / cleave two / stun one / flurry one). spends
   one charge. The aimed enemy ($target) is the focus for single-target behaviors. */
setup.doSpecial = function (spId) {
    var V = State.variables;
    var sp = setup.SPECIALS.filter(function (x) { return x.id === spId; })[0] || setup.SPECIALS[0];
    var dtype = sp.dtype || setup.playerWeaponType(), wdie = setup.playerWeaponDie(), wkind = setup.playerWeaponKind();
    var strMod = setup.mod(V.scores.str);
    var armPen = Math.max(setup.corruptionPenalty(), setup.limbPenalty("arm"));
    var atk = strMod - armPen;
    var log = "You loose a " + sp.name + " — " + sp.flavor + ".", kills = "", landedAny = false;
    function strike(e) {
        var idx = V.enemies.indexOf(e);
        var roll = setup.attack(atk, setup.PLAYER_PROF, e.ac, wdie, strMod);
        if (roll.hit) {
            var dmg = Math.max(1, Math.round(roll.dmg * sp.mult * setup.typeMult(dtype, e, wkind)) + setup.itemDamageBonus(e));
            kills += setup.hurtEnemy(idx, dmg);
            log += " You catch " + setup.theName(e.name) + " for " + dmg + ".";
            landedAny = true;
            return true;
        }
        log += " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " slips it.";
        return false;
    }
    var alive = setup.aliveEnemies();
    var focus = (V.enemies[V.target] && V.enemies[V.target].hp > 0) ? V.enemies[V.target] : alive[0];
    if (sp.behavior === "sweep") {
        alive.forEach(strike);
    } else if (sp.behavior === "cleave") {
        alive.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return b.hp - a.hp; }).slice(0, 2).forEach(strike);
    } else if (sp.behavior === "flurry") {
        for (var k = 0; k < 3 && focus && focus.hp > 0; k++) { strike(focus); }
    } else { /* stun — one foe, and it loses its next turn */
        if (focus) {
            var hit = strike(focus);
            if (hit && focus.hp > 0) { focus.stunned = true; log += " The " + focus.name + " reels — it won't move next."; }
        }
    }
    if (kills) { log += " —" + kills; }
    if (landedAny) { log += setup.weaponTaint(); }   /* the taint takes its wage once per action, not per hit */
    V.specialUses = (V.specialUses || 0) + 1;
    return log;
};
/* use a consumable: apply its effect, remove one from the pack. returns the log clause. */
setup.useItem = function (id) {
    var V = State.variables, it = setup.items[id];
    if (!it) { return "Nothing happens."; }
    var msg = "";
    if (it.heal) {
        var before = V.hp;
        V.hp = Math.min(V.maxhp, V.hp + it.heal);
        msg = "You press the " + it.name + " to your hurts — " + (V.hp - before) + " vigor back.";
    } else {
        msg = "You use the " + it.name + ".";
    }
    var idx = V.inventory.indexOf(id);
    if (idx >= 0) { V.inventory.splice(idx, 1); }
    return msg;
};
/* ===== THE THREAT-READ (review R14) — the canon "consider" check through the game's own
   channel. You can smell ROOMS (room-scent) and the world smells YOU (regard) — but the thing
   squaring up in front of you was the one thing your nose skipped, so the bottom of the curve
   (fresh L1 vs pig-demon: 7%) hit like a trap. threatRead(spec) ranks a fight-offer the way
   tools/combat-sim.mjs ranks it: pack statLevel + 2×hd (the strongest at full weight, the rest
   at half), shifted by the creature's NATURE against the tool in your hand (weakTo/resists ∓2,
   weakTypes/resistTypes ∓2, boss +2), against 3×level + your weapon-die max. Four rungs.
   Calibrated against the 2026-07-02 sim run — holds within one rung across the L1-fists,
   L1-bronze-sword and power-curve tables (<40% win reads "more than you", <~5% reads the
   verdict rung; the Glut reads conservative on purpose — a boss SHOULD smell like leave).
   It is a SMELL, not a stat sheet: coarse by design — it reads potency and nature, and it
   cannot see your armor, your consumables, or your luck. Surfaced by <<scentof>> (widget,
   room-scent band voice). Prose lives HERE (script block — display strings). */
setup.THREAT_SCENT = [
    { tier: "accept",
      one:  "You take its scent without meaning to, and nothing in you tightens. Small. Thin. A smell your body has already ranked and dismissed.",
      many: "You take their scent without meaning to, and nothing in you tightens. Small smells, thin ones, already ranked and dismissed." },
    { tier: "even",
      one:  "It smells like your own weight of trouble — an even reek, the kind you square up to with your feet set and your teeth shut.",
      many: "Together they smell like your own weight of trouble — an even reek, the kind you square up to with your feet set and your teeth shut." },
    { tier: "recoil",
      one:  "Its stink stands over yours the way a bigger animal's does. More than you, says the oldest part of your nose. It has not once lied to you down here.",
      many: "Their stink stands over yours the way a bigger animal's does. More than you, says the oldest part of your nose. It has not once lied to you down here." },
    { tier: "dread",
      one:  "What comes off it is less a smell than a verdict. Every gland you own says leave — whatever it is, it would unmake you.",
      many: "What comes off them is less a smell than a verdict. Every gland you own says leave — whatever they are, they would unmake you." }
];
setup.threatRead = function (spec) {
    var ids = Array.isArray(spec) ? spec : [spec];
    var die = String(setup.playerWeaponDie()).split("d");
    var me = 3 * (State.variables.level || 1) + (parseInt(die[1], 10) || 2);
    var dt = setup.playerWeaponType(), wk = setup.playerWeaponKind();
    var scores = ids.map(function (id) {
        var e = setup.enemies[id]; if (!e) { return 0; }
        var s = e.statLevel + 2 * e.hd;
        if (e.resists === dt) { s += 2; } else if (e.weakTo === dt) { s -= 2; }
        if (wk && e.resistTypes && e.resistTypes.indexOf(wk) >= 0) { s += 2; }
        else if (wk && e.weakTypes && e.weakTypes.indexOf(wk) >= 0) { s -= 2; }
        if (e.boss) { s += 2; }
        return s;
    }).sort(function (a, b) { return b - a; });
    var them = scores[0] || 0;
    for (var i = 1; i < scores.length; i++) { them += Math.ceil(scores[i] / 2); }
    var diff = me - them;
    if (diff >= 0) { return 0; }
    if (diff >= -6) { return 1; }
    if (diff >= -8) { return 2; }
    return 3;
};

/* ===== SIGNATURE MOVES (review R12) — every monster used to fight identically: one
   weapon-die attack per round, forever, which made Guard a dominated button. Now each
   species has ONE move, telegraph-then-payoff: the wind-up SPENDS its attack (the telegraph
   round is your free window), and the payoff AUTO-LANDS next round unless answered —
   Guard blunts it (each move says how), a stun cancels it, Run leaves before it arrives.
   Several take agency ON the turn (the game's whole thesis): held (Run spoken for),
   engulfed (your next action goes to getting out), dragged (the shift's ledger takes your
   name). Prose lives HERE (script block — operator-words in display strings). Each move:
   tele(e) = the wind-up line · land(e, guarding) = apply + narrate the payoff. */
setup.ENEMY_MOVES = {
    /* the pack call — vermin answer vermin; Guard can't stop a sound (stun/kill the caller can) */
    squeal: {
        tele: function (e) { return " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " stops fighting and sets up a shrill, carrying squeal — something answers it, back in the dark."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var V = State.variables;
            if (V.enemies.length < 4) {
                V.enemies.push(setup.combatActor("rat"));
                return " Another demon rat comes boiling out of the runoff, and the fight is one mouth bigger.";
            }
            return " Its call rings down the pipes and dies away — nothing left out there to answer it.";
        }
    },
    /* the filth decides — lose your next action to getting out (Guard keeps your feet) */
    engulf: {
        tele: function (e) { return " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " stops hitting and starts spreading — it draws itself up and out, a slow wave of itself gathering over you."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            if (guarding) { return " The wave of filth breaks over your brace and finds no way in. You keep your feet, and your turn."; }
            State.variables.engulfed = true;
            return " It closes over you like a tide of itself. For a moment the filth decides where your limbs are — you are in it, and your next act belongs to getting out.";
        }
    },
    /* held — the way out is spoken for one round (Guard slips the grip) */
    grapple: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The drowned spreads its swollen hands and wades in close — it means to hold you, not hit you."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            if (guarding) { return " Braced, you slip the sodden grip as it closes, and it gets nothing but your sleeve."; }
            State.variables.held = 1;
            return " It gets its arms around you, waterlogged and impossibly heavy, and leans. The way out is spoken for — you are held.";
        }
    },
    coil: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The drain-crawler pours itself round behind you, pale length gathering into a loop."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            if (guarding) { return " You keep your stance at the loop's centre and it draws tight on nothing."; }
            State.variables.held = 1;
            return " The loop comes tight around your legs, cold as pipework. You are held.";
        }
    },
    pullunder: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The kappa slips low, beak at the waterline, circling for your ankles."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            if (guarding) { return " You brace wide and its webbed grip skates off your stance."; }
            State.variables.held = 1;
            return " It has your ankle and the water has the rest of you — hauled to the edge and held there.";
        }
    },
    /* the drain — it heals from what it bites out of you (Guard halves the bite and starves it) */
    gulp: {
        tele: function (e) { return " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + "'s mouth unmakes itself wider — it has stopped fighting you and started considering you as provisions."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var V = State.variables, dmg = Math.max(1, setup.rollDie(e.weaponDie) + e.dmgMod);
            if (guarding) {
                dmg = Math.max(1, Math.floor(dmg / 2));
                V.hp -= dmg;
                return " Your brace turns the worst of the bite — " + dmg + " through — and it gets no keep from you.";
            }
            V.hp -= dmg;
            e.hp = Math.min(e.maxhp, e.hp + dmg);
            return " It takes its bite out of you — " + dmg + " — and you watch the wound's worth settle into it, its flesh filling where yours went.";
        }
    },
    /* the Guard test — a charge that arrives all at once (double dice); braced, it shears past */
    gore: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The pig-demon drops its head, hooves planting, tusks levelled — the whole mass of it is about to arrive at once."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var V = State.variables, dmg = Math.max(1, setup.rollDie(e.weaponDie) + setup.rollDie(e.weaponDie) + e.dmgMod);
            if (guarding) { dmg = Math.max(1, Math.floor(dmg / 4)); V.hp -= dmg; return " You take the charge on your brace and it shears past — " + dmg + " through, no more."; }
            V.hp -= dmg;
            return " It arrives like a cart. The tusks take you full — " + dmg + " — and the room tilts.";
        }
    },
    manyhands: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The grafted unslings all its arms — the borrowed ones too — and the flail of them starts to build."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var V = State.variables, dmg = Math.max(1, setup.rollDie(e.weaponDie) + setup.rollDie(e.weaponDie) + e.dmgMod);
            if (guarding) { dmg = Math.max(1, Math.floor(dmg / 4)); V.hp -= dmg; return " You wall up and the storm of hands beats itself out on your brace — " + dmg + " through."; }
            V.hp -= dmg;
            return " The flail of borrowed hands arrives from four directions at once — " + dmg + " — no two blows from the same body.";
        }
    },
    /* THE CHORUS (owner 2026-07-20) — the shadow-person's signature, and a miniature of the Phase-3
       plurality horror: the aggregate loosens and speaks with many mouths, and EACH takes a little of
       you to say itself with — identity damage across SEVERAL segments at once. Guard holds your outline
       (fewer segments, less each). No vigor number: this move wounds only the self. */
    chorus: {
        tele: function (e) { return " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " loosens out of its person-shape, and a crowd of voices starts up inside the smoke of it — not quite in unison, not quite words, and every one of them, somehow, yours."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var base = e.idmg || 3, takes = guarding ? 1 : 2, per = guarding ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(base / 2)) : base;
            var segs = setup.SEGMENTS.slice(), hit = [];
            for (var i = 0; i < takes && segs.length; i++) {
                var s = segs.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * segs.length), 1)[0];
                setup.corrupt(s, e.cls, per);
                hit.push(setup.SEG_LABEL[s] || s);
            }
            if (guarding) { return " You brace and hold your outline against the chorus; it still gets a little of you — " + per + " from your " + hit.join(" and ") + " — but you are, mostly, still the one standing here."; }
            return " The chorus speaks you and unspeaks you at once, and each mouth takes a little to say itself with: " + per + " from your " + hit.join(", and " + per + " from your ") + ". For a moment you could not have said, yourself, which of the voices was the one that would have answered to your name.";
        }
    },
    /* the recruiter — a landed drag is a step toward the shift: it claims you for the work */
    drag: {
        tele: function (e) { return " The sty-hand flips its shovel round to the hook end and reaches for your collar — herding, not hurting."; },
        land: function (e, guarding) {
            var V = State.variables;
            if (guarding) { return " You plant your feet and the hook slides off your collar. Not this shift."; }
            V.held = 1;
            if (!V.workStation) { V.workStation = "cage"; }
            V.workOwed = true;
            return " The hook takes your collar and hauls — a step, another, toward the door and the work, and you are held. Somewhere in the Shambles a ledger takes your name: the shift is yours now, whenever the floor collects.";
        }
    }
};

/* THE SMEAR (review R13): winning used to be mechanically sterile — corruption flowed only
   on LOSS or casting, so twenty 1-HP scrapes left you as clean as never being touched, despite
   every enemy carrying a class that canonically rubs off. Now an enemy CRIT (nat 20, ~5% per
   attack — already rolled and narrated) also smears CRIT_SMEAR of its class into one random
   segment. Guard halving a crit halves the smear — Guard's second job. Bounded, avoidable,
   and it makes the win ledger honest: you beat the thing, and you wear a little of it. */
setup.CRIT_SMEAR = 2;
/* IDENTITY DAMAGE (owner 2026-07-20; docs/COMBAT.md → "Poison / identity-damage weapons").
   The smear made WINNING cost a little of the enemy's class — but only on a rare crit. Identity
   damage is the deliberate, primary version, carried by things that wound the SELF instead of the
   BODY: on EVERY landed hit an idmg enemy corrupts a random segment (its class), so you can win the
   fight and still walk out further gone. The vigor loss is small (these things barely tear flesh);
   the cost is what you ARE. Guard halves it (bracing keeps more of you together), as with the smear.
   The smoke creatures are the first carriers — dispersal is the literal reading of "less singular."
   Flavour is keyed off e.idmgFlavor so a future poison-BLADE reads differently from smoke. */
setup.IDMG_LINES = {
    smoke: function (who, dmg, iamt, seg) {
        return who + " comes apart against you and closes again past your guard; the blow barely lands — " +
            dmg + " — but a little of you goes with it as it passes, drawn off into the haze. You are that much " +
            "less one thing: " + iamt + " of your " + seg + " gone to smoke and stink, and not yours to call back.";
    },
    "default": function (who, dmg, iamt, seg) {
        return who + " lands a small, wrong wound — only " + dmg + " — but it does not close like a wound. It " +
            "changes instead: " + iamt + " more of your " + seg + " turned, worked in where the blow went.";
    }
};
/* IDENTITY-DAMAGE RESISTANCE (owner 2026-07-20) — a body already turned toward a class shrugs off more
   of the SAME: you cannot disperse what is already half-gone. Every ~2 fully-turned limbs of `cls` shave
   1 off incoming identity damage of that class (capped 2; every caller floors the result at 1, so it
   never fully negates the cost — it only rewards commitment). This is the build ANSWER to the smoke
   fight: turn toward filth and the shadow-person takes less of you. A fresh (SINGULAR) body has ZERO
   resistance — the cost lands full on exactly the player trying to stay one thing. */
setup.identityResist = function (cls) {
    if (!setup.CLASSES.includes(cls)) { return 0; }
    return Math.min(2, Math.floor(setup.classLimbs(cls) / 2));
};
setup.identityHit = function (e, dmg, guarding, crit) {
    var base = (e.idmg || 0) * (crit ? 2 : 1); if (base <= 0) { return ""; }   /* a crit takes double of you */
    var iamt = Math.max(1, (guarding ? Math.floor(base / 2) : base) - setup.identityResist(e.cls));
    var iseg = setup.SEGMENTS.random();
    setup.corrupt(iseg, e.cls, iamt);                                   /* corrupt() resyncs mirror + sheet + spills */
    var line = setup.IDMG_LINES[e.idmgFlavor] || setup.IDMG_LINES["default"];
    return " " + line(setup.theName(e.name, true), dmg, iamt, setup.SEG_LABEL[iseg] || iseg) +
        (guarding ? " (braced — you hold more of yourself together.)" : "");
};
/* IDENTITY DAMAGE — the PLAYER side (owner 2026-07-20; the original catch: "poison type weapons that do
   identity damage"). A tainted weapon hits like a prize but works its OWN nature into the WIELDER on
   every landed blow: power now, self later — the trade that makes the nastiest weapon not a free pick if
   you are trying to stay human. Reads the equipped weapon's `taint {cls, amt, line?}` (enemies don't
   transform, so the damage lands on YOU, not them); idmg-resistance shaves it; corrupts a random
   segment; returns a log clause. Fires from playerStrike + doSpecial on a LANDED hit. An optional
   `taint.line` string carries the weapon's own voice with {amt}/{seg} placeholders. */
setup.weaponTaint = function () {
    var V = State.variables, w = V.weapon && setup.items[V.weapon], t = w && w.taint;
    if (!t || !(t.amt > 0)) { return ""; }
    var cls = setup.CLASSES.includes(t.cls) ? t.cls : "filth";
    var amt = Math.max(1, t.amt - setup.identityResist(cls));
    var seg = setup.SEGMENTS.random(), where = setup.SEG_LABEL[seg] || seg;
    setup.corrupt(seg, cls, amt);
    var base = t.line || (setup.theName(w.name) + " takes its wage as it bites — {amt} of " + setup.CLASS_LABEL[cls] + " worked into your {seg}.");
    return " " + base.replace("{amt}", amt).replace("{seg}", where);
};
/* ===== MORALE (review C2) — nothing on the enemy side ever broke, fled, or yielded; the
   only self-preservation in hell belonged to the player. Now: when an enemy is BADLY HURT
   (≤ 1/3 hp) or a PACKMATE HAS FALLEN, it weighs the fight ONCE (per-actor moraleChecked —
   bounded, no re-roll spam): d20 + statLevel vs DC 8 + 2×your turned limbs + 2×pack deaths.
   The horror read: the more turned you are, the more hell's own creatures refuse you —
   regard, inside combat. A broken enemy FLEES (hp 0 + fled flag): it pays NO xp, NO coins,
   NO drop (spoils accrue only in playerStrike when a body actually falls) — the cleanest
   kills are the ones that never finish. Bosses and the press-gang hold by nature (paid to
   bring bodies). A held check is silent (courage makes no noise). */
setup.MORALE_DC_BASE = 8;
setup.moraleCheck = function (e) {
    if (e.boss || e.id === "pig_pressgang" || e.moraleChecked || e.hp <= 0) { return ""; }
    var V = State.variables;
    var packDeaths = (V.enemies || []).filter(function (x) { return x.hp <= 0 && !x.fled; }).length;
    var hurt = e.hp < e.maxhp && e.hp <= Math.ceil(e.maxhp / 3);   /* must have TAKEN a wound — a pristine 1-hp rat is not "badly hurt" */
    if (!hurt && packDeaths === 0) { return ""; }
    e.moraleChecked = true;
    var form = V.form || {}, turned = 0;
    setup.SEGMENTS.forEach(function (s) { if ((form[s] || "human") !== "human") { turned++; } });
    var bloodFear = (setup.bloodOf(e.cls) >= setup.BLOOD_FELT) ? 2 : 0;   /* R17: its kind's blood on you argues for running */
    var dc = setup.MORALE_DC_BASE + 2 * turned + 2 * packDeaths + bloodFear;
    if (setup.d(20) + e.statLevel >= dc) { return ""; }        /* it holds — silently */
    e.hp = 0; e.fled = true; e.winding = false;
    var line = " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " reads the fight again — ";
    line += (turned >= 2)
        ? "the turned parts of you, the argument your body is becoming — and wants no part of it. It breaks"
        : (packDeaths > 0 ? "its fallen beside it, the sum going against it — and breaks"
            : (bloodFear > 0 ? "and smells, under everything else on you, how much of its own kind's blood is already there — and breaks"
                : "the wrongness of how this is going — and breaks"));
    line += " and is gone into the dark, and takes nothing of you with it.";
    return line;
};
/* the enemy phase: every living enemy acts. guarding halves each landed hit (and answers
   the signature payoffs — each move says how). A winding enemy spends its attack on the
   telegraph; the payoff auto-lands next round; a stun knocks the gathered move out of it. */
setup.enemyTurn = function (guarding) {
    var V = State.variables, pac = setup.playerAC(V.scores), log = "";
    if (V.held > 0) { V.held = 0; }   /* the hold releases as the round turns over */
    setup.aliveEnemies().forEach(function (e) {
        var broke = setup.moraleCheck(e);          /* C2: it may weigh the fight and refuse it */
        if (broke) { log += broke; return; }
        if (e.stunned) {
            e.stunned = false;
            log += " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " is still reeling, and misses its turn.";
            if (e.winding) { e.winding = false; log += " The gathered violence goes out of it."; }
            return;
        }
        var mv = e.move && setup.ENEMY_MOVES[e.move];
        if (e.winding && mv) {
            e.winding = false;
            log += mv.land(e, guarding);
            return;
        }
        e.rounds = (e.rounds || 0) + 1;
        if (mv && e.rounds % (e.every || 3) === 0) {
            e.winding = true;
            log += mv.tele(e);
            return;                        /* the wind-up spends its attack — your window to answer */
        }
        var a = setup.attack(e.atkMod, 0, pac, e.weaponDie, e.dmgMod);
        if (a.hit) {
            var dmg = guarding ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(a.dmg / 2)) : a.dmg;
            V.hp -= dmg;
            if (e.idmg > 0) {   /* identity damage IS this thing's attack — narrate the self-cost, not the flesh */
                log += setup.identityHit(e, dmg, guarding, a.crit);   /* corrupts every landed hit; a crit takes double */
            } else {
                log += " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + (a.crit ? " savages you for " : " tears into you for ") + dmg + (guarding ? " (braced)" : "") + ".";
                if (a.crit) {   /* R13: a crit smears — the wound keeps a little of what made it */
                    var smear = guarding ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(setup.CRIT_SMEAR / 2)) : setup.CRIT_SMEAR;
                    var sseg = setup.SEGMENTS.random();
                    setup.corrupt(sseg, e.cls, smear);
                    log += " The wound keeps a little of the " + setup.CLASS_LABEL[e.cls] + " that made it (" + smear + " into your " + setup.SEG_LABEL[sseg] + ").";
                }
            }
        } else {
            log += " " + setup.theName(e.name, true) + " lunges and misses.";
        }
    });
    return log;
};

/* ===================== IN-GAME MAP SCREEN =====================
   Fog-of-war view of the descent, drawn from the GENERATED setup.mapGraph
   (tools/passage-graph.mjs --embed: baked force-layout positions + adjacency)
   filtered by the cross-life setup.discoveredSet(). Only rooms you've charted
   show solid; an unknown room adjacent to a charted one shows as a "?" fog node
   (the frontier — you know an exit goes somewhere); deeper unknowns stay dark.
   Reached from the StoryCaption "Map" link (stashes $mapReturn). Lives in this
   raw-JS script-block, not the StoryInit run-block, because it emits SVG markup
   that TwineScript desugaring would mangle. */
setup.mapHuman = function (n) {
    return n.replace(/^The/, "").replace(/Cleared$/, "").replace(/([a-z])([A-Z])/g, "$1 $2").trim() || n;
};
setup.MAP_ROLE_COLOR = { room: "#7d8893", rest: "#4e9a6b", fight: "#b4503e", ending: "#1c1c20", lander: "#566069" };
setup.mapView = function (container, layerKey) {
    if (!container) return;
    var NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
    var disc = setup.discoveredSet();
    var here = State.variables.mapReturn || "";
    var hereLayer = setup.depthOf[here];
    var visited = [];
    for (var L = 1; L <= 9; L++) { if (setup.discoveredCount(L) > 0) { visited.push(L); } }
    container.innerHTML = "";
    if (!visited.length) {
        container.innerHTML = '<p class="map-empty">You have charted nothing yet. The dark is total.</p>';
        return;
    }
    if (layerKey == null) { layerKey = (hereLayer && disc[here]) ? hereLayer : visited[visited.length - 1]; }
    if (visited.indexOf(layerKey) < 0) { layerKey = visited[0]; }
    var meta = setup.mapMeta, G = setup.mapGraph[String(layerKey)];

    /* tab bar — all 9 layers; unvisited ones are dark & inert (hint at depth) */
    var tabs = document.createElement("div");
    tabs.className = "map-tabs";
    for (var t = 1; t <= 9; t++) {
        var b = document.createElement("button");
        var seen = visited.indexOf(t) >= 0;
        b.className = "map-tab" + (t === layerKey ? " active" : "") + (seen ? "" : " locked");
        b.textContent = seen ? "L" + t : "·";
        if (seen) {
            b.title = meta.layerName[t];
            (function (tt) { b.addEventListener("click", function () { setup.mapView(container, tt); }); })(t);
        }
        tabs.appendChild(b);
    }
    container.appendChild(tabs);

    /* title line */
    var head = document.createElement("div");
    head.className = "map-headline";
    head.innerHTML = '<span class="map-title">' + meta.layerName[layerKey] + '</span>' +
        '<span class="map-band band-' + meta.band[layerKey] + '">' + meta.band[layerKey] + '</span>' +
        '<span class="map-count">' + setup.discoveredCount(layerKey) + " / " + G.rooms.length + " charted</span>";
    container.appendChild(head);

    /* which rooms are visible: charted, or frontier (unknown but adjacent to charted) */
    var rooms = G.rooms;
    var isDisc = rooms.map(function (r) { return !!disc[r[0]]; });
    var frontier = rooms.map(function () { return false; });
    G.intra.forEach(function (e) {
        if (isDisc[e[0]] && !isDisc[e[1]]) { frontier[e[1]] = true; }
        if (isDisc[e[1]] && !isDisc[e[0]]) { frontier[e[0]] = true; }
    });
    var visible = rooms.map(function (_, i) { return isDisc[i] || frontier[i]; });

    var svg = document.createElementNS(NS, "svg");
    svg.setAttribute("viewBox", "0 0 1000 640");
    svg.setAttribute("class", "map-svg");
    var defs = document.createElementNS(NS, "defs");
    defs.innerHTML = '<marker id="mapArrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#4a5159"/></marker>';
    svg.appendChild(defs);

    /* edges: draw if at least one end is charted (reveals corridors into fog) */
    G.intra.forEach(function (e) {
        if (!isDisc[e[0]] && !isDisc[e[1]]) { return; }
        var a = rooms[e[0]], b = rooms[e[1]];
        var toFog = !isDisc[e[0]] || !isDisc[e[1]];
        var line = document.createElementNS(NS, "line");
        line.setAttribute("x1", a[2]); line.setAttribute("y1", a[3]);
        line.setAttribute("x2", b[2]); line.setAttribute("y2", b[3]);
        line.setAttribute("stroke", toFog ? "#2a2e34" : "#3a4047");
        line.setAttribute("stroke-width", toFog ? 1 : 1.6);
        if (toFog) { line.setAttribute("stroke-dasharray", "3 4"); }
        else if (e[2]) { line.setAttribute("marker-end", "url(#mapArrow)"); }
        svg.appendChild(line);
    });

    /* nodes */
    rooms.forEach(function (r, i) {
        if (!visible[i]) { return; }
        var g = document.createElementNS(NS, "g");
        g.setAttribute("transform", "translate(" + r[2] + "," + r[3] + ")");
        if (isDisc[i]) {
            var label = setup.mapHuman(r[0]);
            var w = Math.max(40, label.length * 6.4 + 14);
            var rect = document.createElementNS(NS, "rect");
            rect.setAttribute("x", -w / 2); rect.setAttribute("y", -12);
            rect.setAttribute("width", w); rect.setAttribute("height", 24);
            rect.setAttribute("rx", 5);
            rect.setAttribute("fill", setup.MAP_ROLE_COLOR[r[1]] || "#7d8893");
            rect.setAttribute("stroke", r[0] === here ? "#c9b86a" : "#0c0d0f");
            rect.setAttribute("stroke-width", r[0] === here ? 2.5 : 1.5);
            g.appendChild(rect);
            var txt = document.createElementNS(NS, "text");
            txt.setAttribute("x", 0); txt.setAttribute("y", 4);
            txt.setAttribute("text-anchor", "middle");
            txt.setAttribute("font-size", 10.5);
            txt.setAttribute("fill", r[1] === "ending" ? "#c9b86a" : "#0c0d0f");
            txt.setAttribute("font-weight", 600);
            txt.textContent = label;
            g.appendChild(txt);
            if (r[0] === here) {
                var star = document.createElementNS(NS, "text");
                star.setAttribute("x", w / 2 + 7); star.setAttribute("y", 4);
                star.setAttribute("font-size", 13); star.setAttribute("fill", "#c9b86a");
                star.textContent = "★";
                var tt = document.createElementNS(NS, "title"); tt.textContent = "You are here";
                star.appendChild(tt); g.appendChild(star);
            }
            /* up/down connector badges on charted rooms */
            G.links.forEach(function (lk) {
                if (lk[0] !== i) { return; }
                var down = lk[1] > layerKey;
                var badge = document.createElementNS(NS, "text");
                badge.setAttribute("x", -w / 2 - 8);
                badge.setAttribute("y", down ? 11 : -3);
                badge.setAttribute("font-size", 13);
                badge.setAttribute("text-anchor", "middle");
                badge.setAttribute("fill", down ? "#e0925f" : "#7fb0e0");
                badge.textContent = down ? "↓" : "↑";
                var bt = document.createElementNS(NS, "title");
                bt.textContent = (down ? "down to " : "up to ") + meta.layerName[lk[1]] +
                    (disc[lk[2]] ? " · " + setup.mapHuman(lk[2]) : "");
                badge.appendChild(bt);
                g.appendChild(badge);
            });
        } else {
            /* frontier fog node */
            var c = document.createElementNS(NS, "circle");
            c.setAttribute("r", 7);
            c.setAttribute("fill", "#16181c");
            c.setAttribute("stroke", "#3a4047");
            c.setAttribute("stroke-dasharray", "2 2");
            var q = document.createElementNS(NS, "text");
            q.setAttribute("text-anchor", "middle"); q.setAttribute("y", 4);
            q.setAttribute("font-size", 11); q.setAttribute("fill", "#6b727a");
            q.textContent = "?";
            var ft = document.createElementNS(NS, "title"); ft.textContent = "unexplored";
            g.appendChild(c); g.appendChild(q); g.appendChild(ft);
        }
        svg.appendChild(g);
    });
    container.appendChild(svg);
};
<</script>>


:: Widgets [widget]
<<widget "acquire">>
  /* thin wrapper over setup.acquire (handles pickup-curse, auto-equip, recompute) */
  <<run setup.acquire(_args[0])>>
<</widget>>

/* <<corrupt SEGMENT CLASS AMOUNT>> — adds class-attributed corruption to one body
   segment (head/torso/armL/armR/legL/legR · rat/pig/filth). Updates the derived
   $corruption mirror and transforms the segment if it fills. Replaces the old
   `<<set $corruption to $corruption + N>>`. See docs/TRANSFORMATION.md. */
<<widget "corrupt">>
  <<run setup.corrupt(_args[0], _args[1], _args[2])>>
  <<run setup.pushChange()>>   /* queue a body-change beat; PassageHeader flushes it onto the next room */
<</widget>>

/* <<soothe AMOUNT>> — rest/wash: eases corruption on segments that haven't fully
   turned. Replaces `<<set $corruption to Math.max(0, $corruption - N)>>`. */
<<widget "soothe">>
  <<run setup.soothe(_args[0])>>
<</widget>>

/* <<roomart ID>> — a drop-in ROOM ILLUSTRATION: shows img/room/<ID>.png (e.g. above a
   passage's prose) if the file exists, else renders nothing (onerror hides it). Same
   convention as the combat portraits; put room art in img/room/ and build.ps1 syncs it
   into dist/. Usage at the top of a passage: <<roomart "fatberg">> */
<<widget "roomart">>
<<set _ra to "img/room/" + _args[0] + ".png">>
<div class="room-illus"><img class="room-illus-img" @src="_ra" alt="" onerror="this.parentElement.style.display='none'"></div>
<</widget>>

/* <<scentof SPEC>> — the pre-fight "con" read (review R14): smell the thing before you
   commit to it. SPEC = one enemy id ("gorger") or an array (["shitgolem","shitgolem"]).
   Renders one line in the room-scent band voice; rung + prose from setup.threatRead /
   setup.THREAT_SCENT (script block). Place it in the room, above the fight-offering links —
   the read belongs where the player stands deciding. */
<<widget "scentof">>
<<set _tsr to setup.THREAT_SCENT[setup.threatRead(_args[0])]>>
<<set _tsl to (Array.isArray(_args[0]) and _args[0].length > 1) ? _tsr.many : _tsr.one>>
<div @class="'room-scent rs-' + _tsr.tier"><<= _tsl>></div>
<</widget>>


:: StoryCaption
/* Visible corruption meter (boss: visible). Corruption reads as filth on the
   body. Plus a compact kit readout (coins / vigor / gear). */
<<set _c to Math.clamp($corruption, 0, 100)>>
<div class="corruption-block">
  <div class="corruption-label">Corruption —
    <<if _c gte 100>>lost<<elseif _c gte 70>>deeply corrupted<<elseif _c gte 35>>slipping<<else>>wary<</if>>
  </div>
  <div class="corruption-bar">
    <div @class="'corruption-fill' + (_c >= 70 ? ' t2' : (_c >= 35 ? ' t1' : ''))" @style="'width: ' + _c + '%'"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="corruption-num"><<= _c>> / 100</div>
  <div class="body-state">
    <<if _c gte 90>>You can no longer find where the filth ends and you begin.
    <<elseif _c gte 70>>Black slime is worked deep under your nails, into the seams of you.
    <<elseif _c gte 35>>Grime to the wrist. A taste in your mouth you've stopped spitting out.
    <<elseif _c gte 10>>There's muck on your hands and a smell that won't wipe off.
    <<else>>You are still, mostly, clean.
    <</if>>
  </div>
</div>
<<if $deepTurns gte setup.SEAL_WARN or $sealed>><div class="seal-state"><<= setup.SEAL_MIND.caption[setup.sealTier() - 1]>></div><</if>>
<<if $body>>
<div class="bodymap">
  <div class="bm-label">Body</div>
  <<for _seg range setup.SEGMENTS>>
    <<set _stage to setup.segStage(_seg)>>
    <<set _tot to setup.segTotal(_seg)>>
    <div @class="'bm-row s-' + _stage">
      <span class="bm-seg"><<= setup.SEG_LABEL[_seg]>></span>
      <span><<if $form[_seg] neq "human">><<= setup.CLASS_LABEL[$form[_seg]].toUpperCase()>> · turned<<elseif _tot gt 0>><<= setup.CLASS_LABEL[setup.segClass(_seg) || "filth"]>> <<= _tot>>%<<else>><span class="bm-clean">—</span><</if>></span>
    </div>
    <<set _desc to setup.segDesc(_seg)>>
    <<if _desc>><div @class="'bm-desc d-' + _stage"><<= _desc>></div><</if>>
  <</for>>
</div>
<</if>>
<<if $mouthCursed>><div class="curse-line">Your mouth no longer always says what you mean.</div><</if>>
<<if $workCursed>><div class="curse-line">Indentured to <<= setup.workLabel()>>.<<if $workOwed>> A shift is owed.<</if>></div><</if>>
<<if $scores and $scores.str>>
<div class="kit">
  <div class="statsheet">
    <div class="ss-lvl">Level <<= $level>><<if setup.marksAlterStats()>> · <span class="ss-marked">marked</span><</if>></div>
    <div class="ss-xp">XP <<= ($xp != null ? $xp : 0)>> / <<= setup.xpForNext()>></div>
    <div class="ss-grid">
      <span>STR <<= $scores.str>></span><span>DEX <<= $scores.dex>></span><span>CON <<= $scores.con>></span>
      <span>INT <<= $scores.int>></span><span>WIS <<= $scores.wis>></span><span>CHA <<= $scores.cha>></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ss-derived">AC <<= setup.playerAC($scores)>> · <span @class="($hp <= ($maxhp / 3)) ? 'k-hurt' : ''">Vigor <<= Math.max(0, $hp)>>/<<= $maxhp>></span></div>
    <<if $magicKnown>><div class="ss-mana">The Word — Mana <<= Math.max(0, $mana)>>/<<= $maxmana>> <span class="ss-mana-note">(magic <<= setup.magicLevel()>>)</span></div><</if>>
  </div>
  <div><span class="k-coins">Coins: <<= $coins>></span></div>
  <div>In hand: <<if $weapon>><<= setup.items[$weapon].name>> (<<= setup.weaponDie($weapon)>><<if setup.weaponKind($weapon)>> <<= setup.weaponKind($weapon)>><</if>>)<<else>>bare fists (1d2)<</if>></div>
  <div>Worn: <<if $armor>><<= setup.items[$armor].name>> (+<<= setup.items[$armor].ac>> AC)<<else>>your own skin<</if>></div>
  <<set _acc to setup.accessoryNotes()>>
  <<if _acc.length>><div>On you: <<= _acc.join(", ")>></div><</if>>
  <<set _pack to ($inventory ? $inventory.filter(function (i) { var it = setup.items[i]; return it and it.kind neq "junk" and i neq $weapon and i neq $armor and i neq $ring and i neq $necklace and i neq $boots and i neq $gloves; }) : [])>>
  <<if _pack.length>><div>Pack: <<= _pack.map(function (i) { return setup.itemDisplayName(i); }).join(", ")>></div><</if>>
  <<set _crs to setup.activeCurseLabels()>>
  <<if _crs.length>><div class="curse-line">Cursed — <<= _crs.join("; ")>>.</div><</if>>
  <<if passage() neq "Equipment" and passage() neq "Map" and passage() neq "Combat" and not tags().includes("ending")>>
  <div class="gear-link"><<link "⚙ Manage gear">><<set $gearReturn to passage()>><<goto "Equipment">><</link>> <<link "🗺 Map">><<set $mapReturn to passage()>><<goto "Map">><</link>></div>
  <</if>>
</div>
<</if>>


:: PassageHeader
/* Generic succumbing to corruption — GLOBAL loss, fires anywhere the meter
   tops out. Skipped on ending pages so it can't loop or override an ending. */
<<if not tags().includes("ending") and $corruption gte 100>><<goto "EndingBecome">><</if>>
<<silently>>
  /* SELF-HEAL: $scores is a save-variable added with the D&D combat rework. A save
     (or autosave) from before that update lacks it, which would crash Combat. Rebuild
     it from level + marks if it's ever missing. Future-proofs old saves + restart races. */
  <<if not $body or not $form>><<run setup.healBody()>><</if>>
  <<if not $scores or not $scores.str>><<run setup.recomputePlayer()>><</if>>
  <<if $xp == null>><<set $xp to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $mouthCursed == null>><<set $mouthCursed to false>><</if>>
  <<if $workCursed == null>><<set $workCursed to false>><</if>>
  <<if $workStation == null>><<set $workStation to "">><</if>>
  <<if $workOwed == null>><<set $workOwed to false>><</if>>
  <<if $sneakedOut == null>><<set $sneakedOut to false>><</if>>
  <<if $shiftsWorked == null>><<set $shiftsWorked to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $workCooldown == null>><<set $workCooldown to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $ductVented == null>><<set $ductVented to false>><</if>>
  <<if $pressedReturn == null>><<set $pressedReturn to "">><</if>>
  <<if $pressedStation == null>><<set $pressedStation to "">><</if>>
  <<if $cleanPool == null>><<set $cleanPool to "new">><</if>>
  <<if $cleanPoolUsed == null>><<set $cleanPoolUsed to false>><</if>>
  <<if $ring == null>><<set $ring to null>><</if>>
  <<if $necklace == null>><<set $necklace to null>><</if>>
  <<if $boots == null>><<set $boots to null>><</if>>
  <<if $gloves == null>><<set $gloves to null>><</if>>
  <<if $eye == null>><<set $eye to null>><</if>>
  <<if $hand == null>><<set $hand to null>><</if>>
  <<if $hide == null>><<set $hide to null>><</if>>
  <<if $heart == null>><<set $heart to null>><</if>>
  <<if not $idKnown>><<set $idKnown to []>><</if>>
  <<if $gearReturn == null>><<set $gearReturn to "">><</if>>
  <<if $mapReturn == null>><<set $mapReturn to "">><</if>>
  <<if not $enemies>><<set $enemies to []>><</if>>
  <<if $target == null>><<set $target to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $specialUses == null>><<set $specialUses to 0>><</if>>
  <<if not $combatSpoils>><<set $combatSpoils to { coins: 0, xp: 0 }>><</if>>
  <<if not $blood>><<set $blood to { rat: 0, pig: 0, filth: 0 }>><</if>>
  <<if not $swOut>><<set $swOut to {}>><</if>>
  <<if $swStat == null>><<set $swStat to "">><</if>>
  <<if $addiction == null>><<run setup.healAddiction()>><</if>>  /* THE VICES: build the ledger + seed cheese from legacy $cheeseTasted on an old save */
  <<if $stillmanHeard == null>><<set $stillmanHeard to false>><</if>>
  <<if $curdmasterHeard == null>><<set $curdmasterHeard to false>><</if>>
  <<if $gutteringCleared == null>><<set $gutteringCleared to false>><</if>>
  <<if not $combatMenu>><<set $combatMenu to "main">><</if>>
  <<if $encounterReturn == null>><<set $encounterReturn to "">><</if>>
  <<if $encounterFight == null>><<set $encounterFight to false>><</if>>
  <<if not $combatOrigin>><<set $combatOrigin to ($combatReturn || "Hellmouth")>><</if>>
  <<if not $sigil>><<set $sigil to []>><</if>>
  <<if not $inventory>><<set $inventory to []>><</if>>
  <<if not $pendingChanges>><<set $pendingChanges to []>><</if>>
  <<if $sealNoticed == null>><<set $sealNoticed to 0>><</if>>
  <<if ndef $formLast>><<set $formLast to null>><</if>>
  <<if $regardCooldown == null>><<set $regardCooldown to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $regardLast == null>><<set $regardLast to "">><</if>>
  <<if not $noseBlind>><<set $noseBlind to []>><</if>>
  <<if $scentCooldown == null>><<set $scentCooldown to 0>><</if>>
  <<if $scentLast == null>><<set $scentLast to "">><</if>>
  <<if not tags().includes("ending")>>
    /* belonging clock: accrues by the depth of the passage you're in. Deeper
       = faster. Past setup.SEAL_LIMIT the way up is gone. */
    <<set $deepTurns to $deepTurns + (setup.depthOf[passage()] || 0)>>
    <<if $deepTurns gte setup.SEAL_LIMIT>><<set $sealed to true>><</if>>
    /* chart this room on the cross-life map (discover() guards to real rooms) */
    <<run setup.discover(passage())>>
    /* keep music alive after a reload */
    <<if setup.lastTrack and (!setup.current or !setup.current.isPlaying())>>
      <<run setup.playNext()>>
    <</if>>
  <</if>>
<</silently>>
/* BELONGING beat + FORM-SWITCH reset (owner 2026-07-01): PLACED BEFORE the encounter roll on purpose.
   The seal clock is the MIND settling into your CURRENT dominant form (setup.bodyClass), not just the
   way-up closing — so if that form CHANGES (rat → pig), the settling comes undone: reset $deepTurns
   (+ un-seal + re-arm the beats) and narrate the un-settling. First onset (human → first class) only
   records the form, no reset. Otherwise fire the once-per-tier settling beat (monotonic $sealNoticed) as
   the clock climbs. A fired beat sets _sealBeat, which suppresses THIS move's encounter roll below — so an
   encounter <<goto>> (which does NOT abort the rest of this header) can never discard the beat, which
   would lose it permanently since $sealNoticed/$formLast advance here. Skipping one rare encounter is
   negligible (and fitting — the world pauses as the mind lurches). Real rooms only; tiers are 70pts apart
   vs +9 max/move so none is skipped. See setup.sealTier / setup.SEAL_MIND / setup.bodyClass. */
<<nobr>><<if not tags().includes("ending") and (setup.depthOf[passage()] || 0) gte 1>>
<<set _dom to setup.bodyClass()>>
<<set _domCls to _dom ? _dom.cls : null>>
<<if _domCls isnot null and _domCls neq $formLast>>
  <<if $formLast isnot null>>
    /* a real form → form switch: the settling undoes and the deep must re-claim the new you */
    <<set $deepTurns to setup.SEAL_RESET_TO>>
    <<set $sealed to false>>
    <<set $sealNoticed to 0>>
    <<set _sealBeat to true>>
    <div class="settle-line settle-switch"><<= setup.SEAL_MIND.switched($formLast, _domCls)>></div>
  <</if>>
  <<set $formLast to _domCls>>
<<else>>
  <<set _st to setup.sealTier()>>
  <<if _st gt $sealNoticed>>
    <<set _sealBeat to true>>
    <div class="settle-line"><<= setup.SEAL_MIND.beat[_st - 1]>></div>
    <<set $sealNoticed to _st>>
  <</if>>
<</if>>
<</if>><</nobr>>
/* RANDOM ENCOUNTER roll (owner 2026-06-05): ~ENCOUNTER_RATE% per real room move, the local
   denizens accost you. encounterEligible() gates to real rooms (depthOf ≥ 1) and skips arrivals
   back from an encounter/combat so you can't chain. RandomEncounter has no depthOf, so it can't
   re-trigger itself. Suppressed on a move that fired a belonging beat (_sealBeat) so the beat's
   render is never discarded by an encounter <<goto>>. */
<<if not tags().includes("ending") and setup.encounterEligible() and not _sealBeat>>
  /* post-shift cooldown: a worked shift (doShift/doPressedShift) sets $workCooldown to
     setup.WORK_COOLDOWN. While it's up, each encounter-eligible move spends one turn of grace
     and rolls NO encounter — so you aren't accosted to work again the instant you clock out.
     (Currently the only encounter is the back-to-work press-gang, so this just paces shift-checks;
     if non-shift encounters are ever added, scope this to id "backtowork" instead.) */
  <<if $workCooldown gt 0>>
    <<set $workCooldown to $workCooldown - 1>>
  <<elseif random(1, 100) lte setup.encounterRate()>>
    <<set $encounterReturn to passage()>>
    <<goto "RandomEncounter">>
  <</if>>
<</if>>

/* TRANSFORMATION FEED (owner 2026-06-24): flush queued body-change beats at the top of the
   room you land in, so a <<corrupt>> fired inside a link narrates where you arrive. Placed
   AFTER the encounter roll so an encounter-goto carries the queue forward intact — the queue
   is cleared only once it actually renders. Skipped on endings (EndingBecome owns the
   becoming-prose). See setup.describeChange / the transformation-feed block in StoryInit. */
<<nobr>><<if not tags().includes("ending") and $pendingChanges>>
<<set _feed to $pendingChanges.map(function (c) { return { c: c, t: setup.describeChange(c) }; }).filter(function (o) { return o.t; })>>
<<if _feed.length>>
<div class="change-feed">
<<for _o range _feed>>
<div @class="'change-line cf-' + (_o.c.deepen ? 'deepen' : _o.c.toStage)"><<= _o.t>></div>
<</for>>
</div>
<</if>>
<<set $pendingChanges to []>>   /* cleared once we reach a real (non-ending) passage — never cleared-without-shown, since an encounter goto fires before this block */
<</if>><</nobr>>

/* ROOM-SCENT beat (owner 2026-06-25): how the place's stink HITS you — and how your disgust at it
   erodes as you corrupt. The third olfactory system: regard = the world smells YOU; nose-blind = you
   stop smelling YOURSELF; this = your reaction to the WORLD's reek slides revulsion -> acceptance ->
   relish. Revulsion is SILENT (the room's own prose owns the human disgust); the beat speaks only once
   your reaction has drifted past human (eff >= SCENT_EASE_AT). Driven by general $corruption + a species
   affinity (matching turned limbs). LIVE / reversible (re-derived each room) — the continuous slide,
   where nose-blind is the latched milestone. Cooldown-gated + fire-on-change like regard, sharing
   REGARD_COOLDOWN. Sits between the feed (your body) and regard (the world's voice). See setup.scentTier. */
<<nobr>><<if not tags().includes("ending") and (setup.depthOf[passage()] || 0) gte 1>>
<<set _sc to setup.scentTier(passage())>>
<<if _sc and _sc.line>>
<<if _sc.key neq $scentLast or $scentCooldown lte 0>>
<div @class="'room-scent rs-' + _sc.tier"><<= _sc.line>></div>
<<set $scentLast to _sc.key>>
<<set $scentCooldown to setup.REGARD_COOLDOWN>>
<<else>>
<<set $scentCooldown to $scentCooldown - 1>>
<</if>>
<</if>>
<</if>><</nobr>>

/* SYSTEMIC REGARD (owner 2026-06-24): below the change-feed — your body changed, now the world reads
   what you are. Fires on real rooms only (depthOf >= 1, not endings), and is cooldown-gated: a CHANGED
   verdict (new band / tier / body-class) shows at once; the same verdict only refreshes after
   REGARD_COOLDOWN eligible moves. So it's pervasive but not a nag. See setup.regardOf / setup.REGARD. */
<<nobr>><<if not tags().includes("ending") and (setup.depthOf[passage()] || 0) gte 1>>
<<set _rg to setup.regardOf(passage())>>
<<if _rg and _rg.line>>
<<if _rg.key neq $regardLast or $regardCooldown lte 0>>
<div @class="'regard-line r-' + _rg.relation"><<= _rg.line>></div>
<<set $regardLast to _rg.key>>
<<set $regardCooldown to setup.REGARD_COOLDOWN>>
<<else>>
<<set $regardCooldown to $regardCooldown - 1>>
<</if>>
<</if>>
<</if>><</nobr>>

/* NOSE-BLIND beat (owner 2026-06-25): the one-time-per-class realization that you've gone anosmic to
   what you're becoming — olfactory adaptation as the bromidrophobia motif's sharpest point. Standing
   state (the corruption has already landed). Fires once per class per life, flagged in $noseBlind so it
   never repeats; a SPLIT body (saturated in two classes) gets each class's beat, one per passage. Flags
   only on show (a class with no NOSE_BLIND prose is skipped, never silently consumed). Real rooms only. */
<<nobr>><<if not tags().includes("ending") and (setup.depthOf[passage()] || 0) gte 1>>
<<set _nbc to "">>
<<for _c range setup.CLASSES>>
<<if _nbc is "" and setup.noseBlindReady(_c) and $noseBlind.indexOf(_c) lt 0 and setup.NOSE_BLIND[_c]>><<set _nbc to _c>><</if>>
<</for>>
<<if _nbc isnot "">><div class="nose-blind"><<= setup.NOSE_BLIND[_nbc]>></div><<run $noseBlind.push(_nbc)>><</if>>
<</if>><</nobr>>

/* ===================== INTRO — the kidnapping ===================== */

:: CharacterCreation
<<if setup.hasBuild()>><<goto "Start">><</if>>
<<if ndef $ccAssign>><<set $ccAssign to { str: 7, dex: 7, con: 7, int: 7, wis: 7, cha: 7 }>><</if>>
<<set _budget to 6 * setup.baseScore(1)>>
<<set _spent to $ccAssign.str + $ccAssign.dex + $ccAssign.con + $ccAssign.int + $ccAssign.wis + $ccAssign.cha>>
<<set _left to _budget - _spent>>
Before the drain, before the sack — there was a life, and a you who lived it. You will not have
it much longer. The deep takes everything down here eventually, a piece at a time, and hands back
something worse. But it has not started yet. For one more moment you are whole, and ordinary, and
entirely your own.

So: what //kind// of whole? Where were you strong, in the life they are about to drag you out of,
and where were you wanting? Set it down now, while it is still true — what you carry under with you
is all you will have left to lose.

//Seven is the ordinary measure of a thing. Below it you are lacking; above it, gifted; and you have
only so much of yourself to go round.//

''Still to place: <<= _left>>''

<<for _row range setup.CC_STATS>><<capture _row>><<set _v to $ccAssign[_row.key]>>\
<<= _row.label>> — <<= _v>>, <<= setup.ccDescribe(_v)>>  <<if _v gt 1>><<link "[−]">><<set $ccAssign[_row.key] to $ccAssign[_row.key] - 1>><<goto "CharacterCreation">><</link>><<else>>[−]<</if>> <<if _v lt setup.CC_MAX and _left gt 0>><<link "[+]">><<set $ccAssign[_row.key] to $ccAssign[_row.key] + 1>><<goto "CharacterCreation">><</link>><<else>>[+]<</if>>
//<<= _row.blurb>> — <<= _row.does>>//

<</capture>><</for>>\
<<set _hp to Math.max(1, 4 * (5 + setup.mod($ccAssign.con)))>>\
//At these measures your body would wake with <<= _hp>> vigour<<if _hp lte 4>> — barely a body at all<</if>>.//

<<if _left gt 0>>
//(place all your points — <<= _left>> still to set down before they come for you)//
<<elseif _left lt 0>>
//(you have laid out more of yourself than there is — take some back)//
<<else>>
<<set _dump to ($ccAssign.str lte 4 or $ccAssign.dex lte 4 or $ccAssign.con lte 4 or $ccAssign.int lte 4 or $ccAssign.wis lte 4 or $ccAssign.cha lte 4)>>
<<if _dump>>
<<linkreplace "Begin. This is who they take.">>
//You are going down with almost nothing where one of your measures should be. The deep keeps this build: it is who you wake as every life down here, and only a Restart — which scours everything you have earned — ever undoes it. A level or two of surviving lifts a low start within a life, but never the next life's start. Set it down anyway?//

<<link "Yes. This is who they take.">><<run setup.commitBuild()>><<goto "Start">><</link>>
<</linkreplace>>
<<else>>
<<link "Begin. This is who they take.">><<run setup.commitBuild()>><<goto "Start">><</link>>
<</if>>
<</if>>

<<link "Even it out — seven all round, an ordinary life">><<set $ccAssign to { str: 7, dex: 7, con: 7, int: 7, wis: 7, cha: 7 }>><<goto "CharacterCreation">><</link>>


:: Start
<h1>Sewer Demons</h1>

It is the small, ugly hour of the night and you are alone at the mouth of the
alley, where the storm drain breathes its warm rot up at you, because alone at
that hour by an open drain is where a body is most easily taken and least
quickly missed. You don't hear it coming. Nothing that hunts the exposed and the
solitary ever lets you hear it coming.

A weight like a dropped engine hits you from behind, and a smell of wet pork and
sewage closes over your face, and the last thing you see before the sack comes
down is a wet pink snout the size of a manhole and two small eyes that have done
this many, many times before.

<<link "Struggle">>
  /* first interaction also unlocks browser autoplay for the soundtrack */
  <<run setup.playNext()>>
  <<goto "Captured">>
<</link>>


:: Captured
You struggle, which is to say you thrash inside a wet burlap dark while something
enormous carries you slung over its shoulder, down and down, the air getting
hotter and closer with every jolting step. The pig-thing hums as it walks — a
low, satisfied, domestic sound, the sound of someone carrying groceries home.

Then the humming stops. There is a noise above you like a cathedral clearing its
throat, and the pig-thing makes a small sound that is, unmistakably, fear — and
then you are falling, sack and all, because something higher up the food chain
has just plucked your captor off its feet the way a man plucks a shrimp from a
bowl. You hit wet stone. Up above, very briefly, something screams in a register
that loosens your teeth, and then is quiet.

For a while you simply lie there, because the alternative is to find out where
*there* is. The sack has gone slack around you — no longer carried, only dropped —
and through the wet burlap the world begins arriving in pieces. A heat that has
nothing to do with summer. A wet-stone cold under your hip that argues with it. And
a smell: sulphur, and standing water, and under both, impossibly, something cooking
— rich and savoury and close, the smell of a kitchen that has been expecting
company. Somewhere off in the dark, a long way down or a long way in, a great many
things are busy being alive, and none of them, yet, with you.

<<link "Wriggle free of the sack">><<goto "WriggleFree">><</link>>


:: WriggleFree
You get an arm loose, then your head, and you spill out of the sack onto cold
slick flagstones, gulping air that tastes of sulphur and standing water and the
faint sweetness of cooking somewhere close. Whatever took the pig-thing is gone.
You are, for the moment, nobody's property.

You are also nowhere you have a word for. You came down a sewer; this is not the
underside of any city. Ahead of you the passage opens onto an enormous arch of
fused bone and dripstone, and beyond it, light — warm, busy, wrong — and the
unmistakable churn of a great many things living their lives. Behind you, the way
the pig dragged you down: a mortal-smelling dark, brick and rust and rats. A
sewer. The sewer. The way back up to the cold clean world, if there is one.

<<if setup.hasMark("damned")>>
And yet none of it is new. You have stood in this exact wrongness before, in a
life that ended down here — you wore one of their shapes once — and some part of
you that is not your mind knows the cooking-smell for the smell of your own
kitchen. The mark of it is still on you, under the skin, where no washing reaches.
<<elseif $returns gt 0>>
And yet your feet seem to know the slick of the flagstones. You have been here
before; you don't remember how the last time ended, but your body does, and it is
not as afraid as it should be. Whatever the deep put in you, it is still in you.
It always will be.
<</if>>

<<if $workCursed>>
And the binding is already in you — not a memory this time but a *summons*. A past life
signed you to a post down here and the deep never tore the indenture up; it tightens now,
the moment you draw breath, an old familiar weight settling onto your shoulders and turning
your feet. There is no arch for you, no holding-pen, no choosing which way to be swallowed.
There is your station, and a shift already owed, and the long downward pull toward
<<= setup.workLabel()>> that has not, in all the time you were gone, once stopped expecting you.

<<set _workRoom to setup.workRoom()>>
<<link "Let the binding carry you back down to your post">><<goto _workRoom>><</link>>
<<else>>
<<link "Toward the others — the newly-taken, the holding-pen, the unsorted">><<goto "TheArrivals">><</link>>
<</if>>


/* ===================== THE HELLMOUTH ===================== */

/* ===================== THE IN-BETWEEN & HELL (layer files) =====================
   L5 The Hellmouth (the threshold/spawn; the two ways split there) →
     src/layer5-hellmouth.twee  (intro WriggleFree drops into its hub, Hellmouth)
   L6 The Shambles (carnival hell-town, HellMarket/gear) → src/layer6-shambles.twee
   L7 Belly of the Beast / L8 Rendering / L9 Sulphur Deep → their own layer files.
   Core holds only systems, intro, combat, and the endings. */


/* ===================== COMBAT (light randomness) ===================== */

:: Combat
/* MULTI-ENEMY combat screen (owner 2026-06-05): name + portrait + hp bars side by side,
   action buttons below. Turn logic lives in setup.* (playerStrike/doSpecial/enemyTurn/
   useItem) so the displayed prose dodges the operator-word desugaring. $combatMenu drives
   the button row (main / special / items); $target is the aimed enemy. */
<<nobr>>
/* AUTO-SURRENDER curse (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT §D): the worn thing folds you the moment
   a fight starts — drop straight to the loss. (Checked before anything renders.) */
<<if setup.autoSurrender()>><<set $combatLog to "">><<goto "CombatLost">><</if>>
/* keep the aim on a living enemy */
<<if not $enemies[$target] or $enemies[$target].hp lte 0>><<set $target to setup.firstAliveIndex()>><</if>>
<<set _pac to setup.playerAC($scores)>>
<<set _phpw to "width:" + Math.max(0, Math.round($hp / $maxhp * 100)) + "%">>
<<set _ptype to setup.playerWeaponType()>><<set _pkind to setup.playerWeaponKind()>>
<div class="combat-screen">
<div class="combatants">

  <<set _pimg to setup.becameClass() ? ("img/enemy/player_" + setup.becameClass() + ".png") : "img/enemy/player.png">>
  <div class="cbt player">
    <div class="cbt-name">You</div>
    <div class="portrait player-port"><span class="port-glyph"><<= setup.becameClass() ? (setup.CLASS_GLYPH[setup.becameClass()] || "you") : "☖">></span><img class="port-img" @src="_pimg" alt="" onerror="this.style.display='none'"></div>
    <div class="hpbar"><div class="hpfill player" @style="_phpw"></div></div>
    <div class="hp-num"><<= Math.max(0, $hp)>>/<<= $maxhp>> · AC <<= _pac>></div>
  </div>

  <<for _i to 0; _i lt $enemies.length; _i++>>
  <<set _e to $enemies[_i]>>
  <<set _eclass to "cbt enemy" + (_e.hp lte 0 ? " dead" : "") + ((_i is $target) and (_e.hp gt 0) ? " targeted" : "")>>
  <<set _ehpw to "width:" + Math.max(0, Math.round(_e.hp / _e.maxhp * 100)) + "%">>
  <<set _eimg to "img/enemy/" + _e.img + ".png">>
  <div @class="_eclass">
    <div class="cbt-name"><<= _e.name>></div>
    <div class="portrait"><span class="port-glyph"><<= setup.CLASS_GLYPH[_e.cls] || "•">></span><img class="port-img" @src="_eimg" alt="" onerror="this.style.display='none'"></div>
    <div class="hpbar"><div class="hpfill enemy" @style="_ehpw"></div></div>
    <div class="hp-num"><<= Math.max(0, _e.hp)>>/<<= _e.maxhp>> · AC <<= _e.ac>></div>
    <<if (_e.hp gt 0) and _e.winding>><div class="cbt-wind">— gathering itself —</div><</if>>
    <<if _e.fled>><div class="cbt-wind">— fled —</div><</if>>
    <<if (_e.hp gt 0) and (setup.aliveEnemies().length gt 1) and (_i neq $target)>>
      <<capture _i>><span class="tgt-link"><<link "» aim here">><<set $target to _i>><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto "Combat">><</link>></span><</capture>>
    <</if>>
  </div>
  <</for>>

</div>

<<if $combatLog>><div class="clog"><<= $combatLog>></div><</if>>

<<set _tgt to $enemies[$target]>>
<<if _tgt and (setup.typeMult(_ptype, _tgt, _pkind) gt 1)>><div class="special-hint">Your <<= (_pkind or _ptype)>> is the right tool for <<= setup.theName(_tgt.name)>> — it //bites home//.</div>
<<elseif _tgt and (setup.typeMult(_ptype, _tgt, _pkind) lt 1)>><div class="special-hint">Your <<= (_pkind or _ptype)>> barely bites <<= setup.theName(_tgt.name)>> — wrong tool for this one.</div><</if>>

<<if $combatMenu is "special">>
<div class="special-hint">A unique attack — it sweeps the whole pack for a little less than a focused blow. <<= setup.specialsLeft()>> left this fight (one per level).</div>
<div class="combat-actions special-menu">
<<for _sp range setup.availableSpecials()>>
<<capture _sp>>
<<link _sp.name>>
  <<set _log to setup.doSpecial(_sp.id)>>
  <<if setup.combatOutcome() neq "victory">><<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>><</if>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<</capture>>
<</for>>
<<link "Back">><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
</div>

<<elseif $combatMenu is "items">>
<<set _cons to setup.usableItems()>>
<div class="combat-actions items-menu">
<<if _cons.length gt 0>>
<<for _id range _cons>>
<<capture _id>>
<<link setup.items[_id].name>>
  <<set _log to setup.useItem(_id)>>
  <<if setup.combatOutcome() neq "victory">><<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>><</if>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<</capture>>
<</for>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Nothing usable in your pack</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Back">><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
</div>

<<elseif $combatMenu is "yield">>
/* PARLEY (review R16): the middle path. Whether anything out there can HEAR the offer is
   telegraphed here, before you spend the round on it — offering at a deaf pack wastes the
   turn (an informed gamble, never a gotcha). Accepted purse = the loss's robbery formula,
   voluntary, walk out unmauled; accepted shift = marched to work, body untouched. */
<<set _listens to setup.packListens()>>
<<if _listens>>
<div class="special-hint">Something out there is listening. The deep wants labour, not death — everything down here has a price, and you are allowed to name one.</div>
<<else>>
<div class="special-hint">Nothing in front of you has ears for an offer — no mind back of the eyes to buy you. You could spend the breath anyway.</div>
<</if>>
<div class="combat-actions special-menu">
<<if $coins gt 0>>
<<set _ylbl to "Toss them the purse — they take what they take (" + $coins + " carried)">>
<<link _ylbl>>
  <<if setup.packListens()>>
    <<set $yieldTook to setup.yieldPurse()>>
    <<set $yieldKind to "purse">>
    <<set $combatLog to "">><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
    <<goto "CombatYielded">>
  <<else>>
    <<set _log to "You hold the purse out and the offer dies in the air — nothing in front of you has a mind to buy. The gesture costs you the round.">>
    <<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>>
    <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
    <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
    <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
  <</if>>
<</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Toss them the purse — it is empty</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Offer the shift — your labour for your body">>
  <<if setup.packListens()>>
    <<set $yieldKind to "shift">>
    <<if $workCursed>>
      <<set $workOwed to true>>
      <<set $yieldRoom to setup.workRoom()>>
    <<else>>
      <<set $yieldRoom to setup.pressGangTo($combatOrigin)>>
    <</if>>
    <<set $combatLog to "">><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
    <<goto "CombatYielded">>
  <<else>>
    <<set _log to "You offer the one thing the deep is supposed to always want — and it goes unheard. What is in front of you does not recruit; it only continues. The words cost you the round.">>
    <<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>>
    <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
    <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
    <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
  <</if>>
<</link>>
<<link "Back">><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
</div>

<<elseif $combatMenu is "cast">>
<div class="special-hint">The Word — drawn from the deep in you. It lands about twice as hard as a blow and finds the flesh through any guard, but it taints you as it spends, and rots what it touches. <<= Math.max(0, $mana)>>/<<= $maxmana>> mana.</div>
<div class="combat-actions special-menu">
<<for _sp range setup.knownSpells()>>
<<capture _sp>>
<<if $mana gte _sp.cost>>
<<set _spName to _sp.name + " (" + _sp.cost + ")">>
<<link _spName>>
  <<set _log to setup.castSpell(_sp.id)>>
  <<if setup.combatOutcome() neq "victory">><<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>><</if>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent"><<= _sp.name>> (<<= _sp.cost>>)</span>
<</if>>
<</capture>>
<</for>>
<<link "Back">><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
</div>

<<else>>
<<if $engulfed>>
/* ENGULFED (R12): the filth decided — your next action goes to getting out. */
<div class="special-hint">You are inside the mass of it. Nothing else happens until you are out.</div>
<div class="combat-actions">
<<link "Wrench yourself free">>
  <<set $engulfed to false>>
  <<set _log to "You wrench and haul against the mass of it and drag yourself back into the air — the round goes to getting out.">>
  <<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<<link "Surrender">><<set $combatLog to "">><<goto "CombatLost">><</link>>
</div>
<<else>>
<div class="combat-actions">
/* Attack — disabled by the "cannot attack" curse (forces Guard/Items/Surrender) */
<<if setup.canAttack()>>
<<link "Attack">>
  <<set _log to setup.playerStrike($target)>>
  <<if setup.combatOutcome() neq "victory">><<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>><</if>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Attack</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Guard">>
  <<set _log to "You set your feet, cover up, take the next blows braced.">>
  <<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(true)>>
  <<set $combatLog to _log>><<set $combatMenu to "main">>
  /* the enemy phase can now END a fight (C2: a whole pack can break) — full outcome check */
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
/* Special — also a strike; the "cannot attack" curse disables it too */
<<if setup.canAttack() and (setup.specialsLeft() gt 0) and (setup.availableSpecials().length gt 0)>>
<<set _spLabel to "Special (" + setup.specialsLeft() + ")">>
<<link _spLabel>><<set $combatMenu to "special">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Special (<<= setup.specialsLeft()>>)</span>
<</if>>
/* Cast — the Word; appears only once learned. Disabled by the "cannot attack" curse, or with no mana to spend. */
<<if $magicKnown>>
<<if setup.canCastAny()>>
<<set _castLabel to "Cast (" + Math.max(0, $mana) + ")">>
<<link _castLabel>><<set $combatMenu to "cast">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Cast (<<= Math.max(0, $mana)>>)</span>
<</if>>
<</if>>
<<link "Items">><<set $combatMenu to "items">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
/* Yield — the parley middle path (review R16). Gated on the voice: the silver muzzle's
   nospeak curse finally bites in combat (its first mechanical consumer). */
<<if setup.canSpeak()>>
<<link "Yield — offer them something">><<set $combatMenu to "yield">><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Yield — your voice will not come</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Surrender">><<set $combatLog to "">><<goto "CombatLost">><</link>>
/* Run — disabled by the "cannot run in combat" curse, or while HELD (a landed grapple/coil/drag) */
<<if setup.canRun() and not $held>>
<<link "Run">>
  <<if setup.fleeRoll()>>
    <<set $combatLog to "">><<set $combatMenu to "main">><<goto $combatOrigin>>
  <<else>>
    <<set _log to "You break for it.">>
    <<set _log to _log + setup.enemyTurn(false)>>
    <<set $combatLog to _log>>
    <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
    <<if _o is "victory">><<goto "CombatVictory">><<elseif _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
  <</if>>
<</link>>
<<elseif $held gt 0>>
<span class="act-spent">Run — held fast</span>
<<else>>
<span class="act-spent">Run</span>
<</if>>
</div>
<</if>>
<</if>>

</div>
<</nobr>>


:: CombatYielded
/* The parley middle path landed (review R16): the offer was heard and taken. Purse =
   loseFight's robbery formula, voluntary — poorer and whole, back to the room. Shift =
   marched to work, body unmauled ($yieldRoom set at offer time; workCursed players were
   reeled to their own post owing a shift, mirroring the encounter's go-quietly branch).
   Reached by literal goto from the yield submenu; no depthOf entry (not a room). */
<<if $yieldKind is "purse">>
They take it the way the deep takes everything — as //owed//. The purse passes from hand
to paw to hand, is weighed somewhere back in the dark, and is found sufficient: the ring
of them opens, incurious now, a transaction concluded. Whatever they were about to do to
you has been done, instead, to the coin.

//(they took <<= $yieldTook>> coin<<if $yieldTook neq 1>>s<</if>>)//

You walk out poorer and whole — and the worst of it is how ordinary it felt. How much
like paying a toll. How much like knowing the rate.

<<link "Walk out — poorer and whole">><<goto $combatOrigin>><</link>>
<<else>>
The fight goes out of the air the moment the word //work// is in it. Labour they
understand; labour is what a body is //for//, down here, and one that offers itself
saves them the mauling it would have cost to take it. You are looked over the way a
foreman looks over a body — not you, just the work you are worth — and found
serviceable, and marched.

<<link "Be marched to the shift">><<goto $yieldRoom>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: CombatVictory
/* C2 morale note: _kills counts what actually FELL — a fled enemy paid nothing into
   $combatSpoils (spoils accrue in playerStrike on a fall), sources no drop, and an
   all-fled "victory" gets its own beat with nothing to strip. */
<<set _kills to ($enemies || []).filter(function (e) { return !e.fled; }).length>>
<<run setup.tallyBlood()>>   /* R17: the fallen enter the ledger — set-piece and encounter kills alike, this one funnel */
<<set _loot to $combatSpoils.coins + (_kills gt 0 ? random(0, 2) : 0)>>
<<set _got to setup.gainCoins(_loot)>>   /* routed so the coins-turn-to-junk curse can intercept */
<<set _xpGain to $combatSpoils.xp>>
<<set _lvls to setup.gainXP(_xpGain)>>
<<set _nfought to ($enemies ? $enemies.length : 1)>>
<<set $combatLog to "">>
<<set $combatMenu to "main">>
<<set $encounterFight to false>>
<<if _kills is 0>>
The last of them breaks and is gone, and the fight is over the strangest way a fight can
be over down here — nothing dead, nothing to strip, the room simply yours because
everything else in it declined you. The dark where they went stays dark.
<<else>>
<<if _nfought gt 1>>The last of them comes apart into the muck with a sound like a wet cough.<<else>>The <<= ($enemies[0] ? $enemies[0].name : "thing")>> comes apart into the muck with a sound like a wet cough.<</if>>
<<if _loot gt 0 and _got lte 0>>You scrape <<= _loot>> cold coin<<if _loot neq 1>>s<</if>> from what's left of <<if _nfought gt 1>>them<<else>>it<</if>> — but the metal curdles in your fist, going to rubbish before you can pocket it. //(the curse on you eats coin)// //(+<<= _xpGain>> XP)//
<<else>>You scrape <<= _got>> cold coin<<if _got neq 1>>s<</if>> from what's left of <<if _nfought gt 1>>them<<else>>it<</if>>
and wipe your hand on your leg, which does not help. //(+<<= _xpGain>> XP)//<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if _lvls gt 0>>

Something in you settles and hardens — the deep has been teaching you how to last
down here, the way it teaches everything that lasts, and a lesson lands in the
meat of you all at once. The deep does not teach for free: every lesson is one
more way you belong to it. <<if _lvls is 1>>You are a level stronger than the thing
that came down here.<<else>><<= _lvls>> levels at once; the change is almost too
fast to feel as anything but sickness.<</if>> //(Level <<= $level>>.)//
<</if>>
<<set _drop to setup.rollDrop(setup.dropSourceEnemy())>>
<<if _drop>><<run setup.takeDrop(_drop)>>

Something glints in what's left of <<if _nfought gt 1>>them<<else>>it<</if>>. You
work it loose: ''<<= setup.itemDisplayName(_drop)>>''. <<if not setup.isIdentified(_drop)>>You can't tell, yet, what it truly is — only what it looks like. //(Put it on to find out, or have it appraised. Some finds are too good for what carried them.)//<<else>>It's yours.<</if>> //(in your pack — manage gear from the sidebar)//
<</if>>

<<link "Catch your breath">><<goto $combatReturn>><</link>>


:: Equipment
/* Gear management screen (DIRECTION-EQUIPMENT). Equip/swap from the pack; cursed gear is BOUND
   (owner: non-removable). Reached from the StoryCaption "Manage gear" link, which stashes
   $gearReturn. Logic in setup.* (equip/unequip/slotItems/itemDisplayName/itemBrief); passage is
   <<nobr>>-wrapped; loop closures use <<capture>>. No depthOf -> no clock/encounter. */
<<nobr>>
<div class="equip-screen">
<div class="equip-head">Your gear — AC <<= setup.playerAC($scores)>> · Vigor <<= Math.max(0, $hp)>>/<<= $maxhp>></div>
<div class="ss-grid equip-stats">
  <span>STR <<= $scores.str>></span><span>DEX <<= $scores.dex>></span><span>CON <<= $scores.con>></span>
  <span>INT <<= $scores.int>></span><span>WIS <<= $scores.wis>></span><span>CHA <<= $scores.cha>></span>
</div>

<<for _slot range setup.EQUIP_SLOTS>>
<<capture _slot>>
<<set _worn to State.variables[_slot]>>
/* graft slots stay hidden until one is grown there — no empty "Eye/Hand/Hide/Heart" clutter */
<<if not setup.GRAFT_SLOTS.includes(_slot) or _worn>>
<div class="equip-slot">
  <div class="es-name"><<= setup.SLOT_LABEL[_slot]>></div>
  <div class="es-worn">
    <<if _worn>><<= setup.itemDisplayName(_worn)>> <span class="es-brief">(<<= setup.itemBrief(_worn)>>)</span><<if setup.isGraft(_worn)>> <span class="es-bound">· grafted, part of you now</span><<elseif setup.isCursed(_worn)>> <span class="es-bound">· bound to you</span><<else>> · <<link "remove">><<run setup.unequip(_slot)>><<goto "Equipment">><</link>><</if>>
    <<else>><span class="es-empty">— empty —</span><</if>>
  </div>
  <<if setup.slotLocked(_slot)>>
  <<if _worn and setup.isGraft(_worn)>><div class="es-opts es-locked">Grown into you. It does not come off.</div><<else>><div class="es-opts es-locked">A cursed thing holds this slot. It will not come off.</div><</if>>
  <<else>>
  <<set _opts to setup.slotItems(_slot)>>
  <<if _opts.length>>
  <div class="es-opts">
    <<for _id range _opts>>
    <<capture _id>>
    <<set _wlbl to "wear " + setup.itemDisplayName(_id)>>
    <span class="es-opt"><<link _wlbl>><<run setup.equip(_id)>><<goto "Equipment">><</link>> <span class="es-brief">(<<= setup.itemBrief(_id)>>)</span></span>
    <</capture>>
    <</for>>
  </div>
  <</if>>
  <</if>>
</div>
<</if>>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

<<set _junk to ($inventory ? $inventory.filter(function (i) { return setup.items[i] and setup.items[i].kind === "junk"; }) : [])>>
<<if _junk.length>><div class="equip-junk">Rubbish (cursed coin): <<= _junk.map(function (i) { return setup.items[i].name; }).join(", ")>></div><</if>>
<div class="equip-hint">Cursed gear cannot be taken off, and follows you into the next life. Some say there's one down here who can cut a curse loose, for a price.</div>

<<set _back to ($gearReturn ? $gearReturn : "Hellmouth")>>
<<link "Back">><<goto _back>><</link>>
</div>
<</nobr>>


:: Map
/* In-game fog-of-war map. Drawing logic is setup.mapView (in the raw-JS script-block):
   it reads the GENERATED setup.mapGraph (baked positions + adjacency) and filters by
   the cross-life setup.discoveredSet(). Reached from the StoryCaption "Map" link,
   which stashes $mapReturn (= where you opened it, also the "you are here" marker).
   No depthOf entry beyond 0 -> no belonging-clock tick, no encounter roll, and
   discover() skips it. <<done>> defers the DOM build until the passage is attached,
   so getElementById finds the container. */
<div class="map-screen-head">The map you carry between lives. <span class="map-sub">Charted rooms stay charted past death; the rest is fog.</span></div>
<div class="map-screen"><div id="sd-map"></div></div>
<<done>>
  <<run setup.mapView(document.getElementById("sd-map"))>>
<</done>>
<<set _back to ($mapReturn ? $mapReturn : "Hellmouth")>>
<div class="map-back"><<link "Back">><<goto _back>><</link>></div>


/* The layer rooms live in their own files now (one per layer):
   L1 Storm Drains  → src/layer1-storm-drains.twee  (Outfall/Maintenance/ExitShaft + the escape)
   L2 Trunk Mains   → src/layer2-trunk-mains.twee   (Confluence hub, GritChamber, Gut/Tallow)
   L3 Old Drains    → src/layer3-old-drains.twee
   L4 Drowned Gall. → src/layer4-drowned-galleries.twee
   Core holds only systems, the intro, the hellmouth + hell town, combat, and endings. */


/* ===================== ENDINGS ===================== */

:: EndingTrueEscape [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("survivor")>>
You climb, and the rope holds, and the rungs above the gap hold, and the reek
thins with every pull until the air is just rain and cold iron and the sour
breath of the street. You come up through the storm grating into a grey
afternoon, soaked and filthy and shaking, and a passing stranger gives you a wide
and wordless berth.

You are filthy to the elbows and you stink and you will be scrubbing the deep out
of the creases of yourself for a week. But it is only filth. It washes off.
Underneath it you are still entirely, stubbornly yourself.

The hellmouth is far below and it does not follow, because it can't — it belongs
to the dirt, and you, it turns out, do not.

//You got out. As yourself.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: EndingPyrrhic [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("marked_escape")>>
You climb, and you come up into the rain, and you are out — but you are not
alone. Something rode up the shaft behind your eyes, light as a held breath, and
it settles in now like a tenant who has signed a lease you don't remember
offering.

The rain doesn't feel cold. You note this with a detachment that isn't yours. A
stranger passes and you catch yourself reading them the way the things below read
*you* — as a door, as a meal, as furniture that could be moved.

<<if $gaveUpFace>>The face you wear into the daylight is not the one you went down with.<</if>>

//You escaped. But not alone, and not unchanged.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: EndingBecome [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("damned")>>
<<set _became to setup.becameClass()>>
<<if _became>><<run setup.addMark("kin_" + _became)>><</if>>
It doesn't happen all at once. That's the lie the surface tells about damnation —
that there's a moment, a line, a choice you could point to. There wasn't. There
was only the filth working in a little deeper each time you let it, until the day
your hands came out of the black water and you couldn't tell them from the water,
and felt no urge to.

You stop looking for the light. You can't quite remember why you wanted it — it
was thin and cold and it showed you things you'd rather not have seen, yourself
chief among them. Down here nothing is shown. Down here you are finally,
gloriously unwatched, because you have become one of the watchers.

The reek is not a reek anymore. It is the smell of home. You turn back toward the
deep galleries, and the dark says your name like a welcome, and the name fits you
now better than it ever did up there.

<<if _became eq "rat">>You went down rat, every inch of you, and the belly will
read the new shape of you on sight: the rat-kind already half-know your face. //That
recognition outlives this life — it does not wash off.//
<<elseif _became eq "pig">>You went down pig, hoof and snout and weight, and the
sulphur court keeps its own: the pig-demons will smell kinship on you now, in this
life and the next. //That recognition outlives this life — it does not wash off.//
<<elseif _became eq "filth">>You went down filth, wholly aggregate, one more will in
the collective evil — and the swirling things below will never again mistake you for
prey. //That kinship outlives this life — it does not wash off.//
<</if>>

//You became one of them.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: EndingResident [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("kept")>>
There was a stair. You're nearly sure there was a stair. But you stayed too long
in the lamplit deep, and the place has finished its slow work of deciding you
belong to it, and a thing that belongs somewhere cannot also leave — that isn't
cruelty, it's just how down here is shaped.

The lamps don't trouble you now. The cold water is the right temperature. When
the others move through the drowned galleries — and there are others, there were
always others, you simply hadn't been here long enough to see them — they nod to
you the way you nod to a neighbour, with the easy blankness of people who have
forgotten there was ever anywhere else.

Somewhere far above, a grate covers a hole that a person once climbed down. No
one comes looking for the ones who don't come back up. You're what's down there
now.

//You stayed too long. The deep keeps what it's allowed to keep.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: EndingTrapped [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("lost")>>
The honest way out was a lie the architecture told — rungs sheared off above the
break, daylight a coin you can't reach. You never found another, and you never
found the means to bridge the one you had. You turn around, and the tunnels
behind you have quietly rearranged themselves while you were busy hoping, the way
a crowd closes the gap where someone used to stand.

You are still yourself. That's the cruelty of it: you kept your hands as clean as
a person can keep them down here — and it bought you nothing but a clearer view
of the trap.

//You never found the way out.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: CombatLost
/* Losing/surrendering a fight no longer kills you (owner): instead setup.loseFight ROBS you
   of some coins (if any) and works UP TO 5 corruption into ONE OR MORE limbs (the class of
   what beat you), then brings you to half vigor. If that tips you over a full transformation,
   the check below sends you to EndingBecome. Reached by both Run-loss and Surrender. Returns
   to $combatOrigin (or, if work-cursed, to your workstation owing a shift). */
<<set _r to setup.loseFight()>>
<<if $corruption gte 100 or setup.fullyTransformed()>><<goto "EndingBecome">><</if>>
The <<= _r.name>> beats you down — the wet floor comes up, the world goes red and then far
away, and you are certain, this time, that this is the death of you.

It is not. The deep does not waste what falls, and it has long since learned that killing is
the crudest possible use of a body — there is so much more to be done with one that merely
//loses//. You come to on the floor, mauled and whole, half your vigor crawled back and the
rest of you quietly rearranged, because the thing that put you down left more in you than
teeth-marks.
<<if _r.clsSet.length gt 1>>
<<set _mlbl to _r.clsSet.map(function (c) { return setup.CLASS_LABEL[c]; }).join(" and ")>>
Not one nature but several were worked into you at once — <<= _mlbl>> together in the torn
places — and they do not quarrel over the territory. They //pool//, the way everything down
here pools: small separate ruins agreeing into one shared appetite, more than the sum of what
was fed in. The thing they are agreeing about is you.
<<else>>
<<switch _r.cls>>
<<case "rat">>Something quick and verminous has threaded into the torn places — a scurrying
readiness, a hunger that knows the walls — and it is in you now, rat in the wounds, making
itself at home.
<<case "pig">>Something heavy and porcine has settled into the torn places, vast and patient
and domestic, the whole weight of the sty, and it is in you now, pig in the wounds, glad of
the room.
<<case "filth">>The aggregate filth of it has seeped into the torn places and set — the swirl
of a hundred ruined things finding one more — and it is in you now, the deep in the wounds, at
home.
<</switch>>
<</if>>
<<if _r.forceFedCheese>>
And they fed you. Down among the burst rounds of the pallet they pinned you and worked a fistful of
the reeking soft past your teeth, and you swallowed because the alternative was to drown in it — and
the worst of it, the part you carry up out of this, is that some corner of you that was not there
this morning //wanted// the second mouthful. You did not choose the cheese. It has chosen you, and it
knows the way to you now.
<</if>>
<<if _r.coinsLost gt 0>>
And your purse is lighter for it. They went through your pockets while you were under — the way
the deep goes through everything that falls — and lifted <<= _r.coinsLost>> coin<<if _r.coinsLost neq 1>>s<</if>> off you for the trouble of putting you down.
<</if>>
<<set $encounterFight to false>>

<<if $workCursed>>
<<set $workOwed to true>>

And then, under the mauling, the older thing stirs: the binding. It does not care that you are
hurt — it cares only that you are //down//, which is the one condition it was made for. You feel
it take up the slack and begin, without hurry, to reel you in: not up and away, the way a free
thing crawls off to lick its wounds, but down and back, along the line that runs from your post
to wherever in hell you happen to fall — toward <<= setup.workLabel()>>, and the shift that is,
once again, owed. You do not get to drag yourself away from this one. You get to clock back in.

<<set _wr to setup.workRoom()>>
<<link "Let the binding reel you back to your post">><<goto _wr>><</link>>
<<elseif setup.CAPTURE_SCENE[$combatOrigin]>>
/* BESPOKE CAPTURE (owner 2026-07-03): some dens KEEP their catches instead of clocking them into a
   shift. The registry entry supplies the beat + where being taken leaves you. Gated below the
   work-curse: a signed body is still reeled to its post first. */
<<set _cap to setup.CAPTURE_SCENE[$combatOrigin]>>
<<= _cap.prose>>

<<link _cap.label>><<goto _cap.dest>><</link>>
<<else>>
And the deep does what it does with anything idle that falls: it does not let you crawl off to
lick your wounds. You may not be //signed// to anything yet — but you are down, and down is idle,
and idle is the one thing hell will not abide. Hands take you under the arms and haul you off, not
up and out but along, toward the nearest work that needs a body. There is always work.

<<set _wr to setup.pressGangTo($combatOrigin)>>
<<link "Be marched off to the shift">><<goto _wr>><</link>>
<</if>>


/* ===================== RANDOM ENCOUNTERS ===================== */

:: RandomEncounter
/* Reached from PassageHeader's ~ENCOUNTER_RATE% roll (owner 2026-06-05). Picks a type from
   setup.ENCOUNTERS; entry #1 is the press-gang. Comply = a one-off shift at a random work
   location (corruption, NO curse) → continue. Resist = fight the local denizens; win →
   continue (combatReturn), lose → CombatLost (+50% they work you anyway). $encounterReturn is
   the room you were entering; combatOrigin is overridden to it so a loss doesn't loop here. No
   depthOf entry, so it can't re-trigger itself. */
<<set _enc to setup.pickEncounter()>>
<<if _enc is "backtowork">>
<<set _den to setup.denizenPack()>>
<<set _dname to setup.enemies[_den[0]].name>>
<<set _rg to setup.regardOf($encounterReturn)>>
<<set _bld to setup.bloodOf(setup.classOnFloor($encounterReturn))>>
<<set _reck to _bld gte setup.BLOOD_FEARED>>
<<if _reck>>
/* THE RECKONING (R17): past BLOOD_FEARED the floor's own kind no longer come recruiting. They have
   smelled too much of THEIR OWN on your hands — a known killer of their kind is not pressed into a
   shift, he is handled. Go-quietly is withdrawn below; only the binding still collects. */
The way is blocked, and this time it is not about labour. The local denizens — a <<= _dname>> at
the front of them — close in slower than a press closes, and lower, the way things move when they
have already decided. They have smelled it on you: not the floor's filth, which is theirs and
forgivable, but the blood under it. //Their kind's// blood, dried into the creases of you, more of
it than any accident could explain. Nobody grunts back-to-work. Whatever they have come to collect,
it is not a shift.
<<elseif _rg and _rg.relation is "matched" and _rg.tier gte 2 and _bld lt setup.BLOOD_FELT>>
/* KIN-CLAIM: the floor's own denizens read their class in you. The press goes soft — and a free
   way opens that a stranger never gets. The boon IS the horror (you pass because you belong now). */
The local denizens close in around you, a <<= _dname>> at the front of them — and then the menace
goes out of it. They have read the <<= setup.CLASS_LABEL[_rg.body]>> in you, and what they read is
//their own//. The press softens into something worse than a press: a welcome. You are not a stranger
to be put to work, only one of the family come late to it — and a gap opens in the ring of them that
a stranger would never be given.

<<link "Slip through as one of them — it costs you nothing, which is the cost">>
  <<goto $encounterReturn>>
<</link>>
<<elseif _rg and _rg.relation is "matched" and _rg.tier gte 2>>
/* THE WITHERED WELCOME (R17): kin-claim would fire — but at BLOOD_FELT they read their own in you
   AND their own's blood ON you, and the second read wins. The free pass closes; the press stands. */
The local denizens close in around you, a <<= _dname>> at the front of them — and for a moment the
menace goes out of it. They have read the <<= setup.CLASS_LABEL[_rg.body]>> in you, and what they
read is //their own//, and something like a gap begins to open in the ring of them. Then the wind
turns, or you move, and they get the rest of you: the blood. Their kind's, on your hands, under
whatever the floor has since layered over it. The gap closes. The welcome dies before it finishes
forming, and what is left is the press, colder now than a stranger would get it.
<<elseif _rg and _rg.relation is "mismatched" and _rg.tier gte 2>>
/* RIVAL: a body of the wrong class for this floor is read as an intruder, handled, not recruited. */
The way is blocked. The local denizens — a <<= _dname>> at the front — close in, and there is no
//back to work// in it, not really. They have read the wrong thing in you, the thing that does not
belong on this floor, and what they want is less a shift than a //handling//: idle or not, you are a
problem, and down here a problem is solved with labour until it stops being one.
<<else>>
The way is blocked. The local denizens — the kind that work this floor, that fetch and haul and
gnaw and never, ever leave — close in around you, a <<= _dname>> at the front of them, and make
it plain with grunt and gesture what the deep wants of you. Not your death. Your //labour//.
There is always work down here, and you are idle, and idle is the one thing hell will not abide.
Back to work, they tell you. Back to work.
<</if>>

<<if _reck>>
<<if $workCursed>>
<<link "Stand on the binding — you are owed work, not a grave">>
  /* R17: the binding-reel stays reachable at ANY blood — a ledger has no nose, and signed
     property is collected, not killed. Same reel as the ordinary claimed go-quietly. */
  <<set $workOwed to true>>
  <<set _wr to setup.workRoom()>><<goto _wr>>
<</link>>
<</if>>
<<else>>
<<link "Go quietly — it's only a shift">>
  <<if $workCursed>>
    /* CLAIMED: the binding hauls you to YOUR OWN post owing a shift — not a random press-gang
       station — and the station room then works the shift and deposits you on its floor (the
       canonical post-shift page). Mirrors the CombatLost cursed reel; without this guard an
       indentured player got the unclaimed one-off (random station + return to where they were). */
    <<set $workOwed to true>>
    <<set _wr to setup.workRoom()>><<goto _wr>>
  <<else>>
    <<set _wr to setup.pressGangTo($encounterReturn)>><<goto _wr>>
  <</if>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

<<scentof _den>>
<<set _rlbl to _reck ? "Meet them — it was always going to come to this" : "Refuse — put them down instead">>
<<capture _den>>
<<link _rlbl>>
  <<set $encounterFight to true>>
  <<run setup.startFight(_den, $encounterReturn)>>
  <<set $combatOrigin to $encounterReturn>>
  <<goto "Combat">>
<</link>>
<</capture>>

<<elseif _enc is "pigpress">>
/* THE PIG PRESS-GANG (owner 2026-06-17). A sty-hand boar comes recruiting. If the cage is YOUR
   post (workStation "cage") this is the binding finding you — back to your own post, a shift owed.
   Otherwise it's a poaching: marched off to work ONE pig shift at the cage (no curse, no debt). */
A wet sucking tread, and then the smell of it ahead of the sight: a sty-hand, one of the great
mud-caked boars that work the pens, blocking the way with a shovel held crosswise like a turnstile
arm. It looks you over the way a foreman looks over a body — not //you//, just the work you are
worth — and tips the shovel toward the dark behind it. There is a pen that wants mucking. There is
always a pen that wants mucking.
<<if $workStation is "cage">>
And it knows your face. Of course it knows your face — you are //signed//, and the binding has
simply put on boots and come looking, because you are late and the cage does not like to be kept
waiting. Back to your post, the boar grunts. Back to the menagerie row.

<<link "Let the binding walk you back to the cage">>
  <<set $workOwed to true>>
  <<set _wr to setup.workRoom()>><<goto _wr>>
<</link>>
<<elseif setup.bloodOf("pig") gte setup.BLOOD_FEARED>>
/* R17: the poaching offer is withdrawn from a player soaked in pig blood — the boar reads the
   hands, not the ledger, and what the hands say is not "labourer". (The binding branch above is
   untouched: signed is signed.) */
And then it stops. The wet snout works the air between you once, twice — and the foreman goes out
of its eyes, and something older comes up behind them. It has smelled the pens on plenty of bodies.
What it smells on yours is the //other// thing, the thing under the muck: pig blood, and too much of
it, dried in past washing. The shovel comes off its shoulder, slow. It is not going to offer you the
shift. You do not lend the knife a job in the kitchen.
<<else>>
You are not its property — not signed, or signed to some //other// master — but a body is a body,
and the pens are short-handed, and it would very much like to borrow you for the one shift, whatever
it is you think you do instead. Just the once, the grunt says. Just to muck the row. You can go back
to your own troubles after.

<<link "Go muck the pens — just the one shift">>
  <<set _wr to setup.pressGangTo($encounterReturn, "cage")>><<goto _wr>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

<<scentof "pig_pressgang">>
<<set _plbl to ($workStation neq "cage" and setup.bloodOf("pig") gte setup.BLOOD_FEARED) ? "Meet it — the shovel is already turning" : "Refuse — put the sty-hand down">>
<<link _plbl>>
  <<set $encounterFight to true>>
  <<run setup.startFight("pig_pressgang", $encounterReturn)>>
  <<set $combatOrigin to $encounterReturn>>
  <<goto "Combat">>
<</link>>

<<elseif _enc is "vatpress">>
/* THE VAT PRESS-GANG (owner 2026-06-18) — the kappa parallel of pigpress. The kappa tend the
   rendering vats the way they tend a bathhouse tub (same instinct: get the guest into the water).
   Vats-bound → the binding walks you back to your post, a shift owed; else a poaching → ONE filth
   shift at the vats (pressGangTo, no curse). Refuse → fight the kappa. */
A wet slap of webbed feet on hot iron, and a kappa comes out of the steam — but not the bathhouse
kind. This is the vat-tending kind: scalded grey-pink, the dish on its crown brimful not of clean
spring-water but of the grey greasy condensate that drips off the rendering hoods, a long
skimming-paddle held crosswise across the gangway like a turnstile arm. It looks you over the way a
foreman looks over a body — not //you//, just the work you are worth — and tips the paddle toward the
vats steaming behind it. There is a tub that wants skimming. To a kappa there is always a tub that
wants tending, and only the water in it ever changes.
<<if $workStation is "vats">>
And it knows your face. Of course it knows your face — you are //signed//, and the binding has put on
its apron and come skimming for you, because the vats do not idle and neither, signed, do you. Back to
your post, the kappa conveys with a tip of the dripping paddle. Back to the boil-house floor.

<<link "Let the binding walk you back to the vats">>
  <<set $workOwed to true>>
  <<set _wr to setup.workRoom()>><<goto _wr>>
<</link>>
<<elseif setup.bloodOf("filth") gte setup.BLOOD_FEARED>>
/* R17: the kappa parallel of the pigpress withdrawal — it reads the filth-kind blood on you
   (golems scattered, drowned re-drowned, its own kind among them) and does not offer the skim. */
And then it stops. The beak tips; the dish on its crown goes very still, the way still water goes
when something moves under it. It has taken the measure of a thousand bodies for the vats, and it
knows render from renderer — and what is dried into your hands is its //own// side of the ledger:
the aggregate scattered, the drowned put back under, kin of its waters among them. The paddle turns
in its grip, no turnstile now. It is not going to offer you the tub. You do not hand the skimmer to
the thing that empties the bath.
<<else>>
You are not its property — not signed, or signed to some //other// master — but a tub is a tub and a
body is a body, and the vats are short-handed, and it would very much like to borrow you for the one
skim, whatever it is you imagine you do instead. Just the once, the kappa conveys. Just to tend the
tub. You can go back to your own troubles after.

<<link "Go skim the vats — just the one shift">>
  <<set _wr to setup.pressGangTo($encounterReturn, "vats")>><<goto _wr>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

<<scentof "kappa">>
<<set _klbl to ($workStation neq "vats" and setup.bloodOf("filth") gte setup.BLOOD_FEARED) ? "Meet it — the paddle is no turnstile now" : "Refuse — put the kappa down">>
<<link _klbl>>
  <<set $encounterFight to true>>
  <<run setup.startFight("kappa", $encounterReturn)>>
  <<set $combatOrigin to $encounterReturn>>
  <<goto "Combat">>
<</link>>

<<elseif _enc is "goodfind">>
/* POSITIVE: a coin/item/cleanse waiting in a REAL room on this floor (owner 2026-06-17). The
   blurb names that room; taking it grants the reward where you stand (you slip off and back). */
<<set _find to setup.pickFind()>>
<<if _find>>
<<= _find.blurb>>

<<linkreplace "Slip off and fetch it">><<nobr>>
<<set _r to setup.takeFind(_find)>>
<<= _find.take>>
<<if _r.coins>> //(+<<= _r.coins>> coins)//<</if>><<if _r.item>> //(you pocket the <<= _r.itemName>>)//<</if>><<if _r.soothe>> //(a little of the filth lifts — you breathe cleaner)//<</if>><<if _r.cost>> //(it costs you a little: +<<= _r.cost>> corruption)//<</if>>
<</nobr>><</linkreplace>>

<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "kinhelp">>
/* POSITIVE: a creature of a class you've WHOLLY turned (a kin_<class> mark) treats you as its
   own (owner 2026-06-17). Rare; only fires when kinReady() — you carry the mark of this band's class. */
<<set _kc to setup.classOnFloor()>>
<<set _kf to setup.KIN_FLAVOR[_kc]>>
<<if setup.bloodOf(_kc) gte setup.BLOOD_FELT>>
/* R17: the kindness CURDLES — kin read the kin in you, then their own kind's blood ON you, and
   the second read wins. The beat fires (the withdrawal is shown, not silently zeroed) but no
   coin, no healing: you have already spent this kindness, in blood. */
<<= _kf.who>> on this floor stops where it is. It looks at you — at the <<= _kc>> the deep has made
of part of you, the shape it knows for its own — and starts toward you the way kin start toward kin.
Then it stops a second time, harder. The nose knows before the rest of it does: under the floor's
filth, the blood. Its kind's blood, worked into your hands past any washing you've done. Whatever it
was bringing you, it keeps. It goes backward without turning around, the way anything backs away from
a thing it has just recognized, and the dark takes it, and the kindness that was coming to you goes
to somebody with cleaner hands.

<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
<<= _kf.who>> on this floor stops where it is. It looks at you — at the <<= _kc>> you let the deep
make of you, the part of you that is now the same stuff as the part of it — and the hunger you'd
braced for never comes. Instead it <<= _kf.deed>>. One of its own does not go hungry while it has
anything to give. That is the whole of the law down here, and for once it falls on your side of you.

<<linkreplace "Take the kindness">><<nobr>>
<<set _r to setup.takeKinHelp()>>
You take it, because down here you take what's offered by the things that share your shape.
//(+<<= _r.coin>> coins, and <<= _r.heal>> vigor back)//
<</nobr>><</linkreplace>>

<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "ratcraving">>
/* THE CRAVING (owner 2026-06-18). Once you've tasted the cheese it follows you through the sewer.
   Below mostly-rat you can still refuse; at ratLimbs>=3 the body eats before you decide — no resist,
   the rat in you reaching first. Scavenged, not a real pallet: the rat always finds something down
   here. Heals a little (bait), rats you a little (cost). Weight climbs with how far gone you are. */
<<if setup.cheeseCompelled()>>
You do not decide to eat. That is the thing nobody warns you about — that it stops arriving as a
choice. The smell finds you first, cheese or rot or the place where the two stop being different,
and then your hands are already at your mouth, and you are crouched over something soft and reeking
you have no memory of going to find, eating, the way you breathe — the rat in you having simply
taken the wheel for the duration of a meal it did not think to ask your permission for.
<<set _r to setup.eatCheese()>>
<<nobr>>
//(the body feeds itself: +<<= _r.heal>> vigor, and the rat works <<= _r.bite>> deeper into you<<if _r.mana gt 0>>; the Word wells up +<<= _r.mana>> mana<</if>>)//
<</nobr>>

<<link "Come back to yourself, and go on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
It finds you here too. The craving — a smell that may be real and may be only the memory of the
pallet so strong your mouth floods and your stomach turns over like a key in a lock — and somewhere
within reach, because there is always something within reach down here for a thing that has begun to
want what you have begun to want, is something soft and ripe and wrong, and your whole body leans
toward it before you have decided anything at all.

<<linkreplace "Give in — the rat in you knows where the food is">><<nobr>>
<<set _r to setup.eatCheese()>>
You give in, and the giving-in is so much easier than the holding-out that you understand, eating,
exactly how this ends.
//(+<<= _r.heal>> vigor, <<= _r.bite>> rat worked deeper into you<<if _r.mana gt 0>>; +<<= _r.mana>> mana<</if>>)//
<</nobr>><</linkreplace>>

<<link "Clench your jaw and walk on — you are still the one deciding">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "brewwithdrawal">>
/* BREW-WITHDRAWAL (owner 2026-07-20). The dry half of the vice ledger: sewer-brew is the
   dominant addiction and there is no still out here to feed it. Below the compel floor you ache
   and walk on clean; at/above it (setup.brewCompelled) the body takes its due from ITSELF —
   setup.brewPang works a little filth in to fill the absence. Nothing to forage, unlike the
   cheese: out here the brew habit is pure want. This is the arbitration made visible — you only
   reach this branch because you fed brew over the cheese. */
<<if setup.brewCompelled()>>
It comes on between one step and the next — the shakes, a cold crawl up the backs of your hands, your
tongue gone to sand and your whole gut folding around a want with no name but the taste of it. There is
no still down here. There is nothing to drink. And the body, denied, does the only thing it has learned to
do with an absence: it fills the hole with what it has to hand, drawing a little more of the deep up into
the shaking to quiet it, the way a drunk with no bottle will chew the cork.
<<set _r to setup.brewPang()>>
<<nobr>>
//(the shakes take their due: <<= _r.bite>> more of the deep settles into you to fill the want)//
<</nobr>>

<<link "Ride it out, and go on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
The want finds you here too — dry-mouthed, a thin sick thirst that is not for water, the memory of the
tavern's warm measure so sudden and whole that you swallow on nothing and your hands cast about for an
errand. But the still is a floor and a world away, and there is not a drop of the stuff to be had down
here. You stand a moment in the wanting, and then you make your feet move, which is its own small
victory and does not, standing there shaking, feel like one.

<<link "Swallow the want and walk on — you are still the one deciding">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "slopcraving">>
/* SLOP-CRAVING (owner 2026-07-20). The pig-slop habit, foraging. Below mostly-pig you can still refuse;
   at pigLimbs>=3 (slopCompelled) the body goes to the trough on its own, the way the farrow do. There is
   always a spill of it in the pig band. Heals a little (bait), pigs you a little (cost). No boar to pen
   you out here — the CAPTURE is the pens' alone (TheHolding). */
<<if setup.slopCompelled()>>
You do not decide to eat. There is a spill of it here — there is always a spill of it, in the warm places:
a trough gone over, a farrow's leavings, a slick of the grey-pink mash down a wall — and your body is
already at it, down in it, feeding the way you breathe, the pig in you having simply gone to the trough it
always knew was there and not thought to ask you first.
<<set _r to setup.eatSlop()>>
<<nobr>>
//(the body feeds itself: +<<= _r.heal>> vigor, and the pig works <<= _r.bite>> deeper into you)//
<</nobr>>

<<link "Come back to yourself, and go on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
The smell finds you first — warm and thick and sweetish-wrong, the smell of the trough, of //food// to a
part of you that has stopped being particular — and somewhere within reach, because there is always
something within reach in the warm places for a thing that has begun to want what you have begun to want,
is a spill of the grey-pink mash, and your mouth floods and your stomach turns toward it before you have
decided anything at all.

<<linkreplace "Give in — get down to it, the way you're learning to">><<nobr>>
<<set _r to setup.eatSlop()>>
You get down to it, and the getting-down is so much easier than the standing-off that you understand,
feeding, exactly how this ends.
//(+<<= _r.heal>> vigor, <<= _r.bite>> pig worked into you)//
<</nobr>><</linkreplace>>

<<link "Straighten up and walk on — you are still the one deciding">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "smokecraving">>
/* SMOKE-CRAVING (owner 2026-07-20; Phase 0). The glow, foraging — but the glow is the air, so there is
   always a haze to draw. Below smokeCompelled you seek out a wisp and choose; at/above, the lungs draw
   on their own. drawSmoke DIFFUSES (a thin film across several segments), so the meter climbs but no
   single limb turns — you go vaguer, not clawed. Bait = the ache eased, the fear gone quiet (detachment,
   the opium reading — NOT courage). This branch is reached only when smoke is the dominant vice. */
<<if setup.smokeCompelled()>>
You do not decide to breathe it. There is a haze here — there is always a haze, down where things burn
and rot and give up their air — and you have already taken it in, a long slow pull of the glow off the
dark, the way you take in everything now, without asking. The ache goes quiet. The fear goes quiet. //You//
go quiet, and a little more of you goes out with the breath and does not come back, spread thin and
everywhere at once, and it is the easiest thing in the world and you barely feel it leave.
<<set _r to setup.drawSmoke()>>
<<nobr>>
//(the lungs draw on their own: +<<= _r.heal>> vigor, and the glow diffuses <<= _r.total>> of you out thin across <<= _r.n>> parts — no one thing turning, just //less// of you)//
<</nobr>>

<<link "Come back to yourself — what there is of you — and go on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<else>>
It finds you here too — not a hunger in the gut but a want in the //chest//, a shallowness to every breath
that only one thing fills. And there is always a wisp of it somewhere within reach, because there is always
something within reach down here for a thing that has begun to want what you have begun to want: a lick of
the glow off a grate, a curl of it hanging where the warm air pools, and your lungs lean toward it before
you have decided anything at all.

<<linkreplace "Draw it in — the chest wants what the chest wants">><<nobr>>
<<set _r to setup.drawSmoke()>>
You draw it in, and the ache eases, and the fear eases, and the eased feeling is so much simpler than the
wanting that you understand, exhaling, exactly how this ends — with less and less of you each time, and each
time minding it less.
//(+<<= _r.heal>> vigor; <<= _r.total>> of you diffused thin across <<= _r.n>> parts — no limb turns, you just go vaguer)//
<</nobr>><</linkreplace>>

<<link "Hold your breath and walk on — you are still, for now, one thing">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<elseif _enc is "midgossip">>
<<set $heardOfGrimoire to true>>
Two of them are working a quiet corner of the midway between the lit stalls — big carnival pigs in
waistcoats, off the clock, passing a bottle — and they do not lower their voices, because who down
here would understand them, and you are not supposed to yet. But you have been down here long enough
now that some of it lands.

One is complaining about the //new ones//, the marks, how slow they are to take to the Word, how the
management keeps having to leave primers lying about where even a mark will trip over one. The other
laughs, a wet barking thing, and says the best one's the //paper// — //they put it on the bog roll, up
in the old maintenance stalls in the pipes, because that's where a frightened animal sits still long
enough to read//, and a mark will study a thing in a privy it would never pick up anywhere else, and
by the time it understands what it's been reading it's already learned to speak. //"They'll never find
it,"// the first one frets, and the other barks again: //"Can't miss it — they lit the bloody hole
pink so the marks'd look. Management's idea of a joke. The one stall glowing like a fairground."// They
both think this is enormously funny. They drink to whoever thought of it.

They have not noticed you. You have what you came down the midway with and a little more: you know,
now, that the //pink-glowing// stall up in the sewer privy is no accident, and the roll in it is no
roll. //(noted: the stall in TheStallRow that glows pink is a primer — get it when it's free and look
at it with that in mind)//

<<link "Slip away before they clock you, and go on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>

<<elseif _enc is "shortweight">>
/* THE SHORT-WEIGHT MEN (owner 2026-07-03) — the third ledger. dumpStat() picks your weakest number
   and the matching face tests it. WIS is passive — an AMBUSH (review R9): a failed sense = the
   lurker takes a FREE opening turn. The other five sidle up and offer a gamble (beat it on your
   worst stat) or a certain smaller toll; INT's toll is a free walk (the wise decline the con). */
<<set _sw to setup.dumpStat()>>
<<set _stat to _sw.stat>>
<<set _d to setup.SHORTWEIGHT[_stat]>>
<<if _stat is "wis">>
There is a dry corner ahead — a heap of old sacking up out of the wet, the first place in a mile that
looks like you could set your back against something and let your knees go. You are already moving
toward it.
<<if setup.statCheck("wis", setup.SHORTWEIGHT_DC)>>
Something stops you a step short. The heap is //breathing//. Barely — you would never have caught it
if the sense that smells a wrong thing coming were not awake in you — but the sacking lifts and falls,
and in the deepest fold two wet points catch the light and are watching you decide.

<<link "Back away — leave it for the next tired thing">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<<link "Take it first, while it still thinks itself hidden">>
  <<run setup.startFight("shortweight", $encounterReturn)>>
  <<set $combatOrigin to $encounterReturn>>
  <<set $encounterFight to true>>
  <<goto "Combat">>
<</link>>
<<else>>
You set your back against it and let your knees go — and the heap //closes//. It was never sacking. It
had folded itself into the one shape a tired thing cannot walk past, and it had you the moment you
chose to rest; the sense that should have smelled it coming was looking the other way, the way it
always is when you need it. It gets the first of you for free.

<<link "Get your hands up — it's already on you">>
  <<set $combatLog to setup.ambushFight("shortweight", $encounterReturn)>>
  <<set _o to setup.combatOutcome()>>
  <<if _o is "loss">><<goto "CombatLost">><<else>><<goto "Combat">><</if>>
<</link>>
<</if>>
<<else>>
<<= setup.SHORTWEIGHT_LEAD>>

<<= _d.intro>>

<<link _d.tryLabel>><<set $swStat to _stat>><<set $swOut to setup.shortweightTry(_stat)>><<goto "ShortWeightDone">><</link>>
<<link _d.cedeLabel>><<set $swStat to _stat>><<set $swOut to setup.shortweightCede(_stat)>><<goto "ShortWeightDone">><</link>>
<</if>>

<<else>>
/* unknown encounter type — fail safe: just carry on */
<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: ShortWeightDone
/* SHORT-WEIGHTS resolution beat (owner 2026-07-03) — the five social faces land here (WIS ambushes
   straight into Combat instead). Reads $swOut (from shortweightTry/Cede) + $swStat to pick the
   face's prose + annotate the cost. NO depthOf (an encounter resolution, not a room), and excluded
   from the encounter re-roll (encounterEligible) so it can't chain into another accosting. */
<<set _d to setup.SHORTWEIGHT[$swStat]>>
<<if $swOut.ceded>><<= _d.cede>><<elseif $swOut.passed>><<= _d.pass>><<elseif $swOut.shove and _d.failShove>><<= _d.failShove>><<else>><<= _d.fail>><</if>>
<<if $swOut.took>> //(it takes <<= $swOut.took>> coin<<if $swOut.took neq 1>>s<</if>>)//<<elseif $swOut.shove>> //(a shove you cannot stop — −1 vigor)//<<elseif $swOut.amt>> //(+<<= $swOut.amt>> <<= setup.CLASS_LABEL[$swOut.cls]>> into your <<= setup.SEG_LABEL[$swOut.seg]>>)//<</if>>

<<link "Carry on">><<goto $encounterReturn>><</link>>


:: EndingSovereign [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("sovereign")>>
You do not climb. Climbing is for the living, for the frightened, for the ones
who still half-believe the surface is a reward. You walk to the teeth of the mouth
and the teeth draw back — the way a dog's lip draws back from a hand it has
learned not to bite — and the warm wet wind of the place sighs out around you like
a held breath finally let go.

You go up through the throat, through the sewer, past the broken rungs that
stopped you cold in a hundred frightened lives, and they do not stop you now,
because nothing down here detains its own landlords. The grate lifts at your
touch. The grey afternoon receives you without comment, and the rain, when it
touches you, steams.

You wanted out, once. Now you are, and the wanting has changed its shape entirely
— because you come up into the city not as a person who escaped hell, but as the
small bright leading edge of hell, escaping into the city. It will not understand
what arrived until much later. You have all the time there is.

//You walked out the front, because what walks out is no longer something the dark
bothers to keep. A crown is also a kind of door.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>


:: EndingUnbound [ending]
<<run setup.recordRun("unbound")>>
You hold the whole Sigil up to the teeth of the mouth, three fragments made one, cut from
the navel of the belly and the heart of the rendering and the throne of the deep, and the
mark does what the mark was made to do, which is nothing dramatic at all: it simply
*declines* you. It declines hell's claim on you. Not by force, not by fire, not by becoming
something hell respects, but by asserting, in a language older than the place, the plain
fact that you are not the property of the dark and never legally were.

And the dark, which is many things but is above all a thing that keeps accounts, reads the
mark, and checks its ledger, and finds — to a patience that has no bottom — that the entry
is true. The teeth draw back. Not in deference, the way they draw back for the sovereign;
in *release*, the way a bailiff stands aside from a debt that has been, against all
expectation, paid in full.

You walk out the front of hell. You go up through the throat and the works and the belly
and the drowned places and the old drains and the mains and the storm-drains and out, the
whole long way, and at every threshold the thing that would have kept you reads the mark and
lets you by, and you come up through the storm grating into a grey afternoon filthy to the
elbows and stinking and shaking and entirely, unanswerably, *yours*. Not clean. You will
never be clean. But not kept, and not changed, and not theirs.

//You did not escape hell and you did not become it. You unbound yourself from it, and walked
out the front door a free thing, owing nothing, owned by no one. The hardest way out, and the
only one that costs you nothing you wanted to keep.//

<<link "Again">><<run setup.restartCarry()>><</link>>
